{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here","id":11921,"title":"The Great Marriage of Exalted and [Insert Fandom Here]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-15T23:29:55-08:00","id":11921,"title":"The Great Marriage of Exalted and [Insert Fandom Here]","content":"This was one of my favorites on the Old Forum, so I thought I'd bring it over here. The basic idea is to take some sort of other book/anime/movie/story/video game and translate it into the Exalted universe. To quote the original poster:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">A couple quick ground rules. This isn't meant to be an exact translation from existing universe to Exalted. Posters are allowed to finagle it a bit. Yes, Batman and the Joker are mortals. We get it. But if the poster has an idea for turning Nexus into Gotham, with Batman being a Night caste and the Joker being a Fair Folk, that's his prerogative. If you disagree, do so politely, and make your case, with as much detail as possible. Then leave it. The idea is to have fun and be creative, not precise.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Also, keep the general idea close as possible, but feel free to mess with it a bit as well. If you wanted to make an Exalted Hunger Games of Divinity, the characters don't all need to match specific tributes; just make it so that the contestants are randomly drawn from some pool of potential candidates and forced to fight to the death.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Alrighty... let's see what people come up with!</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I have a pretty good one to start off with on this forum:<br /> <br /> The Realm Civil War is now in full swing, and the fighting has practically engulfed all the Blessed Isle. While the Roseblack has taken the Imperial City and still maintains the capital, she has gone to drastic and disturbing lengths to hunt both her enemies and bring back the Wyld Hunt in full force. To do the latter, she has unknowingly recruited a ruthless Moonshadow Caste detective who seems to flicker between disturbingly polite and complete madman.<br /> <br /> In this horrific war, Lookshy decides they must do something in order to keep the Civil War from spilling over into the East. Therefore they send a team of their best soldiers, a team of Dragon-blooded led by a smooth talking Dawn Caste, to assist House Sesus in defeating the forces of the Roseblack.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in a Blessed Isle city occupied by the Roseblack's forces, the Half-Caste daughter of a Zenith killed by the Roseblack's Wyld Hunt (led by the previously mentioned Moonshadow Caste) runs a theater where she puts on plays thought lost to the Blessed Isle. When a Fire-Aspected war hero falls for the Half-Caste, he convinces his Dynast superiors to use her theater to premiere a play written about his heroic deeds. Seeing a chance for revenge against the Roseblack, the Half-Caste allows this, secretly plotting to turn the play's premiere into the execution of all the Dynasts sided with the Roseblack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T23:38:20-08:00","id":11924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here#post11921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm Civil War is now in full swing, and the fighting has practically engulfed all the Blessed Isle. While the Roseblack has taken the Imperial City and still maintains the capital, she has gone to drastic and disturbing lengths to hunt both her enemies and bring back the Wyld Hunt in full force. To do the latter, she has unknowingly recruited a ruthless Moonshadow Caste detective who seems to flicker between disturbingly polite and complete madman.<br /> <br /> In this horrific war, Lookshy decides they must do something in order to keep the Civil War from spilling over into the East. Therefore they send a team of their best soldiers, a team of Dragon-blooded led by a smooth talking Dawn Caste, to assist House Sesus in defeating the forces of the Roseblack.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in a Blessed Isle city occupied by the Roseblack's forces, the Half-Caste daughter of a Zenith killed by the Roseblack's Wyld Hunt (led by the previously mentioned Moonshadow Caste) runs a theater where she puts on plays thought lost to the Blessed Isle. When a Fire-Aspected war hero falls for the Half-Caste, he convinces his Dynast superiors to use her theater to premiere a play written about his heroic deeds. Seeing a chance for revenge against the Roseblack, the Half-Caste allows this, secretly plotting to turn the play's premiere into the execution of all the Dynasts sided with the Roseblack.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very cool, but I don't recognize it..? What are you paraphrasing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T07:42:14-08:00","id":12065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drecain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=11924#post11924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very cool, but I don't recognize it..? What are you paraphrasing?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the point.<br /> <br /> While the topic on the old forums started off as just reframing things in Exalted terms, by the end of the first page people had started playing, &quot;Guess the story that's been Exaltified.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do agree with you though that dreamking's thing sounds pretty awesome, but I have no idea what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T15:48:38-08:00","id":12344,"title":"","content":"It's Inglorious Basterds, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:50:46-08:00","id":12373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=12344#post12344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Inglorious Basterds, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You got it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T19:40:05-08:00","id":12446,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I've got one.<br /> <br /> The might of Tepet Fukof has been revealed. Seizing control of the Realm, the man once thought puppet now seeks to consolidate his control by drawing out and destroying his enemies. To this end, he curses Iselsi Holy with terrible Wyld mutations, hoping to bait in her father, Josuta Josefu from his refuge in the Threshold. A masterful Immaculate martial artist in his younger days, Josefu was famed for his defeat of Karz, the Ever-Living Behemoth. But unbeknownst to Fukof, Josefu had already been destined for something greater- at the age of nearly sixty, he received his preordained Sidereal Exaltation, becoming one of the Chosen of Battles. Now he has abandoned heaven, seeking the aid of Holy's son, Adamant Star, who has recently Exalted as a Dawn Caste. But all the world is not against them: they will be joined by Emerald Monk and Silver Palanquin, both former servants of Fukof's, now seeking revenge against their former master. Crimson Augur, a wise Fire aspect and powerful sorcerer, and Igi the Fool, a tempestuous and diminutive Full Moon Caste. Together, they will travel to the Blessed Isle to confront Fukof, battling along the way the many strange and twisted Dragon-Blooded, demons, and Infernals he throws against them- and along the way, discover the secret of Fukof's power or die to his mysterious strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T20:31:19-08:00","id":12471,"title":"","content":"...This is Jojo's Bizarre Adventure, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T20:34:45-08:00","id":12473,"title":"","content":"Bullseye. Part 3, specifically. (I figured, Exalted was inspired in part by Fist of the North Star, why not adapt FotNS: Glam Rock Edition?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T04:24:39-08:00","id":12650,"title":"","content":"In the First Age, a ruthless Solar Queen has ruled her secluded island with an iron fist, guarded by her powerful weather-controlling Sorcery and her fanatically devoted Air-Aspected DB Gens. In order to ensure her eternal rule, she wove powerful magics that'd let her consciousness transfer to the next bearer of her Exaltation, always chosen from one of her priesthood.<br /> <br /> Some time after the Usurpation (which she survived thanks to storms guarding her island), her masterplan came undone when her current high priestess, destined to be the next bearer of the Exaltation, saw through Queen's game and committed suicide before the transfer was complete, leaving Queen's consciousness trapped in her decaying body. Maddened sorceress raised up all the spells protecting the island, wreaking havoc and ensuring no one can never leave. Over the years, the DB gens has degenerated through centuries of inbreeding, and the vicious storms have caused numerous vessels to get wrecked upon the island's shores. Recently, a group of refugees formed a murderous scavenger cult, led by a man intent on solving the island's mystery and leaving it.<br /> <br /> Into this, a ship bearing a scavenging expedition gets thrown. Among them, a girl who's the last descendant of Solar's priesthood, and her best friend who's secretly a No Moon Lunar and a student of the dreaded Black Claw Style. The Lunar begins to plow through the island, uncovering it's secrets and decimating the cargo cult in order to save her kidnapped friend, never dropping her &quot;damsel in distress trying to survive&quot; act while at it.<br /> <br /> When I posted it on the old forum, nobody got it. Hint: it's a video game, and I made the main heroine a Lunar due to the game's promotional catchphrase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T15:51:40-08:00","id":13011,"title":"","content":"The last Tomb Raider game. &quot;A Survivor is Born&quot;<br /> <br /> Had to check the wikipedia entry to see if the plot actually matched, since I never actually played the game (man, it's a lot crazier than I thought). But your description of the heroine was enough to guess. Not sure why Black Claw Style, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T16:26:34-08:00","id":13680,"title":"","content":"I love the detail of making Lara a Black Claw stylist, now I manically laugh in a quite evil manner when I think back on the game. She sure did murder a lot of cultists while pretending to be defending herself in that game, didn't she?<br /> <br /> She could easily be a Twilight or Chosen of Secrets as well, though, but props. Way awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T17:13:02-08:00","id":13699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=13011#post13011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last Tomb Raider game. &quot;A Survivor is Born&quot;<br /> <br /> Had to check the wikipedia entry to see if the plot actually matched, since I never actually played the game (man, it's a lot crazier than I thought). But your description of the heroine was enough to guess. Not sure why Black Claw Style, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very obvious if you play the game, especially on lower difficulties.<br /> <br /> The thing about combat in Tomb Raider is, Lara is extremely deadly once you buy a few powerups, but she never drops the &quot;innocent girl desperately trying to defend herself&quot; act. By the end of the game, I had to fumble really hard to not trigger the instakill finishing move on every enemy, and even if I did, it was merely downgraded to &quot;stun the bastard and have another go at finishing him off&quot; move or something like that, but the way the fight was animated, if you saw it without ever playing it and with QTE prompts cleared from the screen, you'd think it's hellishly hard, as Lara fumbles and flails about all the time, seemingly winning in the end only by a combination of luck and sheer balls, not being one of the deadliest beings in existence. Hence, Black Claw Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T19:07:14-08:00","id":13730,"title":"","content":"A thousand years has passed since Creation was crushed by the failed onslaught of the Yozi Reclamation. An Infernal empire, lead by the last surviving decendent of the Scarlet Empress, has arisen on the once-Blessed Isle. Powered by their Helltech machines and Infernal Sorceries, their conquest of the world seems certain. Only the city of Why'wal, by the genius of its elderly Twilight prince, has faced the empire and survived. When a young mercenary general betrays the empire and Exalts as a Dawn caste, the empire attaches to his skull a Sapient black gemstone that will kill him if they choose and send him as an infiltrator to deliver Why'wal to them. <br /> <br /> The elderly Twilight sees through the rouse and uses his sorcery to quiet the relic long enough for the Dawn to find a way to permanently draw it under his control. With the assistance of his newly-found midget Lunar mate and the advice of a cryptic Chosen of Battles, the young Solar travels to the corners of Creation, collecting a trio of potent artifacts; an amulet which steals vitality from those slain nearby the wearer, the Aidenweiss and an staff with the power to negate Sorcery. With these weapons and and army of Lumina summoned by the Aidenweiss, the Dawn successfully leads Creation in a decisive battle that destroys the Infernal empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T22:17:05-08:00","id":13795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=13730#post13730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thousand years has passed since Creation was crushed by the failed onslaught of the Yozi Reclamation. An Infernal empire, lead by the last surviving decendent of the Scarlet Empress, has arisen on the once-Blessed Isle. Powered by their Helltech machines and Infernal Sorceries, their conquest of the world seems certain. Only the city of Why'wal, by the genius of its elderly Twilight prince, has faced the empire and survived. When a young mercenary general betrays the empire and Exalts as a Dawn caste, the empire attaches to his skull a Sapient black gemstone that will kill him if they choose and send him as an infiltrator to deliver Why'wal to them.<br /> <br /> The elderly Twilight sees through the rouse and uses his sorcery to quiet the relic long enough for the Dawn to find a way to permanently draw it under his control. With the assistance of his newly-found midget Lunar mate and the advice of a cryptic Chosen of Battles, the young Solar travels to the corners of Creation, collecting a trio of potent artifacts; an amulet which steals vitality from those slain nearby the wearer, the Aidenweiss and an staff with the power to negate Sorcery. With these weapons and and army of Lumina summoned by the Aidenweiss, the Dawn successfully leads Creation in a decisive battle that destroys the Infernal empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... the original Hawkmoon series by Michael Moorcock, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T07:02:48-08:00","id":14004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=13795#post13795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's... the original Hawkmoon series by Michael Moorcock, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes it is!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:27:04-08:00","id":14150,"title":"","content":"Deceitful Surgeon, a void-tainted mortal in Autochthonia, uses unnatural mental influence to control eight young Alchemicals, which he uses to attack the city and wins control through a murder of Emily and trial that discredits the her lover, the noble Luminiferious Physician, Deceitful Surgeon's one-time colleague. Luminiferious Physician builds the ultimate fighting machine, Null, to take back the city but he is overwhelmed by the opposition, unaided by the cowed populace. <br /> <br /> The Blue Bomber is a Blue Jade Alchemical created by Luminiferious Physician in his exile. Despite Luminiferious Physician's pleas not to take up his older late brother's hopeless one man crusade against Deceitful Surgeon's occupation of the city, The Blue Bomber strikes out on his own to win the city back for the people. Unexpectedly he meets his dead predecessor, Null, in battle, and when no one, even Luminiferious Physician, helps his battle he turns his back on humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T11:03:13-08:00","id":14179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=14150#post14150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deceitful Surgeon, a void-tainted mortal in Autochthonia, uses unnatural mental influence to control eight young Alchemicals, which he uses to attack the city and wins control through a murder of Emily and trial that discredits the her lover, the noble Luminiferious Physician, Deceitful Surgeon's one-time colleague. Luminiferious Physician builds the ultimate fighting machine, Null, to take back the city but he is overwhelmed by the opposition, unaided by the cowed populace.<br /> <br /> The Blue Bomber is a Blue Jade Alchemical created by Luminiferious Physician in his exile. Despite Luminiferious Physician's pleas not to take up his older late brother's hopeless one man crusade against Deceitful Surgeon's occupation of the city, The Blue Bomber strikes out on his own to win the city back for the people. Unexpectedly he meets his dead predecessor, Null, in battle, and when no one, even Luminiferious Physician, helps his battle he turns his back on humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know very little about Alchemicals or Autocthonia. However, I know the first two Protomen albums when I see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T11:16:59-08:00","id":14192,"title":"","content":"We have a winner!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T01:12:00-08:00","id":16516,"title":"","content":"I got a super easy one.<br /> <br /> During the Usurpation, a band of Sidereals and Dragon Blooded sailors caught a legendary Eclipse caste upon nothing more than a ragtag ship. At his public execution, he told the crowd that his vast fortune, First Age artifacts and countless secrets would belong to whoever found them first.<br /> <br /> Cut to the second age, and people are still sailing across the West trying to find the legendary belongings of this First Age Eclipse. Among them is a go-lucky but determined Solar (believed by some to be the reincarnation of the First Age Eclipse from legend) who suffers from a strange Wyld mutation and his crew of Exalted pirates. Traveling with this Wyld-mutated Solar include (to name a few) a Dawn Caste feared across the West for his swordsmanship, a Twilight Caste trickster and marksman, a Night Caste navigator and thief who is obsessed with treasure, a No Moon Lunar with exceptional Medicine skills and a polite (if sometimes goofy) Midnight Caste violinist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T01:59:54-08:00","id":16524,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">You forgot an Alchemical magitech engineer/shipwright and... actually I have no idea about Robin. Chimera? Exigent of the god of Limbs?</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T13:41:27-08:00","id":16766,"title":"","content":"Five mortal children growing up in various parts of Lookshy get caught outside during a raid by implacable Infernals. The dying Lunar man charges them with guarding creation from these beings and uses a long-lost artifact called Luna's Benevolence to grant them a limited version of the gift of the Lunars: Changing into any animal whose blood they taste. Should they remain in those forms longer than two hours, however, they would remain those animals until they died. Now, they must battle an akuma and find their own heroism without exposing who they are, lest they be silenced on their knowledge, their families killed or enslaved in Malfeas itself with them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T17:27:51-08:00","id":16881,"title":"","content":"Animorphs. I'm surprised you used Infernals instead of Abyssals, though- they have a better chance of actually conquering Lookshy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T08:32:45-08:00","id":17130,"title":"","content":"Since the First Age, the Ebon Dragon has had a strange fascination with a single soul's journey's through the Loom of Fate. While this soul has shown to be a paragon of the 'virtues' (or lack thereof) of the Ebon Dragon, the Yozi has never blessed the man with an Infernal Exaltation, most likely due to his incompetence in every sinister scheme he comes up with. Thus far, the Ebon Dragon has watched this soul in five lives: His first as the Half-Caste son of a mad, war-mongering Dawn Caste king in the First Age, the second as a Dynast and close adviser (and possibly lover) to the Scarlet Empress, the third as the personal servant of Regent Fokuf and most recently as a commanding officer for House Tepet in the Realm Civil War. Perhaps the Ebon Dragon merely enjoys to watch a mortal he finds so much like himself, or perhaps the Yozi has much larger plans for this particular soul. Perhaps Creation will never know...perhaps it will find out all too soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T09:31:47-08:00","id":17151,"title":"","content":"...All I can think of is Flashman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T09:48:40-08:00","id":17155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=17130#post17130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the First Age, the Ebon Dragon has had a strange fascination with a single soul's journey's through the Loom of Fate. While this soul has shown to be a paragon of the 'virtues' (or lack thereof) of the Ebon Dragon, the Yozi has never blessed the man with an Infernal Exaltation, most likely due to his incompetence in every sinister scheme he comes up with. Thus far, the Ebon Dragon has watched this soul in five lives: His first as the Half-Caste son of a mad, war-mongering Dawn Caste king in the First Age, the second as a Dynast and close adviser (and possibly lover) to the Scarlet Empress, the third as the personal servant of Regent Fokuf and most recently as a commanding officer for House Tepet in the Realm Civil War. Perhaps the Ebon Dragon merely enjoys to watch a mortal he finds so much like himself, or perhaps the Yozi has much larger plans for this particular soul. Perhaps Creation will never know...perhaps it will find out all too soon...</div> </div> </div> </div>Blackadder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T10:44:57-08:00","id":17184,"title":"","content":"You got it, Saur Ops!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T02:52:15-08:00","id":19633,"title":"","content":"Oh wow, I actually have one, now. Ahem:<br /> <br /> Great Forks is well known as a joyous city of temples and leisure. Among the many known revels in the city are the bands of energetic young performers whose dancing skills win them great fame and adoration. However, these bands are also aggressive, and sometimes bitter rivals with each other, competing for fame and the right to the very stages they dance upon. Things have changed lately, however, with the rise of several new Exigents to the leadership of many of these gangs. Simple dance contests and other games of skill between them are now giving way to much more physical and violent contests. These battles are rather intense, but to date, not fatal. Yet. And in the shadows, a group of unknown gods with ties to the Black Market of Exaltations continues to spread these powers around, waiting and seeing what will come next.<br /> <br /> Most strangely of all though, nearly all of the Exigents involved appear to be Chosen of the god of a specific type of fruit...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T20:47:22-08:00","id":20486,"title":"","content":"As the original poster of the original thread, the fact that this was resurrected makes me very happy indeed. Thank you, dreamking89, for bringing it back to life, and thank you to everyone who has posted so far!<br /> <br /> Mmm... I should make a contribution... let's see...<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Several years before, the Realm attempted to go to war with a culture of new Exalts and their Godblooded progeny living in a distant corner of Creation, hidden in the Northeastern Bordermarches, due to a misunderstanding in cultural mores. Despite the power of the distant land, which almost annihilated the Blessed Isle (due to their ability to evade targeting by the Defense Grid), the distant culture discovered something about the Realm that made them halt their attack and sue for peace.<br /> <br /> Now, a new Embassy has been created in the Bordermarches of Western Ocean, where the representatives of the Realm and the new culture are joined by reluctant agents the Guild, representatives from the Jade Folk (who have been able to get partially free of the Great Geas, and who have antagonized the Guild), and a strange representative of a culture from Deep within the Wyld. The head Realm ambassador is a Water-aspected naval commander who inexplicably survived the final battle of the earlier war; joining him are a mysterious representative of the strange culture (who secretly is a Zenith Caste priestess), a disaffected Guild factor with higher desires, and a vengeance-minded Jadefolk with a dozen schemes in mind (including trying to somehow acquire Exaltations for the Jadefolk). In addition, a man representing unusual clients also resides, offering powerful favors in oblique tones; a Sidereal agent keeps an eye on behalf of the Realm, searching for humans with non-Terrestrial Exaltations; and there are strange stirrings in the ruins of ancient cults, as Infernals and their demon servitors begin gathering hidden weapons out of the Wyld...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T08:05:12-08:00","id":20641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=20486#post20486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the original poster of the original thread, the fact that this was resurrected makes me very happy indeed. Thank you, dreamking89, for bringing it back to life, and thank you to everyone who has posted so far!<br /> <br /> Mmm... I should make a contribution... let's see...<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Several years before, the Realm attempted to go to war with a culture of new Exalts and their Godblooded progeny living in a distant corner of Creation, hidden in the Northeastern Bordermarches, due to a misunderstanding in cultural mores. Despite the power of the distant land, which almost annihilated the Blessed Isle (due to their ability to evade targeting by the Defense Grid), the distant culture discovered something about the Realm that made them halt their attack and sue for peace.<br /> <br /> Now, a new Embassy has been created in the Bordermarches of Western Ocean, where the representatives of the Realm and the new culture are joined by reluctant agents the Guild, representatives from the Jade Folk (who have been able to get partially free of the Great Geas, and who have antagonized the Guild), and a strange representative of a culture from Deep within the Wyld. The head Realm ambassador is a Water-aspected naval commander who inexplicably survived the final battle of the earlier war; joining him are a mysterious representative of the strange culture (who secretly is a Zenith Caste priestess), a disaffected Guild factor with higher desires, and a vengeance-minded Jadefolk with a dozen schemes in mind (including trying to somehow acquire Exaltations for the Jadefolk). In addition, a man representing unusual clients also resides, offering powerful favors in oblique tones; a Sidereal agent keeps an eye on behalf of the Realm, searching for humans with non-Terrestrial Exaltations; and there are strange stirrings in the ruins of ancient cults, as Infernals and their demon servitors begin gathering hidden weapons out of the Wyld...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No problem! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for your contribution....is it Ender's Game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T08:52:12-08:00","id":20652,"title":"","content":"EndlessKng's is near-certainly Babylon 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T09:18:32-08:00","id":20662,"title":"","content":"+1 to Saur Ops. This pretty much has to be B5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T05:27:07-08:00","id":21123,"title":"","content":"It is indeed B5! Which I realized after I started writing was a bigger bear to figure out than I had anticipated...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:24:24-08:00","id":21785,"title":"","content":"Two Sidereals (one older and experienced, the other recently Exalted) working as ambassadors in the Realm Civil War find themselves temporarily stranded in the South. While there, they befriend a young slave boy who they discover will one day Exalt as a Dawn Caste. Believing the boy to be important in saving Creation from evil, the Sidereals take him back to the Blessed Isle to train with the Gold Faction both in the Realm and in Yu-Shan. As the boy grows older and Exalts, the Realm Civil War only grows worse thanks to the interference of an extremely well hidden Deathlord (The Pale Emperor Cloaked in Darkness and Lightning) and his numerous Abyssal servants. When the elder of the two Sidereals is killed by an Abyssal, the younger takes on the boy's training, quickly becoming his mentor and best friend.<br /> <br /> While the young Dawn caste proves to be extremely skilled, he also is hot-headed and has little patience for the subtleties of the Gold Faction he now works closely with. After seeing in the Loom of Fate that his God Blooded lover will die, the Dawn Caste becomes desperate to save her life. When the Pale Emperor offers him power enough to save his lover, the Dawn caste swears loyalty to the Deathlord. He quickly betrays his former friends and mentors, opening the gates of Yu-Shan to the Pale Emperor's armies. This betrayal culminates in the destruction of Gem, where the Dawn Caste mortally wounds his pregnant lover and fights his former Sidereal mentor among the lava flows of the catastrophe. The Dawn is horrifically scarred in the fight and left helpless, but the Sidereal cannot bring himself to kill his former friend. While the Sidereal escapes Gem with the dying God-Blooded, the Pale Emperor Cloaked in Darkness and Lightning finds the helpless Dawn Caste, taints his Exaltation and seals him within a suit of Power Armor, transforming him into the Abyssal known as The Burned General Entombed in Obsidian and Soulsteel. Meanwhile, the Sidereal mentor separates and hides the newborn Half-Caste twins who The Burned General fathered as a Solar, then goes into hiding with his fellow Chosen of the Maidens who escaped the assault on Yu-Shan. With a Realm and Heaven now under the control of a Deathlord, Creation's only hope lies with the Half-Caste twins: one hidden among the Dynast nobles who oppose the Pale Emperor Cloaked in Darkness and Lightning, the other in the South being raised by the mortal farmers who once took care of The Burned General many years ago...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":814,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","user":"dreamking89","date":". 12-02-2013, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:40:15-08:00","id":21797,"title":"","content":"A long Age ago, in a Creation far, far away...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:47:20-08:00","id":21800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=21797#post21797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A long Age ago, in a Creation far, far away...</div> </div> </div> </div>*The music of the legendary First Age Zenith composer Yahn Villiams begins to play*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T13:12:22-08:00","id":21850,"title":"","content":"In the farthest reaches of the North, a small tribe of Jadeborn live in relative peace building gadgets for long dead Solar kings. One day, while scavenging for supplies, the Jadeborn find a small infant in a basket and raise it as their own, teaching it the secrets of craftsmanship the Jadeborn are legendary for. The baby eventually grows up into a kind young Twilight Exalted who sees the hardships of life in the North and wishes to help. Traveling to the cities of the North, the young inventor gives away his and the Jadeborn's creations to the mortals. Despite the great usefulness of the Twilight's creations, a magistrate ruling in the area inflicts harsh punishments for anyone possessing &quot;tools of the anathema&quot;. Not to mention the angry blizzard god who is chasing the Twilight since he escaped his wrath in their first encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T14:07:49-08:00","id":21882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=21850#post21850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the farthest reaches of the North, a small tribe of Jadeborn live in relative peace building gadgets for long dead Solar kings. One day, while scavenging for supplies, the Jadeborn find a small infant in a basket and raise it as their own, teaching it the secrets of craftsmanship the Jadeborn are legendary for. The baby eventually grows up into a kind young Twilight Exalted who sees the hardships of life in the North and wishes to help. Traveling to the cities of the North, the young inventor gives away his and the Jadeborn's creations to the mortals. Despite the great usefulness of the Twilight's creations, a magistrate ruling in the area inflicts harsh punishments for anyone possessing &quot;tools of the anathema&quot;. Not to mention the angry blizzard god who is chasing the Twilight since he escaped his wrath in their first encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its \u200bthe 1970 Rankin Bass special <i>&quot;Santa Claus is Comin' To Town&quot;</i>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T15:33:30-08:00","id":23352,"title":"","content":"A hard drinking, smooth talking party animal of a Night Caste has been saved from a life of being hunted as an Anathema thanks to a job offer from his mother: a powerful Gold Faction Sidereal (his father is unknown, but some rumors state that it is none other than Chejop Kejak). He now has a steady job in a fate-planning committee, huge apartments in Yu-Shan with an elderly heroic mortal as his butler and access to all the vices of Creation thanks to his unique status (Which he abuses almost nonstop). This puts him at extreme odds with the other Exalted in his committee, who think the Night caste is a spoiled brat who only gets his many benefits and out of so much trouble thanks to the influence of his mother. Few in the fate committee have more animosity and rage towards the Night Caste than one Exalted: a Changing Moon Lunar and the Lunar Mate of the Solar. The other members of this strange Circle include the sociopathic Chosen of Serenity daughter of a powerful Guild merchant, a bookish Chosen of Secrets who is the current lover of the Changing Moon in the Circle, a Chosen of Battles who Exalted from a Nexus pit fighter and a Defiler Caste inventor who somehow manages to (or is allowed to) stay hidden among the denizens of Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":814,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","user":"dreamking89","date":". 12-05-2013, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T09:24:56-08:00","id":37896,"title":"","content":"With little knowledge of this save some discussion in another topic on these forums...is this <i>Archer?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T09:49:04-08:00","id":37907,"title":"","content":"Hrm...*thinks about one I could use--oh!*<br /> <br /> In a particular part of the Coral Archipelago, the almost-grown children within are made to perform a certain manhood ritual, that begins and ends at Calibration. In this rite, they are divided into teams, which are in turn made to compete in a variety of games to indicate their prowess--all who participate are made men, but only those who do the very best in the games are given the biggest honor--they are tasked to guard a priceless local artifact on the last night of Calibration.<br /> <br /> One of the people who takes part in the rites this year, however, has been saddled with worse odds. He, a mortal who will eventually Exalt as a Twilight Caste as a result of his immense interest in invention and discovery, has been put on a team with the son of a deadbeat with ill repute, two harebrained twins, a big and strong but nearly blind fellow, and a prankster with a slight bit of a thieving streak--and on top of that, this is his team to go against the son of one of the greatest warriors in the tribe (he's a bit of a prick). With the help of his stepfather, an Outcaste Terrestrial and <i>former</i> great warrior turned drunkard, though, this boy and his team manage to beat all the other teams and win the highest honor of the rites--the chance to guard their town and nation's treasure.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this treasure is stolen on their night of guarding it, by a pirate of Lintha persuasion. And obviously, the team now can't be made men with the others--their failure was too great. So, realizing that the one way he and his band could be accepted as citizens of Coral was if they were to get this treasure back, the mortal (later Twilight) leader decides to tell his team to venture off on a mission to get their relic back! Joined by his Outcaste stepfather and mentor, and later on a girl from a tribe in the Neck, the crew ventures out to parts unknown, ultimately seeing most of the West, to get that relic--and their honor---back. They succeed beyond their wildest dreams--the captain getting a Twilight Exaltation, his mentor regaining his confidence <i>and</i> getting a prosthetic hand, and the whole band returning as heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":781,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","user":"Chained Divinity","date":". 12-27-2013, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T15:23:00-08:00","id":38447,"title":"","content":"Our story opens with Two young brothers working with archaeologists among a First Age ruin, believed to have once been a powerful manse belonging to Autocthon himself. When their mentor takes the brothers to a chamber beneath the manse, they find what appears to be a hearthstone. However, when the two brothers touch it, the hearthstone splits in half, granting each of the brothers a unique power. Eventually, the accidental death of their mentor causes the brothers to go their separate ways. Years later, the elder brother has used the power of his hearthstone and his knowledge of magitech to marry into a powerful Dynast family. The younger, however, has found a portal to a Void Tainted region of Autocthonia, using his stone to control the great beasts he finds there and become a powerful leader among a southern tribe of raiders. The clash of the two brothers kingdoms causes a war that consumes most of creation and lasts most of their mortal lives, finally culminating with the elder brother reuniting the two hearthstones and earning a Twilight Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T17:34:16-08:00","id":38502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=38447#post38447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our story opens with Two young brothers working with archaeologists among a First Age ruin, believed to have once been a powerful manse belonging to Autocthon himself. When their mentor takes the brothers to a chamber beneath the manse, they find what appears to be a hearthstone. However, when the two brothers touch it, the hearthstone splits in half, granting each of the brothers a unique power. Eventually, the accidental death of their mentor causes the brothers to go their separate ways. Years later, the elder brother has used the power of his hearthstone and his knowledge of magitech to marry into a powerful Dynast family. The younger, however, has found a portal to a Void Tainted region of Autocthonia, using his stone to control the great beasts he finds there and become a powerful leader among a southern tribe of raiders. The clash of the two brothers kingdoms causes a war that consumes most of creation and lasts most of their mortal lives, finally culminating with the elder brother reuniting the two hearthstones and earning a Twilight Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the Brothers' War from Magic: the Gathering?<br /> <br /> YOU'RE CROSSING THE STREAMS, MAN, YOU'RE CROSSING THE STREAMS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T23:45:05-08:00","id":53751,"title":"","content":"The Reclamation has not gone well for mortals. Yu-Shan has basically abandoned Creation, sealing it's gates to protect itself from the rampaging demons that have almost covered Creation. Nearly every major civilization has been overrun, and the last of Creation's denizens have retreated to the Blessed Isle, doing everything they can to even survive the Reclamation. Thanks to First Age artifacts used by soldiers to rapidly move around battlefields and the leadership of the few remaining Sidereals, humanity has been able to survive, but they can only last for so long.<br /> <br /> Our main character is the survivor of a horrific demon attack several years ago, one which was led by a powerful and merciless Soul of Malfeas. Having lost everything, the mortal joins Creation's final army, along with his adopted sister (a skilled warrior) and his scholarly best friend. He is clearly driven to wipe out every demon in Creation, and take back the world that he should be able to see without fear of being torn apart by demons.<br /> <br /> While fighting in this hopeless fight, our soldier is swallowed whole by a behemoth. Instead of dying, he Exalts as a Slayer caste and uses his power to beat back the attacking demons. While he may be Creation's last hope against the Reclamation, his allies are still wary of trusting one infused with the power of the very demons they are fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T09:21:39-08:00","id":54053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=53751#post53751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Reclamation has not gone well for mortals. Yu-Shan has basically abandoned Creation, sealing it's gates to protect itself from the rampaging demons that have almost covered Creation. Nearly every major civilization has been overrun, and the last of Creation's denizens have retreated to the Blessed Isle, doing everything they can to even survive the Reclamation. Thanks to First Age artifacts used by soldiers to rapidly move around battlefields and the leadership of the few remaining Sidereals, humanity has been able to survive, but they can only last for so long.<br /> <br /> Our main character is the survivor of a horrific demon attack several years ago, one which was led by a powerful and merciless Soul of Malfeas. Having lost everything, the mortal joins Creation's final army, along with his adopted sister (a skilled warrior) and his scholarly best friend. He is clearly driven to wipe out every demon in Creation, and take back the world that he should be able to see without fear of being torn apart by demons.<br /> <br /> While fighting in this hopeless fight, our soldier is swallowed whole by a behemoth. Instead of dying, he Exalts as a Slayer caste and uses his power to beat back the attacking demons. While he may be Creation's last hope against the Reclamation, his allies are still wary of trusting one infused with the power of the very demons they are fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shingeki No Kyojin, AKA Attack on Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T14:16:14-08:00","id":54227,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've got one.<br /> <br /> In the deserts of the South, a young man working for a Guild merchant meets and befriends a young boy, who doesn't remember much of his past. The boy has a powerful friend he summons by playing a flute, and the two team up to try and succeed in looting the First Age tomb their town is built around. The satrap of the town - a psychotic, spoiled brat who views people as playthings - also wants the treasures hidden within the tomb. The duo succeeds in surviving the ordeals within the tomb, and in doing so help to free one of the slaves of the satrap, a young girl descended from a tribe known for their immense physical strength. The young man Exalts as a Night Caste, the girl as a Full Moon Lunar, and it is discovered that the boy is a Chosen of Serenity, destined to choose a future king... so it comes as no surprise that he chooses his friend, the newly-Exalted Solar.<br /> <br /> The Night Caste, it turns out, is the son of the king of another kingdom in the South, one that has recently become extremely indebted, economically, to the Scarlet Empire. Assisted by the wisdom of a famed adventurer-king, an Elder Dawn Caste, the trio makes efforts to free the Night Caste's kingdom from both the Empire's reach and the machinations of the organization of Abyssals, bent on destroying the laws of Fate. Disturbingly, their claws seem to have been sunken into the Night Caste's childhood friend....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:41:07-08:00","id":54424,"title":"","content":"Somewhat Obscure....<br /> <br /> In the Midst of the Realm's succession Crisis, an up and coming Officer from a house currently associated with House Tepet, but formerly House Mnemon, finds a First Age Experiment: an Artificial Intelligence that could observe the Loom of Fate. It gives the dynast a choice: do nothing, and let the Realm crumble to Civil War, eventually consuming the entire Creation, or join with it in stabilizing the Realm under Tepet, and eventually all of Creation under the Realm. <br /> <br /> With the AI's help, he is wildly successful, but the new Empress remembers his house's questionable loyalties, and as his successes grow, she worries about his goals. And her policies to create doubts in his mind, not all assuaged by the AI's calculations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:47:28-08:00","id":54554,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> Years after the war between Autochthonia and Creation was ended and peace began to reign, a Soulsteel Caste assassin has pledged himself to serve justice and protect the mortals of Autochthonia after years of manipulation by political forces he can't hope to comprehend. While protecting an unpopular Autocrat in a city ravaged by war, a Soulsteel Apostate and a Solar with Alchemical charms attack with a massive warstrider. The assassin destroys the Warstrider, but fails to protect the Autocrat from the mysterious Apostates. His mortal allies identify them as working with a Guild faction known as Ronin. Desperate for revenge, he has his body upgraded to a general-purpose war model, and wreaks destruction wherever Ronin attempts to set up shop, destroying their Alchemical leaders one after another (Frigid Nightmare Stranger, Soaking Nightmare Rain, Warring Nightmare Winds, and the nameless Solar). He realizes, after slaying the final Apostate, that their ultimate goal is to restart the Locust War by assassinating the new ruler of Creation on a goodwill mission to Autochthonia, and rushes to stop it, only to find the mastermind behind it all: the Autocrat of Clasat, Unerring Veteran. He believes the natural state of mankind, whether they be Autochthonian or hailing from Creation, is war, and that the best thing to do is purge as much life as possible to create a barren, wasted land where only the strong can survive. In a climactic battle, our Soulsteel hero defeats him, but realizes that the desire to exploit the innocent didn't end with Ronin. He leaves the service of the Great Maker to wage his own war on any who would use those weaker than themselves for their own goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","user":"Yue","date":". 05-07-2014, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T23:47:33-08:00","id":55295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <st