s war, and that the best thing to do is purge as much life as possible to create a barren, wasted land where only the strong can survive. In a climactic battle, our Soulsteel hero defeats him, but realizes that the desire to exploit the innocent didn't end with Ronin. He leaves the service of the Great Maker to wage his own war on any who would use those weaker than themselves for their own goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metal Gear Rising?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:57:28-08:00","id":56346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=56292#post56292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Metal Gear Rising?</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I'm slightly upset with myself that I didn't get that. I love that game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":814,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","user":"dreamking89","date":". 01-23-2014, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T09:10:08-08:00","id":69867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chained Divinity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=37907#post37907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm...*thinks about one I could use--oh!*<br /> <br /> In a particular part of the Coral Archipelago, the almost-grown children within are made to perform a certain manhood ritual, that begins and ends at Calibration. In this rite, they are divided into teams, which are in turn made to compete in a variety of games to indicate their prowess--all who participate are made men, but only those who do the very best in the games are given the biggest honor--they are tasked to guard a priceless local artifact on the last night of Calibration.<br /> <br /> One of the people who takes part in the rites this year, however, has been saddled with worse odds. He, a mortal who will eventually Exalt as a Twilight Caste as a result of his immense interest in invention and discovery, has been put on a team with the son of a deadbeat with ill repute, two harebrained twins, a big and strong but nearly blind fellow, and a prankster with a slight bit of a thieving streak--and on top of that, this is his team to go against the son of one of the greatest warriors in the tribe (he's a bit of a prick). With the help of his stepfather, an Outcaste Terrestrial and <i>former</i> great warrior turned drunkard, though, this boy and his team manage to beat all the other teams and win the highest honor of the rites--the chance to guard their town and nation's treasure.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this treasure is stolen on their night of guarding it, by a pirate of Lintha persuasion. And obviously, the team now can't be made men with the others--their failure was too great. So, realizing that the one way he and his band could be accepted as citizens of Coral was if they were to get this treasure back, the mortal (later Twilight) leader decides to tell his team to venture off on a mission to get their relic back! Joined by his Outcaste stepfather and mentor, and later on a girl from a tribe in the Neck, the crew ventures out to parts unknown, ultimately seeing most of the West, to get that relic--and their honor---back. They succeed beyond their wildest dreams--the captain getting a Twilight Exaltation, his mentor regaining his confidence <i>and</i> getting a prosthetic hand, and the whole band returning as heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm going to put this back up for guessing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T10:35:08-08:00","id":69900,"title":"","content":"That seems like an overwhelmingly specific list of characters, CD - I think that if nobody got it right away, it's probable that none of the dozen or so people following this thread have seen (or played, or read) it besides yourself. I will venture to bet that it's one of a number of shows/games based loosely on Norse Mythology, though, since that sure sounds like Hod, Loki, Odin, and possibly Freya/Freyr.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It is an alternate history of Creation, and The Empress has not disappeared. The Solars have not returned. And yet, still The Realm knows turmoil.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empress is growing old, and the magics she uses to sustain her vitality drain more and more of her time and Essence. Her Sidereal advisors take advantage of the situation to undercut her clout and authority, working towards a new ruler who will prove more tractable... and perhaps towards something more. They have spent over a thousand years on a scheme to draw out a Solar Exaltation into a vessel properly prepared and indoctrinated by the Sidereals, to have a ruler with the power of the Solars of old, but bound to their will, keeping the peace of their Realm.<br /> <br /> One such Sidereal is Yisuka Atadi. Sent to advise (and seduce, and manipulate) Tepet Arada, her orders were clear: produce no viable heirs, and allow no other woman to get close enough to do so - Chejop Kejak had decreed that House Tepet needed a little internal strife to check their growing ambitions and clear the way for what was to come. Of these orders, she heeded only the latter, and her daughter with Arada, Tepet Ejava, proved such a genius in so many fields (even while young and unExalted) that Tepet's star rose higher than ever, and House Mnemon felt compelled to act.<br /> <br /> Mnemon ceded the all-important satrapy of Gem to House Tepet... but first ensured that it was in a state of both political corruption and near-civil war. Since the resources (including both gemstones and the Yasal Crystals which are key to maintaining the Realm's infrastructure) from Gem cannot be disrupted, there was no alternative but for Arada and his family to personally supervise the situation. This was, of course, a trap, and of course Arada knew it, but he walked into it trusting in the strength and loyalty of his Sworn Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> And he died.<br /> <br /> Betrayed by one who had sworn the Brother's Oath, Arada died with most of his allies and retainers. But Yisuka used her Sidereal arts to escape with Ejava, and they hid in the desert. What's more, the stress of the battle caused Ejava to draw the Solar Exaltation which the Sidereals had hunted... but she had not been indoctrinated from birth. The plan was ruined, and Kejak, along with (though for entirely different reasons from) Mnemon wishes to see the girl dead. All of Creation stands opposed to these two.<br /> <br /> Except, perhaps, for the mysterious and reviled Dune People, who may hold deeper answers than either The Realm or Heaven thought possible...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 02-11-2014, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T10:41:33-08:00","id":69904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hrm...*thinks about one I could use--oh!*<br /> <br /> In a particular part of the Coral Archipelago, the almost-grown children within are made to perform a certain manhood ritual, that begins and ends at Calibration. In this rite, they are divided into 