st certainly the first book in the Brother-Band Chronicles by John Flanagan. Took me a second to remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/770-eldrvarya","name":"Eldrvarya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T11:26:08-08:00","id":69926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69900#post69900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an alternate history of Creation, and The Empress has not disappeared. The Solars have not returned. And yet, still The Realm knows turmoil.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empress is growing old, and the magics she uses to sustain her vitality drain more and more of her time and Essence. Her Sidereal advisors take advantage of the situation to undercut her clout and authority, working towards a new ruler who will prove more tractable... and perhaps towards something more. They have spent over a thousand years on a scheme to draw out a Solar Exaltation into a vessel properly prepared and indoctrinated by the Sidereals, to have a ruler with the power of the Solars of old, but bound to their will, keeping the peace of their Realm.<br /> <br /> One such Sidereal is Yisuka Atadi. Sent to advise (and seduce, and manipulate) Tepet Arada, her orders were clear: produce no viable heirs, and allow no other woman to get close enough to do so - Chejop Kejak had decreed that House Tepet needed a little internal strife to check their growing ambitions and clear the way for what was to come. Of these orders, she heeded only the latter, and her daughter with Arada, Tepet Ejava, proved such a genius in so many fields (even while young and unExalted) that Tepet's star rose higher than ever, and House Mnemon felt compelled to act.<br /> <br /> Mnemon ceded the all-important satrapy of Gem to House Tepet... but first ensured that it was in a state of both political corruption and near-civil war. Since the resources (including both gemstones and the Yasal Crystals which are key to maintaining the Realm's infrastructure) from Gem cannot be disrupted, there was no alternative but for Arada and his family to personally supervise the situation. This was, of course, a trap, and of course Arada knew it, but he walked into it trusting in the strength and loyalty of his Sworn Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> And he died.<br /> <br /> Betrayed by one who had sworn the Brother's Oath, Arada died with most of his allies and retainers. But Yisuka used her Sidereal arts to escape with Ejava, and they hid in the desert. What's more, the stress of the battle caused Ejava to draw the Solar Exaltation which the Sidereals had hunted... but she had not been indoctrinated from birth. The plan was ruined, and Kejak, along with (though for entirely different reasons from) Mnemon wishes to see the girl dead. All of Creation stands opposed to these two.<br /> <br /> Except, perhaps, for the mysterious and reviled Dune People, who may hold deeper answers than either The Realm or Heaven thought possible...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Frank Herbert's <i>Dune</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T12:13:19-08:00","id":69942,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldrvarya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69904#post69904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is almost certainly the first book in the Brother-Band Chronicles by John Flanagan. Took me a second to remember.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Incorrect technically in that it's the whole series. But you were pretty much right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T12:20:19-08:00","id":69944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chained Divinity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69942#post69942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Incorrect technically in that it's the whole series. But you were pretty much right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well. I've only read the first one. Just couldn't get into the series like I did the Ranger's Apprentice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/770-eldrvarya","name":"Eldrvarya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T12:37:34-08:00","id":69955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69926#post69926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Frank Herbert's <i>Dune</i></div> </div> </div> </div>But of course!<br /> <br /> <br /> As The Reclaimation ramps up and threatens to unleash demon armies upon Creation, a rogue Scourge Martial Artist known as the Pilgrim In Red fights back, dispatching Malfeas' agents with a demonic daiklave, and an arsenal of new weapons he forges from the many Second Circle demons he slays. But even he may not be enough to prevent Malfeas from intruding directly into Nexus when he is confronted by his own twin brother, an Infernal Exalt in his own right known as Blue Vigil. Will the heroic Pilgrim's infamously unpredictable luck hold out, or is this celebration about to descend into madness?<br /> <br /> (I may be a bad person for this one.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T12:46:32-08:00","id":69959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69955#post69955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But of course!<br /> <br /> <br /> As The Reclaimation ramps up and threatens to unleash demon armies upon Creation, a rogue Scourge Martial Artist known as the Pilgrim In Red fights back, dispatching Malfeas' agents with a demonic daiklave, and an arsenal of new weapons he forges from the many Second Circle demons he slays. But even he may not be enough to prevent Malfeas from intruding directly into Nexus when he is confronted by his own twin brother, an Infernal Exalt in his own right known as Blue Vigil. Will the heroic Pilgrim's infamously unpredictable luck hold out, or is this celebration about to descend into madness?<br /> <br /> (I may be a bad person for this one.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to guess Devil May Cry 3, but your statement at the end means it's probably the &quot;reboot&quot;. Donte and Vorgil, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T13:08:53-08:00","id":69977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69959#post69959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to guess Devil May Cry 3, but your statement at the end means it's probably the &quot;reboot&quot;. Donte and Vorgil, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>How would a riff on &quot;this party's getting crazy&quot; mean it's the reboot? Devil May Cry 3 all the way!<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a tale of Essence and Artifacts.<br /> <br /> In the First Age, there emerged a Daiklave of great and terrible power. Some say it was a Third Circle Demon that wore the form of a sword, some say it was Soulsteel forged from a legendary villain like Gorol Thrice-Damned, and some say that the truth is darker and more mysterious than even that. What is certain is that the blade known as Holocaust's Bite was a great and terrible weapon - to powerful for the Lawgivers to resist its use, and too terrible for even them to withstand the consequences.<br /> <br /> One Lawgiver feared the power of the cursed blade so greatly, he forged his own Shard - costing his life and so much more in the process - into a weapon to counterbalance Holocaust's Bite's evil. This was known as the Final Sword, for the greatest weaponsmith of the age would never smith another after it. In the Usurpation, both claimed the lives of many enemies, but neither was recovered by the Sidereal host. The weapons, and their legends faded from Creation.<br /> <br /> But nothing stays lost forever.<br /> <br /> In RY 584, rumors of an ultimate blade began to once again circulate in the Scavenger Lands. Servants of every power in the region, as well as the Realm, and solitary wanderers from even further afield, came seeking the blade which give them ultimate dominance of all enemies. Of course, the blade they found was Holocaust's Bite, and its evil quickly corrupted the one who held it. In a chaos of legendary warriors and dark powers, the sure outcome seems to be a feast of destruction for the evil weapon... unless the Final Sword should return to tame its old foe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T13:15:51-08:00","id":69985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69977#post69977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would a riff on &quot;this party's getting crazy&quot; mean it's the reboot? Devil May Cry 3 all the way!<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a tale of Essence and Artifacts.<br /> <br /> In the First Age, there emerged a Daiklave of great and terrible power. Some say it was a Third Circle Demon that wore the form of a sword, some say it was Soulsteel forged from a legendary villain like Gorol Thrice-Damned, and some say that the truth is darker and more mysterious than even that. What is certain is that the blade known as Holocaust's Bite was a great and terrible weapon - to powerful for the Lawgivers to resist its use, and too terrible for even them to withstand the consequences.<br /> <br /> One Lawgiver feared the power of the cursed blade so greatly, he forged his own Shard - costing his life and so much more in the process - into a weapon to counterbalance Holocaust's Bite's evil. This was known as the Final Sword, for the greatest weaponsmith of the age would never smith another after it. In the Usurpation, both claimed the lives of many enemies, but neither was recovered by the Sidereal host. The weapons, and their legends faded from Creation.<br /> <br /> But nothing stays lost forever.<br /> <br /> In RY 584, rumors of an ultimate blade began to once again circulate in the Scavenger Lands. Servants of every power in the region, as well as the Realm, and solitary wanderers from even further afield, came seeking the blade which give them ultimate dominance of all enemies. Of course, the blade they found was Holocaust's Bite, and its evil quickly corrupted the one who held it. In a chaos of legendary warriors and dark powers, the sure outcome seems to be a feast of destruction for the evil weapon... unless the Final Sword should return to tame its old foe.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is <i>Soul Calibur</i>?<br /> <br /> .... I'll take Awesome Fighting Games for 500, Mr Kejak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T13:46:02-08:00","id":70014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69985#post69985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is <i>Soul Calibur</i>?<br /> <br /> .... I'll take Awesome Fighting Games for 500, Mr Kejak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll count it, but Jeopardy would dock you for saying Soul Calibur, when this is the original Soul Blade (also called Soul Edge). Those guys are serious sticklers for precision. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's not like <i>haven't</i> spent years of my life obsessing about fighting game plots or anything, but I think it would be a little obvious to immediately smash to BlazBlue at this stage (of history), so let's try a different genre, and something a little more obscure.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the distant past, glorious god-kings fought a new and fearsome foe - betrayers who sought to kill them all. One of them would not fall. He fought back. He survived. He saved the world.<br /> <br /> He has been crushing it in his iron fist for 1000 years.<br /> <br /> The Lord Lawgiver's rule is absolute, and he has brutally crushed rebellions and hope itself for longer than any other being yet living can remember - even the Dragon-Blooded elite, favored by the Lord Lawgiver with rulership over lesser beings. Beneath black skies that block the gaze of the Unconquered Sun, he sits in the Imperial Manse and directs wholesale slaughter of any who even contemplate rebellion.<br /> <br /> But contemplate they do. Litany Of Secrets, an almost unheard-of peasant who Exalted as a Dragonblood, is bringing together a team of criminals and con artists. Their mission: to run a scam on a being greater than a god, which just might be enough to save the world... if they live that long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T16:28:33-08:00","id":70119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=69977#post69977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would a riff on &quot;this party's getting crazy&quot; mean it's the reboot? Devil May Cry 3 all the way!<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't the statement on the end, and you would have been a very bad person for mentioning the reboot. Also, you left out Arkham and Lady.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T16:48:15-08:00","id":70136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70119#post70119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you left out Arkham and Lady.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blame backlash against my goofily long Dune reference.<br /> <br /> Arkham is an Outcaste sorcerer-turned-Akuma. Lady is his Daughter - decide for yourself if you think she should be a Dragon-Blood, too, or just a Heroic Mortal (given my 2E background, my instinct is to go DB, but I can see a strong case flavorfully for the latter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T17:17:49-08:00","id":70158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70014#post70014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll count it, but Jeopardy would dock you for saying Soul Calibur, when this is the original Soul Blade (also called Soul Edge). Those guys are serious sticklers for precision. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's not like <i>haven't</i> spent years of my life obsessing about fighting game plots or anything, but I think it would be a little obvious to immediately smash to BlazBlue at this stage (of history), so let's try a different genre, and something a little more obscure.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the distant past, glorious god-kings fought a new and fearsome foe - betrayers who sought to kill them all. One of them would not fall. He fought back. He survived. He saved the world.<br /> <br /> He has been crushing it in his iron fist for 1000 years.<br /> <br /> The Lord Lawgiver's rule is absolute, and he has brutally crushed rebellions and hope itself for longer than any other being yet living can remember - even the Dragon-Blooded elite, favored by the Lord Lawgiver with rulership over lesser beings. Beneath black skies that block the gaze of the Unconquered Sun, he sits in the Imperial Manse and directs wholesale slaughter of any who even contemplate rebellion.<br /> <br /> But contemplate they do. Litany Of Secrets, an almost unheard-of peasant who Exalted as a Dragonblood, is bringing together a team of criminals and con artists. Their mission: to run a scam on a being greater than a god, which just might be enough to save the world... if they live that long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid I can't think of anything that matches this... I bow to your superior knowledge of Awesome Fighting Games, Mr Kejak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T17:28:05-08:00","id":70161,"title":"","content":"I apologize for being unclear, Noodle - I meant to say that another fighting game right away was too obvious, so this is something else (not a video game at all, in fact).<br /> <br /> I certainly <i>will</i> drop another fighting game sooner or later, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T05:09:48-08:00","id":70502,"title":"","content":"Okay, time for a funny one...<br /> <br /> A bold barbarian from an unnamed land (probably near An-Teng) was just about to finish up his typical day of murdering Tengese soldiers with a bit of philandering at a nearby bar, when a drunken bout with another soldier leads to his arrest! Once there, he's brought before one of the local princes, flabby and soft from the comforts of civilization, and sentence to imprisonment and slave labor, possibly indefinitely. He eventually escapes, and discovers a scantily clad female about to be harmed (possibly sexually) by a priest in some dark ritual--and saves her, of course. After learning a bit about her, that she's a minor Tengese noblewoman who was to be married off to the prince, he learns shortly thereafter that the prince is a terrible ruler who maintains power by sheer force, and that he's apparently part of some Yozi cult, as there are many priests in the area and the last fight he has before leaving the area again is with some strange bloodsucking demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T06:27:09-08:00","id":70535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=56292#post56292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Metal Gear Rising?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I'm late! Yes, that's correct!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T13:15:49-08:00","id":70812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=54227#post54227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I've got one.<br /> <br /> In the deserts of the South, a young man working for a Guild merchant meets and befriends a young boy, who doesn't remember much of his past. The boy has a powerful friend he summons by playing a flute, and the two team up to try and succeed in looting the First Age tomb their town is built around. The satrap of the town - a psychotic, spoiled brat who views people as playthings - also wants the treasures hidden within the tomb. The duo succeeds in surviving the ordeals within the tomb, and in doing so help to free one of the slaves of the satrap, a young girl descended from a tribe known for their immense physical strength. The young man Exalts as a Night Caste, the girl as a Full Moon Lunar, and it is discovered that the boy is a Chosen of Serenity, destined to choose a future king... so it comes as no surprise that he chooses his friend, the newly-Exalted Solar.<br /> <br /> The Night Caste, it turns out, is the son of the king of another kingdom in the South, one that has recently become extremely indebted, economically, to the Scarlet Empire. Assisted by the wisdom of a famed adventurer-king, an Elder Dawn Caste, the trio makes efforts to free the Night Caste's kingdom from both the Empire's reach and the machinations of the organization of Abyssals, bent on destroying the laws of Fate. Disturbingly, their claws seem to have been sunken into the Night Caste's childhood friend....</div> </div> </div> </div>So... nobody's got this one? Anyone? Anyone at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T17:18:28-08:00","id":70933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70812#post70812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... nobody's got this one? Anyone? Anyone at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magi: Secret of the Labyrinth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T17:22:07-08:00","id":70935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chained Divinity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70502#post70502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, time for a funny one...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that one thing, isn't it? The one with the scarlet emerald?<br /> <br /> Argon. <i>The Eye of Argon</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:21:23-08:00","id":70972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70935#post70935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that one thing, isn't it? The one with the scarlet emerald?<br /> <br /> Argon. <i>The Eye of Argon</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dear lord. You're right - it totally is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:52:18-08:00","id":71023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70933#post70933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Magi: Secret of the Labyrinth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ding! One of the most Exatled-y anime on the market!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T07:30:56-08:00","id":71269,"title":"","content":"In the midst of the Shogunate, an Air Aspect Dragon Blood of low rank and dishonoured lineage seeks out a lone Solar of the Dawn Caste, living in unconcerned solitude to perfect the forgotten fighting style of his prior incarnation, that she might recruit his aid in acquiring the twelve legendary daiklaves of an ancient master smith, each of which reaped tremendous destruction in the Usurpation, that the Shogun might secure his power in perpetuity and she might rise to the highest prestige.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T07:48:38-08:00","id":71289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71269#post71269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the midst of the Shogunate, an Air Aspect Dragon Blood of low rank and dishonoured lineage seeks out a lone Solar of the Dawn Caste, living in unconcerned solitude to perfect the forgotten fighting style of his prior incarnation, that she might recruit his aid in acquiring the twelve legendary daiklaves of an ancient master smith, each of which reaped tremendous destruction in the Usurpation, that the Shogun might secure his power in perpetuity and she might rise to the highest prestige.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely, one cannot mention Katanagatari without either specifying that the Dawn's style &quot;be the ultimate swordsman with no sword,&quot; or that the Air Aspect's plan to gain his loyalty is that he will fall in love with her. Is this a different assemble-legendary-weapons story with which I am unfamilar?<br /> <br /> If so,could you PM the real answer to me? I love a good assemble-legendary-weapons story!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T07:52:29-08:00","id":71293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71289#post71289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Surely, one cannot mention Katanagatari without either specifying that the Dawn's style &quot;be the ultimate swordsman with no sword,&quot; or that the Air Aspect's plan to gain his loyalty is that he will fall in love with her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they can. Let me check.<br /> <br /> .....<br /> <br /> Yep, I totally alluded to Katanagatari without including either of those details.<br /> <br /> Am I... a wizard?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(It's actually kind of amazing how easily it fits into Exalted as is, with pretty much no need for altered details or aesthetics)</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T09:37:27-08:00","id":71383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71293#post71293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally alluded to Katanagatari without including either of those details.<br /> <br /> Am I... a wizard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not! &quot;Wizard&quot; is a forbidden word in Exalted. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71293#post71293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It's actually kind of amazing how easily it fits into Exalted as is, with pretty much no need for altered details or aesthetics)</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially once 3E adds Evocations, to help express all the crazy powers of those swords.<br /> <br /> Although, if you were <i>just</i> building your game for Katanagatari, I would remove or reduce native Charms entirely, so emphasize how these people were empowered by the swords, first and foremost. I mean, look how fast magical ninja with no swords go down, time after time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70014#post70014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the distant past, glorious god-kings fought a new and fearsome foe - betrayers who sought to kill them all. One of them would not fall. He fought back. He survived. He saved the world.<br /> <br /> He has been crushing it in his iron fist for 1000 years.<br /> <br /> The Lord Lawgiver's rule is absolute, and he has brutally crushed rebellions and hope itself for longer than any other being yet living can remember - even the Dragon-Blooded elite, favored by the Lord Lawgiver with rulership over lesser beings. Beneath black skies that block the gaze of the Unconquered Sun, he sits in the Imperial Manse and directs wholesale slaughter of any who even contemplate rebellion.<br /> <br /> But contemplate they do. Litany Of Secrets, an almost unheard-of peasant who Exalted as a Dragonblood, is bringing together a team of criminals and con artists. Their mission: to run a scam on a being greater than a god, which just might be enough to save the world... if they live that long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, it seems possible that nobody else here has read these fine novels. Or perhaps I shall be pleasantly surprised in the near future. In either case, no time to brood - let's get a new one out there!<br /> <br /> <br /> In the wake of the Great Contagion, a Twilight Caste Solar awakes with no memories.<br /> <br /> There is nobody left to fill in the gaps for him. The only other people in the area are now either left undead by the necromatic plague, or dream-eaten husks who aimlessly wander in villages they barely remember how to tend, easy prey for their zombified former kin.<br /> <br /> And yet, the Solar must endure. Must build great new works, and tunnel through the earth to more useful ruins of the past, as well as the resources needed to build something worthwhile in these wastes... or just to continue the endless struggle for food. It won't be easy.<br /> <br /> As well as the undead, this place so close to the Bordermarches is plagued by Wyld-mutated spiders and stranger creatures which seem to have no life beyond blowing apart everything the Twilight so desperately builds. And worse: strange demons, spawn of The Ebon Dragon, which act to bring the world into tune with an unknowable purpose, and seek to kill anything that notices their existence.<br /> <br /> The Twilight's journey will lead into The Underworld, and even (with the help of a long-abandoned Manse) Malfeas itself. Who knows what must be built to get there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T10:58:39-08:00","id":71436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71383#post71383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the wake of the Great Contagion, a Twilight Caste Solar awakes with no memories.<br /> <br /> There is nobody left to fill in the gaps for him. The only other people in the area are now either left undead by the necromatic plague, or dream-eaten husks who aimlessly wander in villages they barely remember how to tend, easy prey for their zombified former kin.<br /> <br /> And yet, the Solar must endure. Must build great new works, and tunnel through the earth to more useful ruins of the past, as well as the resources needed to build something worthwhile in these wastes... or just to continue the endless struggle for food. It won't be easy.<br /> <br /> As well as the undead, this place so close to the Bordermarches is plagued by Wyld-mutated spiders and stranger creatures which seem to have no life beyond blowing apart everything the Twilight so desperately builds. And worse: strange demons, spawn of The Ebon Dragon, which act to bring the world into tune with an unknowable purpose, and seek to kill anything that notices their existence.<br /> <br /> The Twilight's journey will lead into The Underworld, and even (with the help of a long-abandoned Manse) Malfeas itself. Who knows what must be built to get there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be mistaken, but I do believe that's &quot;Minecraft&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:43:57-08:00","id":71475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71436#post71436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be mistaken, but I do believe that's &quot;Minecraft&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>8)<br /> <br /> You're on top of my references, Noodle. Hard to say whether that's good or bad...<br /> <br /> <br /> On a humble farm in the Hundred Kingdoms was born Meadow Flower, the most beautiful mortal of the Second Age. She grew up there, alone but for a servant boy, and perhaps inevitably, they fell in love. But when he left to seek his fortune, he died, and her heart was broken.<br /> <br /> But the story doesn't end there. It's also got a prince, who wishes to marry her, and the Guild Factor he hires to kill her as part of a scheme. It's got Wyld-tained beasts prowling the rivers, and Outcaste mercenaries who serve The Guild, but secretly wish to do good and a harrowing journey through an uncapped Fire-aspected Demense, lair to a drea Lunar and his ratman spawn. It has betrayal and mystery and pirates and great necrotech machines made by a mad Liminal who is secretly the creation of his own cruel experiments which began before his Exaltation.<br /> <br /> And, of course, it has true love, strong enough that the serving boy, facing certain death, instead became first an Abyssal, then a renegade, and finally won his way to being a Solar so that he could reunite with Meadow Flower.<br /> <br /> ... it also has kissing, I suppose. But you can skip that part, if you wish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:49:38-08:00","id":71479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71475#post71475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 8)<br /> <br /> You're on top of my references, Noodle. Hard to say whether that's good or bad...<br /> <br /> <br /> On a humble farm in the Hundred Kingdoms was born Meadow Flower, the most beautiful mortal of the Second Age. She grew up there, alone but for a servant boy, and perhaps inevitably, they fell in love. But when he left to seek his fortune, he died, and her heart was broken.<br /> <br /> But the story doesn't end there. It's also got a prince, who wishes to marry her, and the Guild Factor he hires to kill her as part of a scheme. It's got Wyld-tained beasts prowling the rivers, and Outcaste mercenaries who serve The Guild, but secretly wish to do good and a harrowing journey through an uncapped Fire-aspected Demense, lair to a drea Lunar and his ratman spawn. It has betrayal and mystery and pirates and great necrotech machines made by a mad Liminal who is secretly the creation of his own cruel experiments which began before his Exaltation.<br /> <br /> And, of course, it has true love, strong enough that the serving boy, facing certain death, instead became first an Abyssal, then a renegade, and finally won his way to being a Solar so that he could reunite with Meadow Flower.<br /> <br /> ... it also has kissing, I suppose. But you can skip that part, if you wish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that is definitely <i>The Princess Bride</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/770-eldrvarya","name":"Eldrvarya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:12:10-08:00","id":71503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldrvarya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71479#post71479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that is definitely <i>The Princess Bride</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course!<br /> <br /> <br /> Each year, in Nexus, is held one of the premier martial arts tournaments of Creation. No school sanctions it, and no nation provides the prize, but still, warriors from across Creation flock to attend, for the pot is well-financed by an alliance of Nexus gangs and Guild Princes from around the region - a fearsome council known collectively as the Law of Shadows, who seek to find new enforcers and draw out (then assassinate) potential problems.<br /> <br /> But this year, it's going to much bigger, and more dangerous.<br /> <br /> The Law of Shadows has been secretly subverted by the mysterious Chosen of She Who Lives In Her Name known as the Yeddim Shadow Warlord, or sometimes as the Black Flame Beast. He has developed an art designed to merge two Exaltations, similar to adding Primordial power to an existing Exaltation, and wishes to use the tournament the find the most powerful Exalt in the East, to increase his own strength. His standards are high - already, he has a fearsome Full-Moon Lunar (Tiger's Talon), a Second-Circle demon (Gorlab the Darkfist), and a renegade Deathknight (Beauty Behind The Killer's Mask) in his service... yet he deems none of them worthy.<br /> <br /> Many will answer the call, from Realm Magistrate whose father the Yeddim Shadow Warlord killed (Peleps Riichung), to the Lookshyan officer seeking his lost commander (Karal Kokatsu), to a Chimera from the South (The White Demon), to an Immaculate Monk (Rice Grows Through The Storm), to a Jade-caste Alchemical (Grief-Breaking Engine), to a mysterious monk who may be a God in disguise (Darushimu). But the biggest threats (and, from the Warlord's point of view, potential gains) are probably a Dawn Caste known as Rising Dragon, and the Abyssal who has stalked him since the day he Exalted, Impossible Underworld Killer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 02-13-2014, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:52:10-08:00","id":71538,"title":"","content":"Street Fighter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:12:06-08:00","id":71553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71538#post71538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Street Fighter.</div> </div> </div> </div>So true.<br /> <br /> I thought this one might throw some people since Akuma isn't, well, an Akuma (as an evil swap of Ryu, I thought he did the Abyssal thing better, while Bison needs his Mind-Hand Manipulation). But you saw right through it - kudos!<br /> <br /> Coming up with fighting games is harder than I expected, actually, given that Shards already has an alleged Street Fighter homage, which really read to me more like Tekken-meets-King of Fighters. And I thought about doing one for Marvel vs. Capcom, but that was too insane, and though I love me JoJo games almost as much as JoJo comics/anime, that was already taken before I even saw this thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> A young Solar in an isolated Eastern tribe faces an impossible choice, and decides to become an Akuma in order to save his people from an insane Behemoth. Yet his soul remain unbowed and he resists his Urge, leaving his tribe to seek a cure.<br /> <br /> What he finds is a whole world beyond his understanding. Most notably, an Immaculate Monk conspires with a willful Outcaste queen to destroy a powerful Directional God, and is opposed by the Solar's own Lunar Mate. Can he keep peace between the warring factions, and also the warring tides of Essence within his own body?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:27:16-08:00","id":71569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71553#post71553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A young Solar in an isolated Eastern tribe faces an impossible choice, and decides to become an Akuma in order to save his people from an insane Behemoth. Yet his soul remain unbowed and he resists his Urge, leaving his tribe to seek a cure.<br /> <br /> What he finds is a whole world beyond his understanding. Most notably, an Immaculate Monk conspires with a willful Outcaste queen to destroy a powerful Directional God, and is opposed by the Solar's own Lunar Mate. Can he keep peace between the warring factions, and also the warring tides of Essence within his own body?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Mononokehime</i>, even though Ashitaka is not an akuma at all; he's just cursed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T13:45:28-08:00","id":71579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71569#post71569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Mononokehime</i>, even though Ashitaka is not an akuma at all; he's just cursed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really know of any other curses dramatic enough to seem like they should dictate a Solar's arc. Really, if there's one thing I don't feel right about here, it's the Solar Bond bit - San certainly does <i>not</i> have an immediate outpouring of trust when she first sees Ashitaka, so that probably doesn't fit.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, you got it - onwards!<br /> <br /> <br /> House Bencha has fallen on hard times. A century ago, it was a Great House, entrusted with powerful satrapies, and led by perhaps the foremost Sorcerer-Engineer of the Blessed Isle - Bencha Jingyu. But Jingyu died under mysterious circumstances, and was succeeded by his son, Tadeu, who came to be called the Father of Rust, for whatever he touched sank into decline. House Bencha now has only a single minor satrapy in The West and a scant handful of holdings on the Isle. The Great Houses only deign to treat with Bencha when they need Tadeu to repair Manses or Artifacts left from his father, and he only sometimes succeeds. He is even less successful at raising his two sons, Denan and Hanaku.<br /> <br /> Still, due to House Bencha's illustrious past, the Immaculate Order wishes to see it preserved, even if the rest of The Realm would just as soon forget it. They sent the Earth Dragon master Rock of Strength to tend to the family. And has his hands full, warding off the attacks of the Poison Butterfly clan of ninja, the Outcaste Lord of the Iron Jaw, and many other foes... in addition to the dangerous consequences of Bencha Tadeu's own experiments with Sorcery and Artifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:59:32-08:00","id":71903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70935#post70935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that one thing, isn't it? The one with the scarlet emerald?<br /> <br /> Argon. <i>The Eye of Argon</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and mister Kejak (assuming his surname goes last, of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) are both correct!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T07:31:17-08:00","id":71962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71579#post71579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House Bencha has fallen on hard times. A century ago, it was a Great House, entrusted with powerful satrapies, and led by perhaps the foremost Sorcerer-Engineer of the Blessed Isle - Bencha Jingyu. But Jingyu died under mysterious circumstances, and was succeeded by his son, Tadeu, who came to be called the Father of Rust, for whatever he touched sank into decline. House Bencha now has only a single minor satrapy in The West and a scant handful of holdings on the Isle. The Great Houses only deign to treat with Bencha when they need Tadeu to repair Manses or Artifacts left from his father, and he only sometimes succeeds. He is even less successful at raising his two sons, Denan and Hanaku.<br /> <br /> Still, due to House Bencha's illustrious past, the Immaculate Order wishes to see it preserved, even if the rest of The Realm would just as soon forget it. They sent the Earth Dragon master Rock of Strength to tend to the family. And has his hands full, warding off the attacks of the Poison Butterfly clan of ninja, the Outcaste Lord of the Iron Jaw, and many other foes... in addition to the dangerous consequences of Bencha Tadeu's own experiments with Sorcery and Artifice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Venture Brothers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T07:58:52-08:00","id":71977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71962#post71962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Venture Brothers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew someone had to get that one - right you are!<br /> <br /> But, seriously, if I ever run an Exalted game again, I am totally using the Poison Butterfly Clan.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Chosens' great mistake was assuming that Malfeas was somehow attached to Creation.<br /> <br /> But they themselves had forced the Demon City to be a separate realm. Sorcery and surrender oaths allowed them access to it, but the true substance of Malfeas drifted in the Wyld. The Primordials knew where there bretheren had made other Creations, and one by one, they found them. Their surrender oaths forbid them from claiming outright dominion, but they found the lords and champions of these other Creations, and offered them the power of an Akuma. Enough accepted, and these mighty Akuma would overcome the defenders of Creation after Creation, then use foul geomancy to break those worlds until they, too, fell into Malfeas, fueling the Yozis' might.<br /> <br /> After millennia, they are ready to return, and pit the Akuma of a dozen worlds against the defenders of Creation. They were expecting to find the Solar Deliberative at the height of its power. Instead, there are only scattered traditions, rebellious gods, and a few young Celestial heroes to oppose them.<br /> <br /> Delighted, the Akuma, led by a mad sorcerer and a four-armed beast, lured all their foes to a single island, looking to kill them all at once. Their Surrender Oaths require a fair contest, but even one-on-one battles can be rendered sure things when one side has all the experience and control of the location.<br /> <br /> Will Creation's geomancy, too, fall into Malfeas? Or will a ragtag band of monks, soldiers, and outcasts be enough to win this deadly struggle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T08:15:47-08:00","id":71985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71977#post71977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I knew someone had to get that one - right you are!<br /> <br /> But, seriously, if I ever run an Exalted game again, I am totally using the Poison Butterfly Clan.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Chosens' great mistake was assuming that Malfeas was somehow attached to Creation.<br /> <br /> But they themselves had forced the Demon City to be a separate realm. Sorcery and surrender oaths allowed them access to it, but the true substance of Malfeas drifted in the Wyld. The Primordials knew where there bretheren had made other Creations, and one by one, they found them. Their surrender oaths forbid them from claiming outright dominion, but they found the lords and champions of these other Creations, and offered them the power of an Akuma. Enough accepted, and these mighty Akuma would overcome the defenders of Creation after Creation, then use foul geomancy to break those worlds until they, too, fell into Malfeas, fueling the Yozis' might.<br /> <br /> After millennia, they are ready to return, and pit the Akuma of a dozen worlds against the defenders of Creation. They were expecting to find the Solar Deliberative at the height of its power. Instead, there are only scattered traditions, rebellious gods, and a few young Celestial heroes to oppose them.<br /> <br /> Delighted, the Akuma, led by a mad sorcerer and a four-armed beast, lured all their foes to a single island, looking to kill them all at once. Their Surrender Oaths require a fair contest, but even one-on-one battles can be rendered sure things when one side has all the experience and control of the location.<br /> <br /> Will Creation's geomancy, too, fall into Malfeas? Or will a ragtag band of monks, soldiers, and outcasts be enough to win this deadly struggle?</div> </div> </div> </div>MORTAL KOMBAT! [sound of techno beat intensifies]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T09:21:36-08:00","id":72024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71985#post71985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MORTAL KOMBAT! [sound of techno beat intensifies]</div> </div> </div> </div>FLAWLESS VICTORY<br /> <br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empress has returned as the Ebon Dragon's bride, and her dark pall spreads across the land, spelling the end of the Age. Before the fall of the Five-Score Fellowship, one last prophecy revealed how to break her power, however: destroy the original Broken-Winged Crane... which, fortunately, was accidentally recovered by a mortal thief already. But the wise of Creation despair, for its link to the Yozis is so powerful, even touching it qualifies as &quot;submitting&quot; to its promise of power, and any Exalt who does so near-instantly becomes an Akuma.<br /> <br /> Two things are clear. First, the book must be destroyed, and quickly. Second, it must be moved by a mortal.<br /> <br /> The last non-Akuma Sidereal left alive embarks on a desperate mission, to reach the mortal who holds the book, and keep him safe, while gathering a force of Exalts sufficient to storm the Blessed Isle and ascend Mount Meru - a race against time to use the power of the Elemental Pole of Earth against the book, before the Empress and the Ebon Dragon drag Creation into an eternal night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T10:01:25-08:00","id":72045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=72024#post72024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last non-Akuma Sidereal left alive embarks on a desperate mission, to reach the mortal who holds the book, and keep him safe, while gathering a force of Exalts sufficient to storm the Blessed Isle and ascend Mount Meru - a race against time to use the power of the Elemental Pole of Earth against the book, before the Empress and the Ebon Dragon drag Creation into an eternal night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lord of the Rings, of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A lone Dragonblood is held prisoner in the far South. The chieftan of the Dune People tribe that holds him prisoner hopes to channel his power and become first among Chiefs, and permits him the honor of a duel when one of the chief's rivals tries to kill him - a duel he wins, earning himself power and position among the tribe, position he will eventually abandon when the tribe captures another prisoner, the incomparably beautiful princess of one of the slowly-dying citystates of the deep interior, who our hero will risk everything to rescue from not only the Dune People, but from those suitors in other cities who are desperate to claim her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T13:48:10-08:00","id":72197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=72045#post72045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lord of the Rings, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course!<br /> <br /> You know, I took a perverse glee in adapting a game explicitly marketed as &quot;non-Tolkenein fantasy&quot; to cover Lord of the Rings, but I suppose some would argue that Return of the Scarlet Empress already did the heavy lifting for me.<br /> <br /> Alas, I do not believe I can return the favor by recognizing yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T17:07:35-08:00","id":72328,"title":"","content":"John Carter of Mars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T17:52:33-08:00","id":72345,"title":"","content":"I really need to watch that at some point (I had some of the 70s comics growing up, but it's been a long time).<br /> <br /> <br /> A brother-and-sister team of Realm Patricians have been studying First Age ruins in the deep South for years, when they finally find a guide to take them to a site undisturbed since <i>before</i> the Anathema were usurped.<br /> <br /> There's trouble, of course - from a rival team of excavators, from angry locals, and from their guide's colorful past - but they eventually attain their goal... only to unleash a mad First Age ghost bent on the destruction of Creation!<br /> <br /> There are also some garbage sequels, in which most of them Exalt or something, but really, don't bother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T22:25:51-08:00","id":72472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=72328#post72328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John Carter of Mars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically the book <i>A Princess of Mars</i>, but yeah, the franchise in general is perfect Exalted-fodder for the South, and the visuals in Disney's <i>John Carter</i> are ideal, in particular the airships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T03:53:14-08:00","id":72543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=72345#post72345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really need to watch that at some point (I had some of the 70s comics growing up, but it's been a long time).<br /> <br /> <br /> A brother-and-sister team of Realm Patricians have been studying First Age ruins in the deep South for years, when they finally find a guide to take them to a site undisturbed since <i>before</i> the Anathema were usurped.<br /> <br /> There's trouble, of course - from a rival team of excavators, from angry locals, and from their guide's colorful past - but they eventually attain their goal... only to unleash a mad First Age ghost bent on the destruction of Creation!<br /> <br /> There are also some garbage sequels, in which most of them Exalt or something, but really, don't bother.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Mummy</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T07:38:18-08:00","id":72617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chained Divinity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=72543#post72543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Mummy</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeeeeeeeeeeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's trouble in Gethamame.<br /> <br /> The Deathlord known as the Master Of Creation From The Gaze Of The Grinning Skull marshalls his forces and strikes again and again at the city filled with ruins of First Age technology, which was once his sanctum. And the Master of Gethamame, though he tries to marshal a defense, is disheartened, since his only child (Madas) is a worthless layabout who disappoints his parents, tutors, and subjects constantly. While he has (in the Gethamame tradition) named the far more capable noblewoman guard captain (Aleeta) as his heir, the choice weighs on him.<br /> <br /> But still, Gethamame is defended. When the Deathlord's forces attack, a mysterious hero mounted on a monstrous white tiger emerges to fight them off. Some say is a long-forgotten god, while others whisper stranger rumors - the truth, of course, is that he is a Solar Exalt, guided by his No-Moon Lunar mate, and perhaps most importantly, wielder of the Daiklave called The Power of the Grey Soul. When he holds The Power, it reveals to him many useful Invocations, which are crucial in his battles to protect Gethamame... for example, by hiding the fact that he is actually the disgraced Prince Madas.<br /> <br /> (His sister is a rogue Infernal leading an uprising in Malfeas, but he doesn't know that yet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 02-15-2014, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:26:56-08:00","id":72688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=72617#post72617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeeeeeeeeeeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's trouble in Gethamame.<br /> <br /> The Deathlord known as the Master Of Creation From The Gaze Of The Grinning Skull marshalls his forces and strikes again and again at the city filled with ruins of First Age technology, which was once his sanctum. And the Master of Gethamame, though he tries to marshal a defense, is disheartened, since his only child (Madas) is a worthless layabout who disappoints his parents, tutors, and subjects constantly. While he has (in the Gethamame tradition) named the far more capable noblewoman guard captain (Aleeta) as his heir, the choice weighs on him.<br /> <br /> But still, Gethamame is defended. When the Deathlord's forces attack, a mysterious hero mounted on a monstrous white tiger emerges to fight them off. Some say is a long-forgotten god, while others whisper stranger rumors - the truth, of course, is that he is a Solar Exalt, guided by his No-Moon Lunar mate, and perhaps most importantly, wielder of the Daiklave called The Power of the Grey Soul. When he holds The Power, it reveals to him many useful Invocations, which are crucial in his battles to protect Gethamame... for example, by hiding the fact that he is actually the disgraced Prince Madas.<br /> <br /> (His sister is a rogue Infernal leading an uprising in Malfeas, but he doesn't know that yet.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Painfully, obviously He-Man. So much so that more Deathlords should tell their minions that they could write a book about what their underlings don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T12:32:09-08:00","id":72768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=72688#post72688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Painfully, obviously He-Man. So much so that more Deathlords should tell their minions that they could write a book about what their underlings don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Beast Within The Guise Of Man. Surely someone like Jaw Of The Ever-Baited Trap, Threefold Gaze Of Oblivion, or Lady Of The Cruel Cowl could offer more competence.<br /> <br /> And, hey, <i>painfully</i> obviously? Half of the fun in these is making up the allusions - just be glad I restrained myself from mentioning a Manse shaped like a skull!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T12:58:30-08:00","id":80442,"title":"","content":"I got one:<br /> <br /> A Dynast child has been chosen at birth to be the Exigent of a God of Winters. Knowing she will be hunted and killed for her power, the Exigent's parents force her to keep it a secret all her life, even from her younger sister. She grows more and more powerful as she grows older, and her powers become more and more uncontrollable. Eventually, the Exigent becomes the Patrician of her corner of the Blessed Isle, but she accidentally reveals her power during her coronation. Her people turning against her (thinking she's Anathema), the Exigent runs for her life to the Imperial Mountain. Atop the mountain, she gets her chance to test the limits of her powers, using them to rebuild an icy version of Meru. Meanwhile, the rest of the Blessed Isle has been thrown into an eternal winter. The Exigent's mortal younger sister sets off to find her and get her to end the eternal winter. Along the way, she meets an Eclipse Caste from the barbarian tribes of the North, his Lunar Mate and a winter spirit unknowingly summoned by the Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:59:11-08:00","id":80485,"title":"","content":"That's got to be Frozen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T18:55:53-08:00","id":80694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=70014#post70014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll count it, but Jeopardy would dock you for saying Soul Calibur, when this is the original Soul Blade (also called Soul Edge). Those guys are serious sticklers for precision. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's not like <i>haven't</i> spent years of my life obsessing about fighting game plots or anything, but I think it would be a little obvious to immediately smash to BlazBlue at this stage (of history), so let's try a different genre, and something a little more obscure.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the distant past, glorious god-kings fought a new and fearsome foe - betrayers who sought to kill them all. One of them would not fall. He fought back. He survived. He saved the world.<br /> <br /> He has been crushing it in his iron fist for 1000 years.<br /> <br /> The Lord Lawgiver's rule is absolute, and he has brutally crushed rebellions and hope itself for longer than any other being yet living can remember - even the Dragon-Blooded elite, favored by the Lord Lawgiver with rulership over lesser beings. Beneath black skies that block the gaze of the Unconquered Sun, he sits in the Imperial Manse and directs wholesale slaughter of any who even contemplate rebellion.<br /> <br /> But contemplate they do. Litany Of Secrets, an almost unheard-of peasant who Exalted as a Dragonblood, is bringing together a team of criminals and con artists. Their mission: to run a scam on a being greater than a god, which just might be enough to save the world... if they live that long.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=71383#post71383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alas, it seems possible that nobody else here has read these fine novels. Or perhaps I shall be pleasantly surprised in the near future. In either case, no time to brood - let's get a new one out there!</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be <i>Mistborn: The Final Empire.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Here's one:<br /> Some time after the formation of the Realm, two godblooded scoundrels accidentally sneak onto a Realm Expedition to a long lost city of orichalcum in the East said to be ruled by two Anathema. Managing to escape with their Familiar, they find the city, and due to an amusing coincidence regarding their looks, they are taken to be the two Anathema, who ruled the City as gods. But despite their newfound life of comfort, the Realm Expedition draws closer, and the High Priest of the city suspects that these two are not who they claim to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:11:09-08:00","id":80707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80694#post80694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<br /> Here's one:<br /> Some time after the formation of the Realm, two godblooded scoundrels accidentally sneak onto a Realm Expedition to a long lost city of orichalcum in the East said to be ruled by two Anathema. Managing to escape with their Familiar, they find the city, and due to an amusing coincidence regarding their looks, they are taken to be the two Anathema, who ruled the City as gods. But despite their newfound life of comfort, the Realm Expedition draws closer, and the High Priest of the city suspects that these two are not who they claim to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Road to El Dorado. I have that one memorized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:14:19-08:00","id":80709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80694#post80694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be <i>Mistborn: The Final Empire.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Here's one:<br /> Some time after the formation of the Realm, two godblooded scoundrels accidentally sneak onto a Realm Expedition to a long lost city of orichalcum in the East said to be ruled by two Anathema. Managing to escape with their Familiar, they find the city, and due to an amusing coincidence regarding their looks, they are taken to be the two Anathema, who ruled the City as gods. But despite their newfound life of comfort, the Realm Expedition draws closer, and the High Priest of the city suspects that these two are not who they claim to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I applaud your taste in books, friend.<br /> <br /> And for its own part, I found Journey to El Dorado quite underrated.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Tri-Khan of Ciaroscuro has gone mad - each day, he marries a new wife, and each night, kills her. The city lives in fear. But there is hope - the daughter of one of his Dragon-Blooded advisers has Exalted as an Eclipse. Not wanting to invite the Wyld Hunt or force her father to oppose her, she cannot fight the Tri-Khan. Instead, she volunteers to marry him, and each night tells him a story.<br /> <br /> Of course, the stories tend to have cliffhangers at daybreak, and her skill is such, no man could let her die without knowing the ending. But how long can she keep it up, without having to flare her Anima, and making everything so much worse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:28:03-08:00","id":80714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80709#post80709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tri-Khan of Ciaroscuro has gone mad - each day, he marries a new wife, and each night, kills her. The city lives in fear. But there is hope - the daughter of one of his Dragon-Blooded advisers has Exalted as an Eclipse. Not wanting to invite the Wyld Hunt or force her father to oppose her, she cannot fight the Tri-Khan. Instead, she volunteers to marry him, and each night tells him a story.<br /> <br /> Of course, the stories tend to have cliffhangers at daybreak, and her skill is such, no man could let her die without knowing the ending. But how long can she keep it up, without having to flare her Anima, and making everything so much worse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scheherazade, or the Arabian Nights.<br /> <br /> Here's one I've been trying to work out for a while.<br /> <br /> In a sleepy little village, a minor Patrician has exalted as a Twilight rather late in life. No one is any the wiser, though, not even her extensive network of family and friends. Despite rarely leaving the village, and prefering the quiet life of her little town. Still, she has as sharp a mind as ever, and is quite adept at solving the various mysteries brought to her by that network of family. After all, as she often says, people are quite the same whether it's in a sleepy little village, or the Imperial City.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:43:55-08:00","id":80727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80709#post80709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I applaud your taste in books, friend.<br /> <br /> And for its own part, I found Journey to El Dorado quite underrated.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Tri-Khan of Ciaroscuro has gone mad - each day, he marries a new wife, and each night, kills her. The city lives in fear. But there is hope - the daughter of one of his Dragon-Blooded advisers has Exalted as an Eclipse. Not wanting to invite the Wyld Hunt or force her father to oppose her, she cannot fight the Tri-Khan. Instead, she volunteers to marry him, and each night tells him a story.<br /> <br /> Of course, the stories tend to have cliffhangers at daybreak, and her skill is such, no man could let her die without knowing the ending. But how long can she keep it up, without having to flare her Anima, and making everything so much worse?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>One Thousand and One Nights</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In Whitehall, there is a girl with mismatched eyes, and a difficult home. Eventually having enough, she runs away, getting caught in a massive tide, and washed into a hidden Fae Freehold and shadowland. Twenty four islands, each locked into being a specific time, divided between the Day, associated with the Wyld, and Night, associated with the Abyss, with one more island hidden away at the center by a perpetual storm. Despite the odd Wyld-touched she finds and her own background, the girl manages to fit in well, and even resembles a former Fair Folk Noble, once though to possibly bring peace to the lands by marrying the Ghost-touched Ruler of the Night, before being killed. Unfortunately, the Ghost-touched knows this, and seeks this reminder of his lost love, while his dark, unnamed Grandmother looks on, and things stir deep in the Ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:04:39-08:00","id":80737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80714#post80714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a sleepy little village, a minor Patrician has exalted as a Twilight rather late in life. No one is any the wiser, though, not even her extensive network of family and friends. Despite rarely leaving the village, and prefering the quiet life of her little town. Still, she has as sharp a mind as ever, and is quite adept at solving the various mysteries brought to her by that network of family. After all, as she often says, people are quite the same whether it's in a sleepy little village, or the Imperial City.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Murder, She Wrote.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Somewhere in the Scavenger Lands, the last surviving work of one of the First Age's great Twilight craftsmen works as a Scavenger Lord, and a craftsman himself. An automaton in the shape of heavyset man clad in bulky armor, with no face but his two perfectly round lensed eyes, this last product of ultimate genius leads a team of skilled experts in a long, uphill battle to reclaim the glories and wonders of First Age artifice, and along the way, put an end to attempts to misuse First Age wonders. Fighting the undead, a tyrant's army of warstriders, a rogue crystal intelligence, and worst of all, a particularly crazed Dragon King, he is a two-fisted force for justice in a world more vivid than our own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:06:42-08:00","id":80739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80737#post80737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Murder, She Wrote.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite, though they share the same inspiration","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:29:17-08:00","id":80755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80714#post80714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a sleepy little village, a minor Patrician has exalted as a Twilight rather late in life. No one is any the wiser, though, not even her extensive network of family and friends. Despite rarely leaving the village, and prefering the quiet life of her little town. Still, she has as sharp a mind as ever, and is quite adept at solving the various mysteries brought to her by that network of family. After all, as she often says, people are quite the same whether it's in a sleepy little village, or the Imperial City.</div> </div> </div> </div>Miss Marple, I presume?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80737#post80737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhere in the Scavenger Lands, the last surviving work of one of the First Age's great Twilight craftsmen works as a Scavenger Lord, and a craftsman himself. An automaton in the shape of heavyset man clad in bulky armor, with no face but his two perfectly round lensed eyes, this last product of ultimate genius leads a team of skilled experts in a long, uphill battle to reclaim the glories and wonders of First Age artifice, and along the way, put an end to attempts to misuse First Age wonders. Fighting the undead, a tyrant's army of warstriders, a rogue crystal intelligence, and worst of all, a particularly crazed Dragon King, he is a two-fisted force for justice in a world more vivid than our own.</div> </div> </div> </div>This automaton would not, by any, chance, happen to be some sort of... Atomic Robot?<br /> <br /> <br /> In a strange Shard of Creation, the Dragon-Blooded Usurpation succeeded at wiping out the Solars, but underestimated the loyalty which billions of mortals felt towards their od-kings. They were in turn destroyed, and with the Sidereals in hiding and the Lunars totally absorbed by holding back the Wyld, mortals alone reigned. They slaughtered the kin of the fallen Terrestrials, that no more would rise, and made their kingdoms, and religions which equated the chosen of the Dragons with the Yozis themselves. \u200bYet after the Sword of Creation ended the Great Contagion, the dragon lines shifted, and many, many more Terrestrials were born than in the past Age.<br /> <br /> This is the story of that time, as more and more Terrestrials are born. Some form brutal brotherhoods of terror, seeking to tear down the world which fails to match their desires. But others strike back from the shadows, seeking to protect a world which hates and fears them. Each faction is championed by a potent Sidereal mentor, two men who were once fast friends.<br /> <br /> Welcome to the struggle for the fate of Creation... hope you survive the experience!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:37:33-08:00","id":80757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80755#post80755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This automaton would not, by any, chance, happen to be some sort of... Atomic Robot?</div> </div> </div> </div>He would indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:45:04-08:00","id":80759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80755#post80755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miss Marple, I presume?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, good sir. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T21:09:29-08:00","id":80779,"title":"","content":"<div class=