yxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T22:40:58-08:00","id":80817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80727#post80727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Whitehall, there is a girl with mismatched eyes, and a difficult home. Eventually having enough, she runs away, getting caught in a massive tide, and washed into a hidden Fae Freehold and shadowland. Twenty four islands, each locked into being a specific time, divided between the Day, associated with the Wyld, and Night, associated with the Abyss, with one more island hidden away at the center by a perpetual storm. Despite the odd Wyld-touched she finds and her own background, the girl manages to fit in well, and even resembles a former Fair Folk Noble, once though to possibly bring peace to the lands by marrying the Ghost-touched Ruler of the Night, before being killed. Unfortunately, the Ghost-touched knows this, and seeks this reminder of his lost love, while his dark, unnamed Grandmother looks on, and things stir deep in the Ocean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clive Barker's Abarat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T07:42:15-08:00","id":81028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=80779#post80779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... is that X-men?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keh keh keh...<br /> <br /> <br /> A young apprentice healer in a quiet city sees a Sidereal. Somehow, his eyes can pierce Resplendent Destinies, and his mind resists Arcane Fate. As such, she recruits him to aid her work in the region, but it somehow backfires, and her Exaltation impossibly passes from her into him. Still, there's all kinds of trouble from a nearby Shadowland to be dealt with, so they get to work, him fighting and her advising, until Yu-Shan learns what has happened, and sends elite operatives to recover her.<br /> <br /> How, the boy must ally with a taciturn Lunar, a vengeful Solar archer, and even stranger beings to storm Heaven itself and effect a rescue. Along the way, they will uncover a plot by one of the highest officials in the Bureau of Destiny... which could shatter the very pillars of Creation!<br /> <br /> (Then there's a follow-up involving Getimians which dragged out <i>far</i> too long.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T07:45:24-08:00","id":81029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81028#post81028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keh keh keh...<br /> A young apprentice healer in a quiet city sees a Sidereal. Somehow, his eyes can pierce Resplendent Destinies, and his mind resists Arcane Fate. As such, she recruits him to aid her work in the region, but it somehow backfires, and her Exaltation impossibly passes from her into him. Still, there's all kinds of trouble from a nearby Shadowland to be dealt with, so they get to work, him fighting and her advising, until Yu-Shan learns what has happened, and sends elite operatives to recover her.<br /> How, the boy must ally with a taciturn Lunar, a vengeful Solar archer, and even stranger beings to storm Heaven itself and effect a rescue. Along the way, they will uncover a plot by one of the highest officials in the Bureau of Destiny... which could shatter the very pillars of Creation!<br /> (Then there's a follow-up involving Getimians which dragged out <i>far</i> too long.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right. I spilled some of that on my pants yesterday and took the color right out of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T08:37:40-08:00","id":81064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81029#post81029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, right. I spilled some of that on my pants yesterday and took the color right out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, aren't you quick on the draw... and on the erasure? Still, you may find it a hollow victory.<br /> <br /> <br /> A grand horserace has been planned, from An-Teng to Harborhead! We follow the story of an unlikely pair of companion riders - Whirling Eye (who is secretly an Immaculate Monk racing because if he wins, a small god who asks for worship but truly does protect his people will be spared), and Horned Star (a mortal nobleman who was once a famous jockey, before he was crippled in a ritual to Sondok, and lost the use of his leg). But Star believes that Eye's exotic martial arts may hold the key to his cure, so he enters the race at the last minute, riding on a barely-controlled Simhata.<br /> <br /> They will face many strange foes in the race: a child of Ahlat with a particular command of horses called Lonesome Mountain, a mysterious figure who is actually an undercover All-Seeing Eye operative, a Dune Folk tribesman who wants to leverage his win into a non-agression pact, and the rival team of one of Eye's former companions and a Guild enforcer obsessed with magitech restoration. Yet none seem more dangerous than Raven Fire God, a showy racer who may be responsible for the loss of Star's legs and brother.<br /> <br /> And yet, the race is merely a diversion. In fact, it was arranged by the Tri-Khan to recover numerous fragments of the Broken-Winged Crane scattered across the South. And as the racers find these fragments, they gain shreds of Infernal power... who will be corrupted and who empowered? And even with this new-found power, will any allies left standing be able to overcome the Tri-Khan - an Akuma of incredible might?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T11:33:28-08:00","id":81143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81064#post81064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A grand horserace has been planned, from An-Teng to Harborhead!</div> </div> </div> </div>This was literally all I needed to identify this as <i>JoJo's Bizarre Adventure</i>, part VII:<i> Steel Ball Run</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 02-27-2014, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T12:14:04-08:00","id":81162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81143#post81143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was literally all I needed to identify this as <i>JoJo's Bizarre Adventure</i>, part VII:<i> Steel Ball Run</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well-played. Though I maintain there was <i>some</i> chance I could have written up <i>Hidalgo</i> instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Zu Rat Te, a legendary hero and master of Even Blade Style, just wants to live out his twilight years in peace, and possibly mend fences with Resolute Brigada, who he lives despite an overall awkward relationship. But when his legendary Daiklave is stolen at just the same time he begins hearing rumors of the Lunar assassin who killed his master centuries ago, he comes out of retirement one last time... into a web of intrigue involving an Outcaste Delzahn bandit, a murdered Magistrate, and most notably, the Patrician noblewoman who has secretly Exalted as both a Dawn Caste, and the Solar Mate to the Lunar assassin he seeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T12:19:48-08:00","id":81164,"title":"","content":"During the War with the Bull of the North, a aged Dragonblooded of the very minor family Ben't is living in Ang Teng with his Patrician wife and 5 moral daughters. The talk of the town is when the Fire Aspect Scion of an up-and coming minor house, the Bin Gli, arrive for a vacation, and with him an Air Aspect from the house Ledaal. While the oldest sister and Bin Gli fall into a relationship, Ledaal offends all around him, especially the headstrong Second Ben't sister. Meanwhile, the former Immaculate cousin of the Ben'ts is coming, hoping to marry into the main line, and there are the officers of the Vermilion legion to tempt young hearts, especially those of the youngest sisters. <br /> <br /> <br /> I really liked this work of fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T13:04:42-08:00","id":81188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81164#post81164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the War with the Bull of the North, a aged Dragonblooded of the very minor family Ben't is living in Ang Teng with his Patrician wife and 5 moral daughters. The talk of the town is when the Fire Aspect Scion of an up-and coming minor house, the Bin Gli, arrive for a vacation, and with him an Air Aspect from the house Ledaal. While the oldest sister and Bin Gli fall into a relationship, Ledaal offends all around him, especially the headstrong Second Ben't sister. Meanwhile, the former Immaculate cousin of the Ben'ts is coming, hoping to marry into the main line, and there are the officers of the Vermilion legion to tempt young hearts, especially those of the youngest sisters.<br /> <br /> <br /> I really liked this work of fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proud to say, I already share this judgement.<br /> <br /> Ledaal Fizwil certainly has potential...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T13:30:17-08:00","id":81204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81162#post81162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well-played. Though I maintain there was <i>some</i> chance I could have written up <i>Hidalgo</i> instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Zu Rat Te, a legendary hero and master of Even Blade Style, just wants to live out his twilight years in peace, and possibly mend fences with Resolute Brigada, who he lives despite an overall awkward relationship. But when his legendary Daiklave is stolen at just the same time he begins hearing rumors of the Lunar assassin who killed his master centuries ago, he comes out of retirement one last time... into a web of intrigue involving an Outcaste Delzahn bandit, a murdered Magistrate, and most notably, the Patrician noblewoman who has secretly Exalted as both a Dawn Caste, and the Solar Mate to the Lunar assassin he seeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't..<i>.Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon</i>, is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T15:54:10-08:00","id":81282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81204#post81204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't..<i>.Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon</i>, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also known as &quot;Pride And Prejudice with swords&quot; - how apropos!<br /> <br /> <br /> In Nexus, a mysterious behemoth tears up from beneath the earth. It rampages through the city for hours before The Emissary corners it, fights it, and kills it... but The Emissary, too, is destroyed. A confused funeral is held by a city which never truly believed The Emissary was mortal, and then the Council of Entities immediately begins pondering how to keep Nexus' enemies and allies alike from immediately trying to seize control.<br /> <br /> This not the end of the story. It is the beginning.<br /> <br /> Four newcomers emerge, and each is hailed as The Emissary's successor. One is a powerful ghost, which appears in tatters of The Emissary's robes, with half its mask intact and the other shattered to reveal a grinning skull - it dispenses harsh justice, and says that from now on it shall rule for itself, rather than the Council or Guild. One is a silent figure - thin and wearing very different mask and clothing, it nonetheless behaves much as the Emissary might have, but its methods are different, and it never speaks. The third is a young boy: he claims that he, the Emissary, was a powerful Spirit, and he has reformed in his Sanctum after his &quot;death&quot; - his power is prodigious, but his attitudes very different from The Emissary, and more than once he has had public arguments with the Council. The last is a very different puzzle - a mortal Artificer (in truth, a Twilight) who makes no claims to be related to The Emissary, but to whom many flock as Nexus' new protector, as his artifice gives him power, and he is certainly much more stable and reliable than any of the other options.<br /> <br /> (Spoilers: the ghost ultimately snaps and levels Great Forks, the boy nearly dies trying to stop it, the Twilight succeeds in finding the real original Emissary and returns alongside it, and the silent one sort of disappears without a trace.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T15:59:07-08:00","id":81284,"title":"","content":"The first paragraph and the words &quot;four newcomers&quot; were enough this time. <i>The Death and Return of Superman</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, consider that I am <i>not</i> a comics person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T16:28:58-08:00","id":81307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81284#post81284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first paragraph and the words &quot;four newcomers&quot; were enough this time. <i>The Death and Return of Superman</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, consider that I am <i>not</i> a comics person.</div> </div> </div> </div>But when I try making them hard, I have to wait weeks for the satisfaction of making up another! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> In a remote corner of Creation, a curious festival has emerged, which is known to few, welcomed by fewer, and might just manage to destroy all of Creation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should explain.<br /> <br /> On Calibration, once every few decades, the leylines will converge such that (without The Loom to deem it impossible) it becomes a fact that the Eye of Autochon exists, Insubstantial, somewhere in the town. Hidden by Calibration and the Eye's own treacherous nature, this is known only to a handful of esoteric necromancers across Creation, and the Sidereals. But the Sidereals dare not intervene, due to a prophecy, so each time the festival occurs, the necromancers gather - a handful from long-standing families, a representative from the Raiton Academy, a few wild cards and drifters. To access the Insubstantial Eye, each one summons the most powerful First Age ghost they can, who is then granted access to the Charms and Artifacts they wielded in life by the power of the Eye suffusing the area (though by that same token, calling any additional ghosts in the region becomes exceedingly difficult).<br /> <br /> That night is upon us. Prepare for the war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T16:38:15-08:00","id":81310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81307#post81307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when I try making them hard, I have to wait weeks for the satisfaction of making up another! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> In a remote corner of Creation, a curious festival has emerged, which is known to few, welcomed by fewer, and might just manage to destroy all of Creation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should explain.<br /> <br /> On Calibration, once every few decades, the leylines will converge such that (without The Loom to deem it impossible) it becomes a fact that the Eye of Autochon exists, Insubstantial, somewhere in the town. Hidden by Calibration and the Eye's own treacherous nature, this is known only to a handful of esoteric necromancers across Creation, and the Sidereals. But the Sidereals dare not intervene, due to a prophecy, so each time the festival occurs, the necromancers gather - a handful from long-standing families, a representative from the Raiton Academy, a few wild cards and drifters. To access the Insubstantial Eye, each one summons the most powerful First Age ghost they can, who is then granted access to the Charms and Artifacts they wielded in life by the power of the Eye suffusing the area (though by that same token, calling any additional ghosts in the region becomes exceedingly difficult).<br /> <br /> That night is upon us. Prepare for the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe that's Type-Moon's Fate series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T16:59:55-08:00","id":81325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81307#post81307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when I try making them hard, I have to wait weeks for the satisfaction of making up another! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Just do what I did an leave the post alone in it's obscurity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T22:00:33-08:00","id":81421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81310#post81310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do believe that's Type-Moon's Fate series.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right-o. Don't ask me about how Tsukihime figures in when Servants are already undead, though...<br /> <br /> <br /> Among the Forest Witches, there is a single man, the Signaler Of The Path, who has never entered their dreaming lake. He lives alone in the forest of mist, though he often travels abroad. Whether at home or in the wider East, his mission is to gather information on the forests of Creation to relay back to his fellows, who see only fantasies, that they might be informed. And yet, he must still labor under the strange curses of his fellows, for wherever he goes, he will inevitably find the same thing:<br /> <br /> A man, with a beard, who seeks to bring ruin to those things the Signaler must chronicle. And this man will, in due time, be beaten into submission by the Signaler's flawless kung fu.<br /> <br /> This is so inexorably consistent, the Signaler might wonder if he were not in the dreaming lake after all, save that his mortal wife and adoptive son assure him it is not so. Mortals, after all, could not survive that lake's reality, and are they not real?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T23:04:06-08:00","id":81436,"title":"","content":"This is not the Creation we know. Oh, the past is much like it, but in this Creation all of the Exalted were bound within the Jade Prison for their madness, not only the Solars. The world that was built without them was lesser, but it managed to survive - until the Prison was shattered, releasing the shards to the world. <br /> <br /> But these shards still bear the madness of their forbears. <br /> <br /> Now, these Chosen, beings of greater or lesser power but all beyond the reach of mortal men, rule madly and squabble over a Creation which has no strength to check them. In Nexus, now a city of neverending night ruled by a despotic Dusk Caste named The God-Emperor Who Surveys All And Weighs Them In A Heart Of Iron and his small cabal of exalted helpers, a savant who has made special study of the Chosen and their weaknesses seeks to join the resistance, wishing to destroy Heart of Iron. But can all of the Savant's new friends be trusted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T00:42:59-08:00","id":81456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81436#post81436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not the Creation we know. Oh, the past is much like it, but in this Creation all of the Exalted were bound within the Jade Prison for their madness, not only the Solars. The world that was built without them was lesser, but it managed to survive - until the Prison was shattered, releasing the shards to the world.<br /> <br /> But these shards still bear the madness of their forbears.<br /> <br /> Now, these Chosen, beings of greater or lesser power but all beyond the reach of mortal men, rule madly and squabble over a Creation which has no strength to check them. In Nexus, now a city of neverending night ruled by a despotic Dusk Caste named The God-Emperor Who Surveys All And Weighs Them In A Heart Of Iron and his small cabal of exalted helpers, a savant who has made special study of the Chosen and their weaknesses seeks to join the resistance, wishing to destroy Heart of Iron. But can all of the Savant's new friends be trusted?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't actually read it (yet), but... is that Steelheart, from Brandon Sanderson?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:20:47-08:00","id":81528,"title":"","content":"Yes. Yes it is!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T09:40:22-08:00","id":86816,"title":"","content":"Do you see? <b><i>Do you see?!</i> </b> I make one that's hard to guess, and <i>the thread dies</i>.<br /> <br /> Just sayin'.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the later days of the High First Age, society falls to corruption and apathy. One determined Eclipse seeks to make an amusement to rouse the passions of even his most jaded peers - an island populated by Third Circle Demons, so that Exalts can relive the glory of the Primordial War!<br /> <br /> He and his allies traverse the deep Wyld, finding pockets of reality which broke off of Creation during the Three Spheres Cataclysm and where no time has passed since. There, they find the Primordial Essence needed for their project, and it all goes much better than you'd expect, mostly due to the Eclipse's Lunar Mate, an actual Primordial War survivor. In time, the pseudo-Third Circle Souls are constructed, and the battlefield prepared.<br /> <br /> With mere weeks to go before the Calibration Banquet at which he intends to unveil his grand project, he brings a group of other Exalts, all reincarnations of famous Primordial War heroes, to look upon his work - a Twilight archivist of Primordial lore, his Lunar mate, and a Sidereal adviser.<br /> <br /> All of them barely have time to gain Limit from the sheer insanity of this project before a Wood Aspect servant, secretly in the employ of Bright Ice Shadow, flees with the soulcores of several Third Circles... and accidentally unleashes all of the others in his haste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T14:59:46-08:00","id":87025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=86816#post86816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you see? <b><i>Do you see?!</i> </b> I make one that's hard to guess, and <i>the thread dies</i>.<br /> <br /> Just sayin'.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the later days of the High First Age, society falls to corruption and apathy. One determined Eclipse seeks to make an amusement to rouse the passions of even his most jaded peers - an island populated by Third Circle Demons, so that Exalts can relive the glory of the Primordial War!<br /> <br /> He and his allies traverse the deep Wyld, finding pockets of reality which broke off of Creation during the Three Spheres Cataclysm and where no time has passed since. There, they find the Primordial Essence needed for their project, and it all goes much better than you'd expect, mostly due to the Eclipse's Lunar Mate, an actual Primordial War survivor. In time, the pseudo-Third Circle Souls are constructed, and the battlefield prepared.<br /> <br /> With mere weeks to go before the Calibration Banquet at which he intends to unveil his grand project, he brings a group of other Exalts, all reincarnations of famous Primordial War heroes, to look upon his work - a Twilight archivist of Primordial lore, his Lunar mate, and a Sidereal adviser.<br /> <br /> All of them barely have time to gain Limit from the sheer insanity of this project before a Wood Aspect servant, secretly in the employ of Bright Ice Shadow, flees with the soulcores of several Third Circles... and accidentally unleashes all of the others in his haste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about your other one, but this one's Jurassic Park.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:37:31-08:00","id":87073,"title":"","content":"And thus, the benefits of guessability are revealed.<br /> <br /> And who doesn't want Sidereals to say &quot;boy do I hate being right all the time.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> A Patrician girl of minor station lives resenting her infant half-brother, who has better Breeding and thus odds of Exaltation. Yet when this jealousy results in her striking a foolish bargain with the Raksha, she ventures forth herself into the Freehold of a seductive Fair Folk Noble to save her brother, and conquer her dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T17:13:15-08:00","id":87094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=81421#post81421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right-o. Don't ask me about how Tsukihime figures in when Servants are already undead, though...</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically nothing important in Tsukihime is undead. I mean, there's the vampire mooks, and Satsuki, and <i>maybe</i> Near Side Roa, but the rest are very much alive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=87073#post87073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And thus, the benefits of guessability are revealed.<br /> <br /> And who doesn't want Sidereals to say &quot;boy do I hate being right all the time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but is it unguessable because you obscured it, or because it's <i>obscure</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T17:35:49-08:00","id":87103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=87073#post87073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Patrician girl of minor station lives resenting her infant half-brother, who has better Breeding and thus odds of Exaltation. Yet when this jealousy results in her striking a foolish bargain with the Raksha, she ventures forth herself into the Freehold of a seductive Fair Folk Noble to save her brother, and conquer her dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess would be Labyrinth. A movie which I have never seen.<br /> <br /> Which would make it the third one I get without reading/watching/playing it. ...Actually, I don't think I HAVE been able to guess something I actually knew first-hand (not without someone else having been faster than me, at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:23:54-08:00","id":87123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=87073#post87073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Patrician girl of minor station lives resenting her infant half-brother, who has better Breeding and thus odds of Exaltation. Yet when this jealousy results in her striking a foolish bargain with the Raksha, she ventures forth herself into the Freehold of a seductive Fair Folk Noble to save her brother, and conquer her dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pan's Labyrinth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:29:37-08:00","id":87127,"title":"","content":"Right you are, Kazorh - but there's no time to bask in the glow of victory. There is a hole in your life, you poor deprived soul. Make haste - find and watch Labyrinth before it's too late!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=87094#post87094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, but is it unguessable because you obscured it, or because it's <i>obscure</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would posit that more people than not in this thread have at least seen it. It is, as one might say, hardly news, and is front of us every day.<br /> <br /> But why dwell on the unpleasant? I enjoy my silly sendups, else I'd not post them. And others enjoy seeing through them, else they'd not post that. I really don't see any problem with this arrangement.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Deathknight known as the Jester On The Wings Of Night has gone rogue. Stealing one of the most potent Artifacts of his master - and, indeed, of all the Underworld - he makes his way to Lookshy, where he simply drops it. The Jester did not rebel out of moral outrage, or even a desire for personal freedom, for he believes in neither. Rather, he is profoundly bored, and wants to see what a resident of Creation would do with the greatest powers of death.<br /> <br /> The one to find it is a young Air Aspect - Amilar Yu-Ming. A child of privilege, Yu-Ming realizes that he now holds the power to slay almost anyone in Creation, so long as he has seen them, and rather than being horrified or running amok as the Jester might have expected, seeks to end the sinful ways of the River Province (and eventually, the world) with tactically considered murder.<br /> <br /> His initial forays are wildly successful, but hit their first snag when a mysterious figure - an anonymous agent of justice claimed variously to be a God, an Anathema, or a rogue Realm Magistrate, comes to hunt him down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:41:08-08:00","id":87137,"title":"","content":"DID I ever finish Death Note? I don't think so... Well, I've at least seen it partially, this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:48:46-08:00","id":87141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=87137#post87137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DID I ever finish Death Note? I don't think so... Well, I've at least seen it partially, this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not Chejop Kejak, but have this prize!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HxDJIpwHAPc\" data-code=\"HxDJIpwHAPc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HxDJIpwHAPc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T15:49:40-07:00","id":88471,"title":"","content":"The Princess Magnificent has gained her freedom from the First and Forsaken Lion, and has begun her own conquest of Creation. A Sidereal sage prophesies that a baby girl, born with within the Princess' domain, and bearing the sign of Saturn upon her brow will be the final doom of the Deathlord. Fearful of the Sidereal's prophetic powers, the Princess orders that all pregnant women be housed within her dungeons, until they give birth and their children can be examined. When the prophesied child is born, the desperate midwife smuggles the infant from the citadel, sending it downriver before being slain. The child ends up in the hands of an aspiring djala sorcerer, who tries to find the child a home among her own kind. Shenanigans ensue as the djala encounters a half-mad Dawn-caste Solar, encounters some Fae, and battles with the Princess's Dusk-caste General and Moonshadow-caste daughter. In the end, the Princess captures the infant and begins a Necromantic ritual to cast the child, body and soul, into Oblivion. The djala's slight-of-hand tricks cause the ritual to back-fire, destroying the Princess forever. <br /> <br /> And proving that all Sidereals forever are manipulative trolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T19:05:14-07:00","id":88565,"title":"","content":"I love Willow.<br /> <br /> So much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T21:06:00-07:00","id":88620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=88565#post88565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Willow.<br /> <br /> So much.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a pretty good movie. Really schlocky, but good. Anyways...<br /> <br /> A new age of peace and prosperity has settled upon the Blessed Isle. The handful of Terrestrial Exalts on the Isle organize themselves into an &quot;Exalted Guild&quot;, whereupon the mortal populace can make requests for the Exalts to fulfill. Motivated by a Reputation system wherein ranking is based off of how favorably the populace views you, the Terrestrials all work to prove that they are the most altruistic, virtuous and noble soul of them all.<br /> <br /> Alas, it is not to last. A young boy Exalts when bandits attack and destroy his hometown. Rescued by a high ranking Guild member, the Exalt is trained to use his powers, before he is let loose on the trail of those who destroyed his home. Turns out the bandit leader was once in the Guild and has his older sister (who is now a Sidereal), and she points the Exalt to a plot for some jerk called &quot;The Onyx Dragon&quot; to get this immensely powerful Infernal Daiklaive that was once his, but was stolen from him by someone named 'Scarlet' of whom the Exalt is a direct descendant (through his mother, who is also an Exalt, and is also inexplicably alive). Only one of his bloodline can release the Sword, so the &quot;Onyx Dragon&quot; cuts hismom's throat above the sword, getting it back. The Exalt beats him up and seals him in another dimension (which is apparently where he was from to begin with), and may or may not have kept the sword.<br /> <br /> But he totally didn't, because keeping it means that he would have had to kill his sister, who may have been the evil mastermind behind the plot of the sequel (which takes place an undisclosed number of centuries in the future, when the blood of the Dragons has been watered down a TON), and but proved that she was actually just a person with sufficient foresight and willing to make the hard choices for the good of the world in the next sequel. So, she's a pretty generic Sidereal. Also, that desiccated mummy-lady that lead the Exalt to the North after the Dragon was killed? Yeah, that's totally Scarlet. Yup. Calling it. Totally Scarlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T21:31:28-07:00","id":88634,"title":"","content":"Is this...Fables? The original one first, and then the sequels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T10:57:13-07:00","id":88936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=88634#post88634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this...Fables? The original one first, and then the sequels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it is!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T11:16:18-07:00","id":89594,"title":"","content":"In the First Age, there was a great Twilight sorcerer-king who ruled a mighty nation with the help of a council of twelve other Exalts. After his death, the Council tracked his next incarnation to a young girl. The new Exalt had no experience in statecraft, and so the Council ruled as a regency while she grew up. The Council, however, proved to be corrupt, grievously misruling their subjects in their sorcerer-queen's name. The queen herself came to believe that the solution to her problems lay in Sorcery, and so, while the Council grew decadent, she labored on a sorcerous working of terrible power. After many years, her craft was completed, and she unleashed it on her kingdom.<br /> <br /> Tragically, her spell was fundamentally flawed: Her kingdom was torn from the fabric of Creation and plunged into the Labyrinth. The queen could only watch in dismay as the necrotic energies of that place twisted her subjects into horrible monsters and drove them to kill each other. Not even the Council could stand against such horrors, and soon the Twilight was left to wander her former kingdom alone. This strange portion of the Neverborn's dreams proved an apt reflection of the Void, for once the monsters that had been her subjects died, no new creatures came to replace them. All that was left was silence and emptiness, and, with no track of time, the queen did not even notice when she died. She lingered as a ghost, mourning her lost kingdom and regretting her foolish hubris, until she finally succumbed to the whispers of the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> In the Time of Tumult, there was a noted Patrician thaumaturge of good Breeding who had recently joined the Wyld Hunt. Though he had never Exalted himself, his distinguished lineage still gave him some degree of influence. His unit was given a village where a Lunar Anathema was predicted to arise and ordered to prevent its birth by any means necessary. The Patrician's commander, knowing the cunning deceptions the Lunars were capable of, ordered the village burned and all its inhabitants put to the sword. The Patrician was a good Immaculate, but he could not bring himself to do it. While the Hunt carried out its massacre, he managed to smuggle a single young girl to safety. It was she, he later learned, who had been destined to become Anathema.<br /> <br /> The Patrician's actions brought inconceivable dishonor to his family. He was dragged back to the Blessed Isle in chains and forced to watch his House disown him and his immediate family suffer for his transgression. With a combination of luck and desperation, he managed to escape immediate execution, but he could not escape his own knowledge of what he'd done. Finally, the shame became too much to bear, and he resolved to end it all. Yet as the murky waters filled his lungs, he heard the voice of a woman long dead. She, too, had seen disaster spring from the best of intentions. She, too, knew how cruel the world could be. Together, they would rise up and smash the petty, rotted Creation that had perverted their goals. And so the Patrician became Exalted after all.<br /> <br /> In the present day, the world lives in fear of a great Abyssal necromancer. All who dare to oppose him have their souls mutilated by his death-magics, reduced to pitiful mockeries of human beings. Yet there are still places free of the necromancer's touch: Small pockets of reality that, even after an entire Age, survive in the ocean of the Wyld. From one of these pockets, a boy emerges. Guided by a Raksha companion, he crosses the Wyld and enters Creation proper. He wields great magics, and in his soul he bears a special Exaltation: That of the necromancer's Lunar mate! He has the power to undo the Abyssal's magics, and he believes that defeating the necromancer is the key to saving his mother's soul. As the Deathlord exerts increasing pressure on her pawn, the world moves closer to a mighty confrontation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T18:11:06-07:00","id":89859,"title":"","content":"Ni no Kuni?<br /> <br /> That sounds like a rad backstory, especially as I could not begin to place it until the last sentences of the last paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T22:07:45-07:00","id":89941,"title":"","content":"Sleek Lone Pi is the assistant director for ecology of a small kingdom. She is an active, type-A personality who looks up to the powerful female leaders in the Deliberative. Her boss is a staid Twilight known for both a disregard of civic duties and a keen hand at crafting. Sleek assembles a group of friends to work in the ecology department, including her best friend, a Water DB healer; a hirsute slacker Lunar with a talent for music; an entrepreneurial Night caste; and a morose Abyssal. Together they repel attacks from demonic raccoons and try to beautify the kingdom. However, the kingdom\u2019s finances have not been managed well, and soon the Deliberative sends two Eclipses to oversee the running of the kingdom. The elder Eclipse is friendly and cheerful to fault as he always delivers bad news with a big, shit-eating grin. The younger Eclipse is quiet and has a penchant for the arcane. The elder Eclipse has an on again, off again relationship with the DB, and the younger Eclipse falls in love with Sleek Lone Pi. Eventually, the junior Eclipse is appointed chancellor of the kingdom. Sleek Lone Pi herself tries her hand at the governing council, but is chased off by an angry mob when she engineers the conquest of a nearby kingdom. She returns to her role as assistant director and lives happily ever after with the young Eclipse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":1338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","user":"BvBPL","date":". 03-13-2014, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T08:59:03-07:00","id":90255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=89859#post89859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ni no Kuni?<br /> <br /> That sounds like a rad backstory, especially as I could not begin to place it until the last sentences of the last paragraph.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it in one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T18:08:12-07:00","id":90530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=90255#post90255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got it in one!</div> </div> </div> </div>Never played the game, but I recently read someone's thoughts about the White Witch and this deathlord kind of guy in its plot.<br /> <br /> I'm curious regarding the hero and what features define him as a Lunar in your eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T19:10:44-07:00","id":90561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=89941#post89941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleek Lone Pi is the assistant director for ecology of a small kingdom. She is an active, type-A personality who looks up to the powerful female leaders in the Deliberative. Her boss is a staid Twilight known for both a disregard of civic duties and a keen hand at crafting. Sleek assembles a group of friends to work in the ecology department, including her best friend, a Water DB healer; a hirsute slacker Lunar with a talent for music; an entrepreneurial Night caste; and a morose Abyssal. Together they repel attacks from demonic raccoons and try to beautify the kingdom. However, the kingdom\u2019s finances have not been managed well, and soon the Deliberative sends two Eclipses to oversee the running of the kingdom. The elder Eclipse is friendly and cheerful to fault as he always delivers bad news with a big, shit-eating grin. The younger Eclipse is quiet and has a penchant for the arcane. The elder Eclipse has an on again, off again relationship with the DB, and the younger Eclipse falls in love with Sleek Lone Pi. Eventually, the junior Eclipse is appointed chancellor of the kingdom. Sleek Lone Pi herself tries her hand at the governing council, but is chased off by an angry mob when she engineers the conquest of a nearby kingdom. She returns to her role as assistant director and lives happily ever after with the young Eclipse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sweet jegus I'm actually getting one of these! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ... man i dont like these emoticons<br /> <br /> Excellent analoguing of Parks and Recreation. I didn't quite pick up on it until The Manager of the Impassioned Grin came into it, but it all works so well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T19:31:57-07:00","id":90579,"title":"","content":"In one! Congrats.<br /> <br /> here's another:<br /> <br /> <br /> Three Fair Folk noblewomen need to travel from their home in one area of the Wyld across Creation to another area of the Wyld to attend the ordination of the Fair Folk queen. The trip is dangerous because the Fair Folk aren't necessarily welcome in Creation. Along the way, they are harried by an inept, but dogged, celestial censor who is distrustful of the Fair Folk. After such an encounter, the noblewomen take refuge in a small mortal community. This township isn't a particularly nice place; the women are downtrodden and joyless and the men are largely thuggish goons. One woman puts the noblewomen up in her boarding house. <br /> <br /> As they recover, the Fair Folk engage with the community and bring life and color back to the women. They even cure one mute woman and help their landlady get out of an abusive relationship. Thanks to the guidance of the Fair Folk the women of the town find and assert their independence. Then the Fair Folk, along with the women work to civilize the men of the town, who go from uncouth toughs to gentlemen. The townfolk and the Fair Folk work together to brighten up the town and put an exciting and colorful harvest festival.<br /> <br /> The climax comes as the celestial censor shows up to town at the height of the festival looking for the Fair Folk. The Fair Folk, in their weakened state, are no match for the censor and are ready to give themselves up. However, the people of the town stand beside the Fair Folk and together they chase out the censor.<br /> <br /> The noblewomen make it to the election of the Fair Folk queen. The denouement comes as the youngest of the noblewomen is elected Queen of the Fair Folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T20:47:31-07:00","id":90611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BvBPL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=90579#post90579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one! Congrats.<br /> <br /> here's another:<br /> <br /> <br /> Three Fair Folk noblewomen need to travel from their home in one area of the Wyld across Creation to another area of the Wyld to attend the ordination of the Fair Folk queen. The trip is dangerous because the Fair Folk aren't necessarily welcome in Creation. Along the way, they are harried by an inept, but dogged, celestial censor who is distrustful of the Fair Folk. After such an encounter, the noblewomen take refuge in a small mortal community. This township isn't a particularly nice place; the women are downtrodden and joyless and the men are largely thuggish goons. One woman puts the noblewomen up in her boarding house.<br /> <br /> As they recover, the Fair Folk engage with the community and bring life and color back to the women. They even cure one mute woman and help their landlady get out of an abusive relationship. Thanks to the guidance of the Fair Folk the women of the town find and assert their independence. Then the Fair Folk, along with the women work to civilize the men of the town, who go from uncouth toughs to gentlemen. The townfolk and the Fair Folk work together to brighten up the town and put an exciting and colorful harvest festival.<br /> <br /> The climax comes as the celestial censor shows up to town at the height of the festival looking for the Fair Folk. The Fair Folk, in their weakened state, are no match for the censor and are ready to give themselves up. However, the people of the town stand beside the Fair Folk and together they chase out the censor.<br /> <br /> The noblewomen make it to the election of the Fair Folk queen. The denouement comes as the youngest of the noblewomen is elected Queen of the Fair Folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>To Wong Fu, thanks for everything, Julie Newmar.<br /> <br /> I love that movie!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T20:56:57-07:00","id":90615,"title":"","content":"Way to go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T09:11:08-07:00","id":90936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=90530#post90530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious regarding the hero and what features define him as a Lunar in your eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really answer that without MEGA NI NO KUNI SPOILERS:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First off, he comes from another world with a fairy companion. That nicely translates to having him slip through the Wyld at some point, which is more a Lunar thing.<br /> <br /> Secondly, Lunar Exaltation fit best with Alicia's backstory: She manages to survive quite a bit before coming in to her power. Oliver is her legacy, and he gets his powers after her death, so it makes sense that Exalted-Oliver would inherit her Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Lastly... 'cause Shadar is his Sol(ar) Mate! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T00:54:42-07:00","id":91467,"title":"","content":"There is a secret, hidden from all the world. Exaltations are not of the sun, or moon, or stars, or this base earth. They are of the void beyond. Each exaltation is the shard of a mighty cosmic being, one of the great Entities that transcend the borders of worlds gifted to mortals not out of benevolence, but in order that the Entity may feed on their experiences, and grow rich in understanding and insight. And then, when the day comes, the shards will be recalled, and the Entity will resume it's travels in the cosmic void, leaving behind a world sundered by it's greed.<br /> <br /> But something has gone wrong with this cycle... Perhaps, this Creation is not doomed.<br /> <br /> (yeah, that was terrible. I will go and try to dig up a better one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T12:48:42-07:00","id":92409,"title":"","content":"The son of a great king exalted as a Zenith Caste, and was placed into a circle with a Twilight caste and a much older Zenith caste. His kingdom came under assault from the forces of the Underworld - the dead and damned walked the world, destroying and ravaging towns and villages. Perhaps worst of all, the people were turned into undead through powerful enchantments. As the fight pressed on, the horrors began to break the prince's sanity. When he ordered a city purged before they could rise as undead, his circle refused to follow. He destroyed the city and attacked the Daybreak caste that had masterminded most of the horrors, though the Daybreak managed to escape. He chased the monster to the underworld with a vast army, and the army he brought perished to a man. He struck down the Daybreak, but was captured and converted to an Abyssal. He would return one day, and slay his father and old mentor. As for the old Twilight caste, she would sail to the blessed isle, make contact with the Realm and attempt to enlist their aid in combatting the Neverborn and Infernal invasions.<br /> <br /> ... Well that was awful &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T13:25:01-07:00","id":92438,"title":"","content":"WarCraft III.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T13:35:41-07:00","id":92442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=92438#post92438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WarCraft III.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Not particularly hard, if you've played the human campaign through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T15:03:27-07:00","id":92483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satori</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=91467#post91467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a secret, hidden from all the world. Exaltations are not of the sun, or moon, or stars, or this base earth. They are of the void beyond. Each exaltation is the shard of a mighty cosmic being, one of the great Entities that transcend the borders of worlds gifted to mortals not out of benevolence, but in order that the Entity may feed on their experiences, and grow rich in understanding and insight. And then, when the day comes, the shards will be recalled, and the Entity will resume it's travels in the cosmic void, leaving behind a world sundered by it's greed.<br /> <br /> But something has gone wrong with this cycle... Perhaps, this Creation is not doomed.<br /> <br /> (yeah, that was terrible. I will go and try to dig up a better one.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted flavored Worm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T16:07:21-07:00","id":92519,"title":"","content":"In this version of the universe, there are magical gemstones, each aligned with a particular Attribute, and each containing a particular Charm or spell, that can be used by any Essence-user who sockets it into an item they wield. These gems are so ubiquitous and so useful that many Exalted never bother to develop non-Permanent native Charms. However, they are not merely tools to be picked up and used, but hide a mysterious, corrupting, dangerous power. A few centuries ago, the Realm used these gems in a mighty Working to drive back a force of invading Barbarians led by a potent Dawn caste, and allied with an internal, Zenith-led rebellion. The ritual defeated the invaders... and also turned the Blessed Isle into a haunted wasteland. Now, the largest remaining human civilization is a former backwater colony off the Realm's coast.<br /> <br /> That small island is now ruled by a harsh, oppressive theocracy, headed by The Black Templar of Dominance Unbroken, a Midnight caste who is obsessed with the hidden powers of the gems. He uses the former Blessed Isle as a penal colony, feeding those guilty of all crimes great and small into the mouths of its endless hordes of monsters, in the hopes that one will become strong enough, and uncover enough of its secrets, to lead him to the ultimate power he seeks.<br /> <br /> Most of his Exiles die, or huddle on the coast or the ruins of the Imperial City in fear, or become little better than beasts themselves. But now, seven of them show the potential to become what the Black Templar needs. A savage Dusk, descended by blood from the barbarian leader as well as bearing his Shard. A Changing Moon mistress of the bow. A Daybreak girl who seeks out Sorcery and Necromancy even more greedily than himself. Another Dawn, who cares for nothing but the glory of battle and accolades of a bloodthirsty crowd. An aging Zenith, determined to reform the religion that the Black Templar has corrupted. A Night caste assassin, annoyed that his employers betrayed him, but eager to ply his trade in this savage land. And finally, an Eclipse noblewoman, whose talents seem to know no bounds, but is troubled by her seeming affinity for the Isle's corrupted Essence.<br /> <br /> The Black Templar of Dominance Eternal is sure that one of them will be his perfect vessel. He has already traveled to the Imperial Manse, and is using its Dragon Lines to drain the life from the entire Isle, and twist the remaining humans upon it into horrible monsters. When one of the Seven Exiles reaches him, he will congratulate them, on becoming the perfect sacrificial vessel to grant him the ascension he craves. And then, he will slay them, and and become something that surpasses the Primordials and Incarnae themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T16:20:58-07:00","id":92527,"title":"","content":"Path of Exile, a pretty neat Free To Play(that involves no pay to Win). Pretty difficult, too.<br /> <br /> Pity the story isn't relayed to the audience that well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T17:27:45-07:00","id":92552,"title":"","content":"Got it in one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T03:28:31-07:00","id":93348,"title":"","content":"I heart this thread, guys. Great work.<br /> I'll try one.<br /> -<br /> A young girl goes mad with grief after her family is killed by bandits, and leaves her village to run with a pack of wolves. It is then that Luna exalts her, bringing her back to sanity. But the girl's feral nature is not so easily cured; her time without tattoos has made her chimerae, and she risks insanity every time she touches her newfound power.<br /> Fearing this, the girl travels south, to a fair where she meets a kindly horse trader. The trader gives her a job, but soon becomes suspicious of her 'knack' for communicating with animals, and asks a colleague (a playful Chosen of Secrets who's on the run from a tyrannical Twilight emperor) to mentor her. Gradually, the Sidereal works with the Lunar to develop her power, teaching her to trust people.<br /> The book's climactic battle involves the emperor's navy laying siege to a Night Caste's fortress and summoning a greater elemental dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T15:34:47-07:00","id":93853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=92483#post92483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted flavored Worm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, yeah, but it was still terrible. have revalid's version: <br /> <br /> Clearly, what happened is that Ramethus never returned to Creation. Instead, he fled into the space between realities to seek some way of defeating the hated usurpers. Eventually, in a move ironically taken straight from the playbook of He Who Forged Death, he settled on becoming an Exalt-Primordial-cyborg, modifying his spiritual structure into a legion of lobotomized, self-replicating pseudo-Exaltations. These get shed into whatever manvantara he is currently passing through, leaving his jouten on sleep mode a short distance away from that realm, and seek out suitable mortal hosts, roughly guided by his fetich, Xion the Warrior. Granting their hosts potent Essence-based powers, these shards leech off their xp, and eventually gain enough to bud off new shards, which seek out new hosts and so on. When the profit margins of that world are judged low enough, he kills off most of the reality with Adamant Circle Sorcery to retrieve any remaining shards, and moves on, bloated with new subsouls and the stolen experience of a thousand battles between his false Chosen. So successful has this strategy been throughout the years that he even managed to spawn a secondary Fetich, Yden the Strategist, albeit at the cost of his own motive. Guided to worlds devoid of threat by his left hand and guarded against those few that learn of him by his right, Ramethus - the Crusader Worm, the Garden of War, the Legion Without Frontier - is little more than a wandering idiotic god-blob, supping on the ambrosia of endless wars in endless realities, barely able to recall the vengeance he once sought.<br /> <br /> So should an Exaltation make its way, somehow, to a reality he was involved in, it would avoid uplifting the false-Exalted that surround it, and instead seek a mortal of its own, one yet to be seized by the symbiote-shards that flit, invisible, through the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/general-exalted-debate-third-edition-actually-2nd.263244/page-84#post-13046538\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.spacebattles.com/data/svg/12/1/1794175159/sb_2022_favicon_192x192.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/general-exalted-debate-third-edition-actually-2nd.263244/page-84#post-13046538\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Debate, Third Edition(Actually 2nd) </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/general-exalted-debate-third-edition-actually-2nd.263244/page-84#post-13046538\" target=\"_blank\"> http://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/general-exalted-debate-third-edition-actually-2nd.263244/page-84#post-13046538 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Probably, yes. In the context of a crossover, it seems like the type of thing that'd get replaced. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Much better, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2438-satori","name":"Satori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T19:04:12-07:00","id":94009,"title":"","content":"The Exalted have long been nothing more than a memory, but that does not mean the supernatural has left the Earth. Powerful Hungry Ghosts stalk humanity, with cunning Hekatonkhire above them. Nothing mortal made can defeat them, and few humans can even see them. But Humanity is not along, as the Spirits watch over humanity, wielding powerful evocations and mighty spells, seeking to send the ghosts back to lethe, a neverending battle.<br /> <br /> One young spirit, heir to a powerful Bureau Head, is on a mission in the mortal world, where she is wounded, only saved by the first Solar Exaltation in millenia. But while the youth has so much promise, he needs time to grow, to find the power his evocations grant him, and something is rotten in the Spirit courts. Will the Teen be able to find his power before the Courts move to crush him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T22:08:09-07:00","id":94103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=94009#post94009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exalted have long been nothing more than a memory, but that does not mean the supernatural has left the Earth. Powerful Hungry Ghosts stalk humanity, with cunning Hekatonkhire above them. Nothing mortal made can defeat them, and few humans can even see them. But Humanity is not along, as the Spirits watch over humanity, wielding powerful evocations and mighty spells, seeking to send the ghosts back to lethe, a neverending battle.<br /> <br /> One young spirit, heir to a powerful Bureau Head, is on a mission in the mortal world, where she is wounded, only saved by the first Solar Exaltation in millenia. But while the youth has so much promise, he needs time to grow, to find the power his evocations grant him, and something is rotten in the Spirit courts. Will the Teen be able to find his power before the Courts move to crush him?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's been a Bleach in the thread already. Though I like you making the shinigami spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T23:05:43-07:00","id":103201,"title":"","content":"An up and coming Midnight Caste leads a raid upon the Northern barbarian tribes, slaughtering most of them and selling their children into slavery. Among these slaves is a young boy who sees his parents killed by said Midnight Caste before he is sold to work in a jade mine. Growing of age in these mines, the boy is bought by a Guild lord traveling to the East. There the child of the barbarian tribes is forced to fight in pit battles, eventually accumulating countless wins and becoming a champion in the City of Nexus, where he also trains with master swordsmen and learns to read and write. The pit fighter eventually escapes in a slave revolt, running as far from Nexus as he could, his masters in hot pursuit. He hides in a cave which turns out to be the tomb of a First Age solar. Taking the daiklaive from the skeleton of the Solar Warrior King, the pit fighter exalts as a Dawn Caste and slays the slavers who pursued him.<br /> <br /> Now free from a lifetime of slavery that tempered him into a powerful warrior and endowed with the power of a god-king, the Dawn Caste sets off to kill the Midnight Caste who slaughtered his people. Easier said than done, since the Abyssal is now the head of an enormous death worshiping cult that spans most of the Threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T23:50:55-07:00","id":103230,"title":"","content":"@dreamking89: Conan the Barbarian?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T19:55:43-07:00","id":104543,"title":"","content":"A Zenith empress is assassinated and her human bodyguard framed for it. On the day of his execution for treason, he Exalts as a Lunar and uses his newfound abilities to take revenge on her killers and save the crown princess (who is implied to be his own daughter) from those seeking to usurp her power. He is assisted in this by an underground faction of loyalists and the macabre stealth armor an eccentric Twilight crafted for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T20:28:03-07:00","id":104559,"title":"","content":"Damn! It's on the tip of my tongue...<br /> <br /> <br /> Dishonored!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T23:25:42-07:00","id":104641,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=104559#post104559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dishonored!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Devouring Swarm, anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T00:39:45-07:00","id":105429,"title":"","content":"The Blessed Isle is terrorized by a mysterious string of murders which leave the Wyld Hunt baffled. The only mark left on any of the victims is a strange insect only found naturally in the jungles of the Underworld. A young Sidereal apprentice (merely months from Exalting as a Sidereal herself) has been investigating the grisly murders with her superiors, but has been getting absolutely nowhere. Things get especially desperate when a daughter of Memnon is discovered to be missing, leading the apprentice to take drastic measures. <br /> <br /> The apprentice has begun seeking advice from the Five Score Fellowship's greatest and most dangerous asset: a frighteningly charming Daybreak Caste. Years ago, the Wyld Hunt captured the Abyssal alive after a string of his own murders and had him imprisoned in Yu-Shan rather than killing him outright. The apprentice and the Sidereals only have a matter of time before Memnon's daughter is murdered, but the Daybreak (with nothing to lose) continues to play mind games with them, taking a special interest in the young apprentice and her troubling past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T03:59:50-07:00","id":105478,"title":"","content":"That has to be ...<br /> <br /> The Silence of the Lambs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2551-lucil","name":"Lucil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:54:33-07:00","id":106428,"title":"","content":"A easy going Dawn who is a been disowned by the house of Cathak sets out west to claim the treasure and throne of a long dead solar godking. He joined in his journey by a fellow Dawn caste who desires to become the greatest swordsman in creation. A red headed half caste with the uncanny ability to navigate the seas. A tall tale telling cowardly heroic mortal archer. A chosen of culinary arts who seems to fall in love with every women he meets and hopes to find a legendary stretch of sea in the west where every fish in creation resides. A naive childlike deer totem Lunar who wishes to purge all disease form creation. A level headed Chosen of Secrets who is looking for a scroll that chronicles some unsavory details of the usurpation. A melodramatic Jade caste alchemical who strives to build the greatest ship to every sail the sea. A Liminal musician who's deemed his purpose in life is to meet Leviathan. In their travels they end up ruining a malfactor plan to conquer Lap. Imprison a tyrannical deranged greater elemental dragon in the silver chair. Foil a plot by the all seeing eye to take control of Ten Metal Shriek. All while staying one step ahead of the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1544-vectorfox","name":"VectorFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1544_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:48:51-07:00","id":106538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VectorFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=106428#post106428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A easy going Dawn who is a been disowned by the house of Cathak sets out west to claim the treasure and throne of a long dead solar godking. He joined in his journey by a fellow Dawn caste who desires to become the greatest swordsman in creation. A red headed half caste with the uncanny ability to navigate the seas.</div> </div> </div> </div>RED hair? My life was a lie. I thought it was orange because of the entire oranges motif o_O","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:55:58-07:00","id":106542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=106538#post106538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RED hair? My life was a lie. I thought it was orange because of the entire oranges motif o_O</div> </div> </div> </div>The English language is kind of flawed that way. Red hair is not actually red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:58:40-07:00","id":106546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=106542#post106542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The English language is kind of flawed that way. Red hair is not actually red.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except in Creation/anime, where red hair can actually be red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T18:05:04-07:00","id":106635,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, obviously. Though some languages offer the ability to call red hair <i>red</i>, and use another word to talk about the kinda-orangy hair color.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T08:56:21-07:00","id":108235,"title":"","content":"*starts writing a 40K-as-exalted*<br /> *stops*<br /> *erases*<br /> *starts again*<br /> *...stops again*<br /> <br /> ......<br /> <br /> ... Okay, here's one. Not 40k.<br /> <br /> Creation has shrunk to the size of a single region (let's say... a bit bigger than Rhode Island) From the Wyld, the Fae continue to push their advance. Only a small number of humans remain to hold back the tide, and they die in droves every day. The Dragon-blood has grown thin, but some still manage to Exalt. The Solars are gone entirely, and only a scant handful of Lunars remain. However, a few of the Lunar Exalted have found a way to turn into the Behemoths of old, and are doing what they can to hold the line.<br /> <br /> The fae are the prey, the lunars the hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:01:25-07:00","id":108710,"title":"","content":"...Attack on Titan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T21:23:58-07:00","id":110580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=108710#post108710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Attack on Titan?</div> </div> </div> </div>...*grumble* yes...<br /> <br /> I need to make these harder to guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T16:21:50-07:00","id":111815,"title":"","content":"In A World where Sidereals walk openly among the people and their armies battle the Fae for survival, the first Liminal Exalt rises. Though the Sidereals foresaw his awakening from the dead, they are surprised by one thing: he has no fate. Any attempts to see his future are futile.<br /> But this is the Liminal's greatest strength, for the Fae of this world are bound to fate and reincarnation. They believe it is the fate of Creation to die, to be swallowed under the entropy their winter army brings. They- and the Sidereals- believe humanity is doomed.<br /> With the help of a femme fatale Chosen of Endings, the Liminal proves them wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T19:06:50-07:00","id":111865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=111815#post111815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In A World where Sidereals walk openly among the people and their armies battle the Fae for survival, the first Liminal Exalt rises. Though the Sidereals foresaw his awakening from the dead, they are surprised by one thing: he has no fate. Any attempts to see his future are futile.<br /> But this is the Liminal's greatest strength, for the Fae of this world are bound to fate and reincarnation. They believe it is the fate of Creation to die, to be swallowed under the entropy their winter army brings. They- and the Sidereals- believe humanity is doomed.<br /> With the help of a femme fatale Chosen of Endings, the Liminal proves them wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <i>I, Frankenstein</i>, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T05:45:22-07:00","id":113274,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=111865#post111865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's <i>I, Frankenstein</i>, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking more along the lines of <i>Kingdoms of Amalur</i>, with the Fateweavers as Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T07:10:59-07:00","id":113301,"title":"","content":"As the Neverborn stir in their deathly slumber, horrible mists gather in the Underworld and seep from Shadowlands into Creation at night. Some who enter those mists end up forever trapped in a bleak dream world populated by all manners of horrors. Those who give in to the malice permeating the place get rewarded with great boons by the Neverborn, at the price of getting stuck in horrible passion plays where they're forever tormented by their past failures until no shred of joy remains in their hearts. Ultimately, each such individual ends up ruling his own domain within the dream world as a nigh-omnipotent being, waging wars against each other through proxies, for the mists don't allow them to leave their domains and do battle in person. The most notable of those twisted lords are the bitter count overseeing his feudal domain from a looming castle, a knight in soulsteel armor commanding vast armies of undead, and an emaciated, horribly maimed sorcerer constantly plotting his escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T07:19:04-07:00","id":113306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=113301#post113301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the Neverborn stir in their deathly slumber, horrible mists gather in the Underworld and seep from Shadowlands into Creation at night. Some who enter those mists end up forever trapped in a bleak dream world populated by all manners of horrors. Those who give in to the malice permeating the place get rewarded with great boons by the Neverborn, at the price of getting stuck in horrible passion plays where they're forever tormented by their past failures until no shred of joy remains in their hearts. Ultimately, each such individual ends up ruling his own domain within the dream world as a nigh-omnipotent being, waging wars against each other through proxies, for the mists don't allow them to leave their domains and do battle in person. The most notable of those twisted lords are the bitter count overseeing his feudal domain from a looming castle, a knight in soulsteel armor commanding vast armies of undead, and an emaciated, horribly maimed sorcerer constantly plotting his escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ravenloft?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T07:35:49-07:00","id":113315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=113306#post113306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ravenloft?</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be correct!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T01:06:51-07:00","id":113910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=113315#post113315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would be correct!</div> </div> </div> </div>Always loved that setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T21:39:41-07:00","id":115116,"title":"","content":"An apprentice thaumaturge, upon slaying a demon sent to assassinate him, Exalted as a Lunar. Now he works as a detective and unofficial protector of his city- a protector it sorely needs, being the battlefield of factions mortal, Exalted and fae. He rarely <i>means</i> to get caught up in all the magical shenanigans ensnaring the city, but somehow, trouble always seems to find him. He survives it with resilience, wit, and a motley collection of allies: a stern Dawn who works in law enforcement, an lustful spirit bound to a skull, an handsome Moonshadow trying to redeem himself, and a young Chosen of Serenity with a talent for disappearing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T21:48:01-07:00","id":115119,"title":"","content":"I wasn't totally sure until I got to Murphy and Bob, but that's totally the Dresden Files.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T03:07:12-07:00","id":115185,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=115119#post115119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't totally sure until I got to Murphy and Bob, but that's totally the Dresden Files.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. (I still remember the debate fans had on the old forum about which type and caste each DF character was. Good times.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T16:34:07-07:00","id":115588,"title":"","content":"In the universe of Heaven's Reach, in a fledgling empire comfortably beyond the reach of His Divine Lunar Presence, there once was a young naval officer. At the beginning of her career, she was idealistic, naive, dedicated, and far more talented than anyone except her closest teachers realized. Now, twenty years, several wars, multiple diplomatic missions, a list of titles as long as her arm, a husband and wife and son, and a Zenith Exaltation later, she is <i>still </i>idealistic and dedicated, has gained wisdom and maturity, and become one of the most feared military names in the explored galaxy. She has won numerous battles, and more than a few allies for her star nation, including an even larger, albeit less advanced, empire that was once their bitterest enemy.<br /> <br /> However, even all her skills and willpower may not be enough. For the might of the central empire now sets itself against these backwater upstarts who have dared deny its authority. And they are not even the true threat... behind this move lies a secret network of demonic spies, festering in the heart of the galaxy, slowly advancing a plot by the Yozis and their servants to remake humanity in their own image.<br /> <br /> But the transhumanists have made one mistake. They, like so many others before, have underestimated the honor of the Empire of the Sphynx.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T17:55:25-07:00","id":115618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=115588#post115588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the universe of Heaven's Reach, in a fledgling empire comfortably beyond the reach of His Divine Lunar Presence, there once was a young naval officer. At the beginning of her career, she was idealistic, naive, dedicated, and far more talented than anyone except her closest teachers realized. Now, twenty years, several wars, multiple diplomatic missions, a list of titles as long as her arm, a husband and wife and son, and a Zenith Exaltation later, she is <i>still </i>idealistic and dedicated, has gained wisdom and maturity, and become one of the most feared military names in the explored galaxy. She has won numerous battles, and more than a few allies for her star nation, including an even larger, albeit less advanced, empire that was once their bitterest enemy.<br /> <br /> However, even all her skills and willpower may not be enough. For the might of the central empire now sets itself against these backwater upstarts who have dared deny its authority. And they are not even the true threat... behind this move lies a secret network of demonic spies, festering in the heart of the galaxy, slowly advancing a plot by the Yozis and their servants to remake humanity in their own image.<br /> <br /> But the transhumanists have made one mistake. They, like so many others before, have underestimated the honor of the Empire of the Sphynx.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Horatio Hornblower in Space!</i><br /> <br /> Ahem. <br /> <br /> I mean David Weber's <i>Honor Harrington </i>Series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T18:35:18-07:00","id":115632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=115618#post115618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Horatio Hornblower in Space!</i><br /> <br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> I mean David Weber's <i>Honor Harrington </i>Series.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T21:40:43-07:00","id":115704,"title":"","content":"A brilliant, coldhearted Air Aspect (and his Earth Aspect bodyguard) holds one of the Fair Folk for ransom in hopes of gaining enough gold to reestablish his family fortune. A game of cat-and-mouse ensues, as the Fae in question- an ambitious, relatively young guard- and her military Court attempt to outwit his nefarious plots. Of course, both sides team up in future sequels.<br /> (The story would probably take place in the First Age, as it involves a lot of high-Essence artifacts and magically-enabled espionage.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T23:52:14-07:00","id":115737,"title":"","content":"*grin* Artemis Fowl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T19:09:02-07:00","id":116279,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=115737#post115737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*grin* Artemis Fowl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I'll try another.<br /> <br /> In the West there exists a small island town, home to fishermen and patricians' pleasure retreats. It's protected by three peasant girls- all Water Aspects- who keep their Exaltations secret for fear of being shipped off to the Blessed Isle.<br /> They don't know why Daana'd chose them, but it seems to have something to do with a moon-touched pool they bathed in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T19:40:52-07:00","id":116802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=93348#post93348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heart this thread, guys. Great work.<br /> I'll try one.<br /> -<br /> A young girl goes mad with grief after her family is killed by bandits, and leaves her village to run with a pack of wolves. It is then that Luna exalts her, bringing her back to sanity. But the girl's feral nature is not so easily cured; her time without tattoos has made her chimerae, and she risks insanity every time she touches her newfound power.<br /> Fearing this, the girl travels south, to a fair where she meets a kindly horse trader. The trader gives her a job, but soon becomes suspicious of her 'knack' for communicating with animals, and asks a colleague (a playful Chosen of Secrets who's on the run from a tyrannical Twilight emperor) to mentor her. Gradually, the Sidereal works with the Lunar to develop her power, teaching her to trust people.<br /> The book's climactic battle involves the emperor's navy laying siege to a Night Caste's fortress and summoning a greater elemental dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Wild Magic?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2777-doublelarry22","name":"doublelarry22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T04:54:24-07:00","id":116890,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>doublelarry22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=116802#post116802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Wild Magic?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Upon reading about Lunar Exalted for the first time, my first thought was literally; 'Okay, so- like Daine, but silver and glowy.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T20:09:54-07:00","id":117345,"title":"","content":"I just realized that the Star Brand from Marvel Comics is essentially Marvel's Exaltation or Exigent.<br /> <a href=\"http://marvel.wikia.com/Star_Brand\" target=\"_blank\">http://marvel.wikia.com/Star_Brand</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T22:25:13-07:00","id":117420,"title":"","content":"So my wife and I watched Short Peace tonight, and three of the stories map to some degree While I'm generally more a fan of &quot;Guess the story!&quot;, the multiple stories and relative obscurity and newness make this no fun at all. So let's be explicit:<br /> <br /> Possessions, the story of a man stuck in a shrine overnight with the unquiet spirits of discarded items, only to appease them with praise, attention, and repair, is right at home in Creation's animistic setting, although it ascribes a bit more power and awareness to the Least Gods.<br /> <br /> Ganbo is pretty much the tale of a Lunar Exalt defending a village against a wicked Erymanthos, briefly working alongside a Wyld Hunt to do it.<br /> <br /> And then there's Farewell to Weapons, which is a Scavenger Lord team investigating First Age ruins only to encounter its ancient, invincible protector, which cuts each perceived threat down one by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T10:22:12-07:00","id":119117,"title":"","content":"<i>Once, I was a good man, with a good family. I protected the innocent and upheld the law. But like so many in Creation, I was destroyed by the corrupt, the evil, the selfish. And so the Neverborn came to me with a suit of armor. They offered me so much, for so little. My name, for my service and life. So I took the deal, and was placed in armor of soulsteel to walk the earth again. I found those who tried to end me, and I ended them in turn. But I was serving masters as evil as those I once fought. I shall regain my humanity, and evil shall learn to fear the sounds of my boots.</i><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I haven't seen [redacted], just heard a lot about it, so I might have a few details wrong...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T11:14:51-07:00","id":119158,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Spawn","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T13:29:12-07:00","id":119268,"title":"","content":"Nah, the armor makes it <i>Robocop</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T14:52:26-07:00","id":119354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=119268#post119268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, the armor makes it <i>Robocop</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> (Originally it was in 3rd person and actually mentioned which Deathlord exalted him, but then i got a server error or something and lost the post.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T21:35:55-07:00","id":119560,"title":"","content":"A Night Caste Solar has seemingly passed from the world for years, and there are some in the place he once protected who wonder if he was ever a reality. With his passing, the horrors he confronted seem to have left the land he once guarded relatively safe, and few would seek a return to those old battles.<br /> <br /> But evil doesn't have to be made of demonic armies and Abyssal souls to ruin a region. Mortal criminals arise over time, pervading society, becoming more than the local magistrates can handle.<br /> <br /> When the hour grows darkest, rumors arise of a strange aura, a subtle but terrifying anima, being seen near the sites where the mortals are found beaten. And similar rumors about a Lunar anima, once a legendary companion to the Night Caste, begin to circulate. Some believe that their saviors have returned.<br /> <br /> But other doomspeaking prophets cry against this, as the stirrings of the monsters the Solar once faced begin anew, and the battle threatens to throw the whole nation into chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T23:20:34-07:00","id":119588,"title":"","content":"That's pretty archetypical, no? Could you throw in a couple more specific hints, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T03:00:39-07:00","id":120261,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=119560#post119560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Night Caste Solar has seemingly passed from the world for years, and there are some in the place he once protected who wonder if he was ever a reality. With his passing, the horrors he confronted seem to have left the land he once guarded relatively safe, and few would seek a return to those old battles.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Zorro? Or Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T10:49:34-07:00","id":120406,"title":"","content":"Batman Beyond?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:23:45-07:00","id":120418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=120406#post120406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman Beyond?</div> </div> </div> </div>That mostly fits, but BB didn't have an analogue for a Lunar Exalt running after the new Batman shows up. Terry McGinnis didn't have a Robin analogue, and none of the past Robins showed up until Return of the Joker... and that Robin was well-retired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:29:01-07:00","id":120420,"title":"","content":"Batman: The Dark Knight Returns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T19:46:39-07:00","id":122876,"title":"","content":"Here's something a little more obscure for ya... moreso than Batman or Robocop, anyway.<br /> <br /> Long ago, there was a city of sorcerors and mystics that defied and then held against the armies of the dragons. They may very well have outlasted their foe, had they not been betrayed from within by a man who had sold his soul to the Yozi. Only a handful of Exalted - mostly new, in fact - survived the attack, and fled to live in hiding. Over the course of centuries, one Secrets Aspect Sidereal manipulated world events, gathered allies from all corners of the globe and even the Underworld itself, and led an assault on the Realm. The world's history would be a lie, but it would build a better world as they moved forward.<br /> <br /> Creation needed stability, but not the Realm's stability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T21:06:35-07:00","id":122920,"title":"","content":"A lonely, introverted mercenary attends a combat school run by a Chosen of Secrets, and eventually becomes embroiled in a plan to prevent an ancient Twilight sorceress from destroying time itself. To eliminate the sorceress, he teams up with a quirky group of Dragon-Blooded students and a civilian rebel who, unfortunately, Exalts as a Solar Twilight. But it's okay, because the mercenary himself Exalts as a (lion-totemed) Lunar and vows to protect her. Fighting ensues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T11:42:56-07:00","id":123315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=122920#post122920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lonely, introverted mercenary attends a combat school run by a Chosen of Secrets, and eventually becomes embroiled in a plan to prevent an ancient Twilight sorceress from destroying time itself. To eliminate the sorceress, he teams up with a quirky group of Dragon-Blooded students and a civilian rebel who, unfortunately, Exalts as a Solar Twilight. But it's okay, because the mercenary himself Exalts as a (lion-totemed) Lunar and vows to protect her. Fighting ensues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Final Fantasy VIII, is it not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:50:29-07:00","id":124905,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=123315#post123315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Final Fantasy VIII, is it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Here's another.<br /> <br /> This is a world on the brink of destruction. Nature has all but withered away; humanity is ruled by scheming tyrants. All Anathema have either been hunted to extinction or fallen to the Great Curse- all but a Circle of five wolf-totemed Lunars. Together, they search for the reincarnation of Gaia, who is prophesied to lead them to a better world.<br /> It's a pity that everyone they meet tries to kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T20:12:01-07:00","id":124934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=124905#post124905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a world on the brink of destruction. Nature has all but withered away; humanity is ruled by scheming tyrants. All Anathema have either been hunted to extinction or fallen to the Great Curse- all but a Circle of five wolf-totemed Lunars. Together, they search for the reincarnation of Gaia, who is prophesied to lead them to a better world.<br /> It's a pity that everyone they meet tries to kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://img.pandawhale.com/post-11756-I-understood-that-reference-gi-SfRH.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Wolf's Rain!!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T20:21:15-07:00","id":124940,"title":"","content":"My turn: A sailor aboard a Realm ship is the only survivor of a Lintha attack. He hangs on against all odds, until another Realm ship, owned by a Great House, comes...and passes him by, leaving him to die, for seemingly no reason. Filled with rage and hatred, and the determination to survive and gain his revenge on the ship, he Exalts as a Tiger-totemed Lunar, and makes his way to an island of Wyld Barbarians, where he is tattooed as a Full Moon. However, his direct attacks on the Great House fail, until he rescues a Night Caste thief. She convinces him to seek revenge against the *captain* of the ship instead of the ship itself, and a female Sidereal Chosen of Secrets helps him to create a new identity of a wealthy eccentric in order to get closer to the truth behind the ship's abandoning him, while evading the skull-faced, Final Veridiance-infected Abyssal investigating him...which unfortunately leads him to fall in love with the blind albino Demon-Blooded daughter of the House patriarch...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T20:53:20-07:00","id":124960,"title":"","content":"So apparently <a href=\"http://www.remembercomic.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\">Remember</a> was TOO obscure... =( It's too bad, it's a pretty good webcomic... albeit with some wonky early artwork.<br /> <br /> Here's an easy one:<br /> <br /> The alchemical Extreme Prejudice discovered a prophecy that would lead to Autocthon's destruction at the hands of a young solar. To prevent this, Extreme Prejudice fashioned himself into a merciless killing machine and traveled to Creation to murder the young Solar. Unfortunately, said Solar had not been born yet, so instead it went after the Solar's mother. It failed, and inadvertently drove the woman to conceive the solar in question.<br /> <br /> Nice job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T21:05:17-07:00","id":124972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=124960#post124960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently <a href=\"http://www.remembercomic.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\">Remember</a> was TOO obscure... =( It's too bad, it's a pretty good webcomic... albeit with some wonky early artwork.<br /> <br /> Here's an easy one:<br /> <br /> The alchemical Extreme Prejudice discovered a prophecy that would lead to Autocthon's destruction at the hands of a young solar. To prevent this, Extreme Prejudice fashioned himself into a merciless killing machine and traveled to Creation to murder the young Solar. Unfortunately, said Solar had not been born yet, so instead it went after the Solar's mother. It failed, and inadvertently drove the woman to conceive the solar in question.<br /> <br /> Nice job.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it left behind a good number of Resources 5 purchases, too. Princess Wolf Lover is set for life!<br /> <br /> (The Terminator)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:07:50-07:00","id":125849,"title":"","content":"After an incident involving a circle of Exalts of all types, as well as the growing threat of newly minted Exigents (as well as new artifacts brought by a Fair Folk invasion), the All-Seeing Eye creates a special detachment of trained mortals. Led by a man thought to have been killed by the invading Lunar Akuma, and including two highly trained marital artists and two techno-thaumaturges, the team sets out to observe Exigent and Artifact-based activity, bringing along a girl they find on their first case who proves to have a great deal of insight into the emerging threats. Among those threats are an apparent rogue Sidereal, who appears to use his prophetic powers to manipulate events, and his Alchemical enforcers, men whose charms are subtle enough to allow them to hide (save for one man who he blackmails into working for him). Among the threats they don't foresee are the intrigues within the Realm, the All-Seeing Eye, and their own team...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:11:07-07:00","id":125852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=125849#post125849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After an incident involving a circle of Exalts of all types, as well as the growing threat of newly minted Exigents (as well as new artifacts brought by a Fair Folk invasion), the All-Seeing Eye creates a special detachment of trained mortals. Led by a man thought to have been killed by the invading Lunar Akuma, and including two highly trained marital artists and two techno-thaumaturges, the team sets out to observe Exigent and Artifact-based activity, bringing along a girl they find on their first case who proves to have a great deal of insight into the emerging threats. Among those threats are an apparent rogue Sidereal, who appears to use his prophetic powers to manipulate events, and his Alchemical enforcers, men whose charms are subtle enough to allow them to hide (save for one man who he blackmails into working for him). Among the threats they don't foresee are the intrigues within the Realm, the All-Seeing Eye, and their own team...</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Agents of SHIELD, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:18:40-07:00","id":125860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=125852#post125852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be Agents of SHIELD, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be! And my earlier one was Dark Knight Returns. Points to both!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:40:19-07:00","id":125886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=124940#post124940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My turn: A sailor aboard a Realm ship is the only survivor of a Lintha attack. He hangs on against all odds, until another Realm ship, owned by a Great House, comes...and passes him by, leaving him to die, for seemingly no reason. Filled with rage and hatred, and the determination to survive and gain his revenge on the ship, he Exalts as a Tiger-totemed Lunar, and makes his way to an island of Wyld Barbarians, where he is tattooed as a Full Moon. However, his direct attacks on the Great House fail, until he rescues a Night Caste thief. She convinces him to seek revenge against the *captain* of the ship instead of the ship itself, and a female Sidereal Chosen of Secrets helps him to create a new identity of a wealthy eccentric in order to get closer to the truth behind the ship's abandoning him, while evading the skull-faced, Final Veridiance-infected Abyssal investigating him...which unfortunately leads him to fall in love with the blind albino Demon-Blooded daughter of the House patriarch...</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds so familiar... but I can't seem to place it in my mind...<br /> <br /> However, it does give me another idea to work with in a similar vein...<br /> <br /> A man, stranded on an island for five years, returns to his House and the Satrapy they inhabit after being spotted by a passing ship in the West. Unbeknownst to his friends and family (at least at first), he Exalted as a Night caste on the island, and has returned to help heal the satrapy of the infection of crime that has plagued it, fulfilling a mission from his dying father and a message granted to him by the sun. But in the shadows, another like him lurks, trying to stop him - a Scourge of immense power stalks the city, trying to keep his own plans in line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:44:15-07:00","id":125947,"title":"","content":"A rich, spoiled Patrician arrives in a particularly troublesome satrapy in the South. Soon after, the Satrap and his men have to contend with a new menace, a masked Night Caste Anathema sabotaging the workings of the Satrapy and helping the locals. Despite the Satrap's fury, the fat garrison commander tasked with catching the Anathema is helpless against this master swordsman riding a magnificent black steed.<br /> <br /> That's, like, total easy mode. Still, would love to play it one day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:57:07-07:00","id":125960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=125947#post125947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A rich, spoiled Patrician arrives in a particularly troublesome satrapy in the South. Soon after, the Satrap and his men have to contend with a new menace, a masked Night Caste Anathema sabotaging the workings of the Satrapy and helping the locals. Despite the Satrap's fury, the fat garrison commander tasked with catching the Anathema is helpless against this master swordsman riding a magnificent black steed.<br /> <br /> That's, like, total easy mode. Still, would love to play it one day.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first thought was &quot;Batman,&quot; but the sword part didn't fit. Then I realized it was his ancestor, Zorro.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:57:49-07:00","id":125961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=125886#post125886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds so familiar... but I can't seem to place it in my mind...<br /> <br /> However, it does give me another idea to work with in a similar vein...<br /> <br /> A man, stranded on an island for five years, returns to his House and the Satrapy they inhabit after being spotted by a passing ship in the West. Unbeknownst to his friends and family (at least at first), he Exalted as a Night caste on the island, and has returned to help heal the satrapy of the infection of crime that has plagued it, fulfilling a mission from his dying father and a message granted to him by the sun. But in the shadows, another like him lurks, trying to stop him - a Scourge of immense power stalks the city, trying to keep his own plans in line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=125947#post125947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A rich, spoiled Patrician arrives in a particularly troublesome satrapy in the South. Soon after, the Satrap and his men have to contend with a new menace, a masked Night Caste Anathema sabotaging the workings of the Satrapy and helping the locals. Despite the Satrap's fury, the fat garrison commander tasked with catching the Anathema is helpless against this master swordsman riding a magnificent black steed.<br /> <br /> That's, like, total easy mode. Still, would love to play it one day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zorro.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T08:17:38-07:00","id":127481,"title":"","content":"A decade or two into the future, the Bull's war with the Realm overtook the entire North, then ground to a stalemate, both sides stretched too thin to seize victory but too invested to give up. A cunning Realm general bets everything on a plan to trap Yurgen Kaneko and succeeds, but the promptly scheduled execution of the dangerous Anathema gets interrupted by the appearance of a nigh-omnipotent destructive behemoth, progenitor-god of an entire race so powerful, even the combined might of the Exalted Host couldn't slay them, only force them into dormancy. Their sudden reemergence would surely spell ruin for the weakened world of the Age of Sorrows, but not all hope is lost, as a person seemingly randomly caught up in the war suddenly Exalts as a chosen of a forgotten god, the sole being capable of permanently slaying the destructive behemoths. Both sides of the war vie for the support of this new hero, but can he bring peace to the North while saving the world from fiery doom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T08:28:50-07:00","id":127486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=127481#post127481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A decade or two into the future, the Bull's war with the Realm overtook the entire North, then ground to a stalemate, both sides stretched too thin to seize victory but too invested to give up. A cunning Realm general bets everything on a plan to trap Yurgen Kaneko and succeeds, but the promptly scheduled execution of the dangerous Anathema gets interrupted by the appearance of a nigh-omnipotent destructive behemoth, progenitor-god of an entire race so powerful, even the combined might of the Exalted Host couldn't slay them, only force them into dormancy. Their sudden reemergence would surely spell ruin for the weakened world of the Age of Sorrows, but not all hope is lost, as a person seemingly randomly caught up in the war suddenly Exalts as a chosen of a forgotten god, the sole being capable of permanently slaying the destructive behemoths. Both sides of the war vie for the support of this new hero, but can he bring peace to the North while saving the world from fiery doom?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'mma say Skyrim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T09:56:55-07:00","id":127557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=127486#post127486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'mma say Skyrim.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be right!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T12:15:40-07:00","id":127646,"title":"","content":"How did I not know this thread was here? I mean, really?<br /> <br /> <u>The Sunlight-Moonlight Waltz</u><br /> <br /> When enemies assault Creation from beyond the world a group of disparate Chosen is trained to wiled the only three artifacts left. Trained by a Sidereal through means such as cosplay, caligraphy and dreams each champion learns to draw a singular power from the panopaly and together they overcome all obstacles. The invaders are revealed to be led by a Lunar driven to mate with his lover's reincarnation, but the ending is not as it seems. <br /> <br /> <u>A Hopefull Heartbeat Stutters</u><br /> <br /> Savagely disturbed by her experiences in the underworld the Green Lady turns Solar Exaltations from their intended course and guides them to ingenue, unprepared for the trials heaped upon them. At their darkest moment she visits them once again and helps them slip through to Abyssal-hood, calling it a kindness for all the world. Can any child caught in this doomed spiral achieve a wish for freedom, or must all hope lead to a cursed end?<br /> <br /> <u>Twelve Pretty Girls in Pain</u><br /> <br /> As stars align and the chosen time approaches, twelve girls are forced through fate and circumstance to become Olichike, bound to and possessed by Gods. Given a wide leash at first, they are slowly drawn into tighter and tighter circles, until they hunger for each other's blood and the blood of those most precious to their enemies. A wolf, a sword, a dragon and and a hydra are the last left standing ... but if they destroy one anther, who will be left to birth the golden millennium?<br /> <br /> <u>Pretty Girls Triumphant</u><br /> <br /> At a cost of thousands of talents of jade, countries send one or two girls to the Rose Academy, where they are bound to suits of armour and take on the names of the Hearthstones that power them. Schoolgirl rivalry gives way to political infighting, and then to savage bloody war. When might can only be released by permission it takes an administar to give everyone freedom and set things right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T13:58:35-07:00","id":127705,"title":"","content":"In the Threshold, the younger son of a dragon-blooded royal house flees from the increasingly tyrannical rule of his brother and exalts into the Dawn caste. He travels around the kingdom in secret, aided by a knight and a butler, gathering forces for a revolution by promising to right the wrongs done to different groups and rule justly. When he travels across a sea to the land that was his brother's most recent conquest, he discovers that there are dead things coming from the Underworld to slaughter all the life in both kingdoms, led by a Deathlord called the Undertaker Crawling with Pale Dooms. His brother's tyranny stems from desperately trying to prepare to face the coming forces of darkness. Though the younger son returns from across the sea with a powerful coalition and decisively seizes the crown, he is faced with a dwindling treasury and a looming war. Can he keep his promises to his people <i>and </i>keep them alive? Surely something has to give.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":". 05-07-2014, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T14:19:29-07:00","id":127721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=127705#post127705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Threshold, the younger son of a dragon-blooded royal house flees from the increasingly tyrannical rule of his brother 