p in dealing with supernatural problems from various spirits, fair folk, demons, ghosts and other such troubles, and works with a Zenith Caste wielding a sword given to him by the Unconquered Sun himself, a Dawn Caste guardswoman who distrusts him half the time, a spirit that dwells in a skull, his Abyssal brother in dealing with the problems they cause.<br /> <br /> A mortal Dynast apart of the Scarlet Empire, in exile in an oppressed nation conquered by said Empire when he was a child along with his sister, saves a strange girl who is really a Malefactor Caste and Exalts as an Eclipse Caste with War 5. He then proceeds to try to use an alternate persona as a symbol to rally the peoples of this nation into a fighting force to destroy the Scarlet Empire while dealing with getting through the academy he is enrolled in, but is consistently foiled by a Dawn Caste who fights for the Scarlet Empire, who thinks he can change things from within. Together their fight makes things worse and worse, as the Eclipse's power makes a Zenith Caste princess kill everyone in the oppressed nation on accident, while the Eclipse caste makes more sacrifices to advance themselves politically and militarily to defeat the Realm.<br /> <br /> A Twilight Sorcerer who can summon twelve spirits representing astrological signs, a Dawn Caste Fire Dragon Stylist, another Night Caste using Infinite Glacial Armory Style, and a Dawn Caste who specializes in using artifacts and evocations, all join a guild of Exalts who all take jobs to fight threats across the land and fighting other Exalts who take advantage of others. They have a flying cat companion, and their guildmaster is a high-level Sorcerer capable of casting Adamant Circle Spells. they are joined by a guy who knows Iron Dragon Style, another who knows Water Dragon Style and is in love with the Night Caste, as well as three Lunars, one of which is still getting a hang of their war form, another who occasionally comes out of retirement to unleash theirs and kick ass, and the third who was recently rescued from a foreign lan after being gone for so long, and is close friends with the Fire Dragon Stylist, as well as a child Twilight Caste who knows Air Dragon Style and has her own flying cat companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T23:06:11-08:00","id":792955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=792950#post792950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Twilight Caste Sorcerer who made a deal with a Fair Folk to defend himself from his evil mentor, and as a result got judged by a secret organization of Sidereals, some who wanted to kill him for the danger he posed, but some defended him and he was taken under the wing of a Chosen of Endings who taught him responsibility and discipline, but was of course put under a curse that would fall upon him if he prove a threat, and afterwards and constantly watched by a Chosen of Battles to observe and determine if he is evil and needing to executed. He now takes anyone coming for help in dealing with supernatural problems from various spirits, fair folk, demons, ghosts and other such troubles, and works with a Zenith Caste wielding a sword given to him by the Unconquered Sun himself, a Dawn Caste guardswoman who distrusts him half the time, a spirit that dwells in a skull, his Abyssal brother in dealing with the problems they cause..</div> </div> </div> </div>*Reads first sentence*<br /> That sounds like the Dresden Files.<br /> <br /> *Gets to the part about the skull*<br /> <br /> Yup, that's Dresden Files.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T23:08:42-08:00","id":792957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=792950#post792950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mortal Dynast apart of the Scarlet Empire, in exile in an oppressed nation conquered by said Empire when he was a child along with his sister, saves a strange girl who is really a Malefactor Caste and Exalts as an Eclipse Caste with War 5. He then proceeds to try to use an alternate persona as a symbol to rally the peoples of this nation into a fighting force to destroy the Scarlet Empire while dealing with getting through the academy he is enrolled in, but is consistently foiled by a Dawn Caste who fights for the Scarlet Empire, who thinks he can change things from within. Together their fight makes things worse and worse, as the Eclipse's power makes a Zenith Caste princess kill everyone in the oppressed nation on accident, while the Eclipse caste makes more sacrifices to advance themselves politically and militarily to defeat the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>....Code Geas???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T23:10:33-08:00","id":792959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=792950#post792950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Twilight Sorcerer who can summon twelve spirits representing astrological signs, a Dawn Caste Fire Dragon Stylist, another Night Caste using Infinite Glacial Armory Style, and a Dawn Caste who specializes in using artifacts and evocations, all join a guild of Exalts who all take jobs to fight threats across the land and fighting other Exalts who take advantage of others. They have a flying cat companion, and their guildmaster is a high-level Sorcerer capable of casting Adamant Circle Spells. they are joined by a guy who knows Iron Dragon Style, another who knows Water Dragon Style and is in love with the Night Caste, as well as three Lunars, one of which is still getting a hang of their war form, another who occasionally comes out of retirement to unleash theirs and kick ass, and the third who was recently rescued from a foreign lan after being gone for so long, and is close friends with the Fire Dragon Stylist, as well as a child Twilight Caste who knows Air Dragon Style and has her own flying cat companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that familiar with the anime, but I'm pretty sure that's Fairy Tail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T10:23:41-08:00","id":807127,"title":"","content":"I got another one:<br /> <br /> Near a small city in the East, two children get lost in a Bordermarch on the eve of Calibration. Determined to find their way home again, the two brothers explore the forest with the help of a talking songbird who claims to be a woman cursed by a powerful Fair Folk. Along the way, the brothers find many a strange encounter in their journey, including a Shadowland village (secretly) ruled by a Lunar, a Dynast scholar trying to educate a tribe of beastmen and a half-mad Guild merchant wandering the labyrinthine corridors of his palace seeking a woman who may not exist. However, the greatest threat of this forest is constantly following them: A Deathlord who wishes to use their souls to fuel his own immortality and his Renegade Abyssal who is trying to sate his master while protect the children at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T09:46:29-08:00","id":810665,"title":"","content":"A human Zenith Caste enters a tournament for the throne of a kingdom in an empire of beastmen and non-humans, professing to seek the destruction of all humans. The non-human Chosen of Fire overseeing the tournament is immediately suspicious, knowing humans are their enemy, and tries to sabotage him to no avail.<br /> <br /> But she does not even begin to suspect the terrible secrets behind the Zenith's smiling face, and his connection to the mysterious threat that now endangers her people.<br /> <br /> Will the Zenith prove to be the world's salvation or its destruction?<br /> <br /> And will the Fire-Chosen prove the Zenith's saviour or his killer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T05:22:24-07:00","id":866764,"title":"","content":"Everyone who is anyone in the fashion world recognizes the Sion name. Almost as renowned are the city's newfound protectors- a pair of masked, prenaturally agile teenagers whose task is to subdue and purify the minions of their Abyssal nemesis.<br /> In truth, these youngsters are a bonded Solar and Lunar...not that they know that. Or that their comrade-in-arms is also their classmate at the Sion Arts Academy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:14:29-07:00","id":866979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=866764#post866764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone who is anyone in the fashion world recognizes the Sion name. Almost as renowned are the city's newfound protectors- a pair of masked, prenaturally agile teenagers whose task is to subdue and purify the minions of their Abyssal nemesis.<br /> In truth, these youngsters are a bonded Solar and Lunar...not that they know that. Or that their comrade-in-arms is also their classmate at the Sion Arts Academy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Miraculous Lady Bug and Chat Noir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:32:51-07:00","id":867583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=866979#post866979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like Miraculous Lady Bug and Chat Noir.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. (char limit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T02:49:21-08:00","id":1009699,"title":"","content":"<i>Final Fantasy XV</i> is very Exalted, as expected, but what surprised me was the more Dragon-Blooded feel it has compared to other franchise entries. Lots of kinship and noblesse oblige.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:01:02-08:00","id":1010221,"title":"","content":"Nexus's been through some rough years, to say the least.<br /> <br /> First the influx of refugees following the fall of Thorns, then a demon invasion*, then some Twilight Akuma'd gone and blown up the Immaculate temple. It's no wonder the Dawn Sargeant completely snapped, and started calling anyone who disobeyed her &quot;Anathema&quot;. 'Course, she herself wound up corrupted by her daiklave, and... well, it's a good thing a certain Solar was there - even if no one knows where the hell they disappeared to afterwards.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*actually just beastmen the locals provoked, but who could tell.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12013-artex","name":"artex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12013_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T22:22:32-08:00","id":1010520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=1010221#post1010221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nexus's been through some rough years, to say the least.<br /> <br /> First the influx of refugees following the fall of Thorns, then a demon invasion*, then some Twilight Akuma'd gone and blown up the Immaculate temple. It's no wonder the Dawn Sargeant completely snapped, and started calling anyone who disobeyed her &quot;Anathema&quot;. 'Course, she herself wound up corrupted by her daiklave, and... well, it's a good thing a certain Solar was there - even if no one knows where the hell they disappeared to afterwards.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*actually just beastmen the locals provoked, but who could tell.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I see your <i>Dragon Age 2 </i>and raise you:<br /> <br /> The Second Age has rolled into a Third that looks a lot like the First-except there's only one Solar ruler, and they (they keep all but their name and title secret out of fear of Sidereals) have in the course of a few centuries have shackled all remaining Exalted as lieutenants in their empire. Only the Scavenger Lands hold on before the onslaught, and their fall is inevitable under the dual-pronged assault of the emperor's two greatest generals, a mighty Full Moon who absorbs the pain his beastfolk soldiers suffer and renders his army invulnerable and a crazed but brilliant Getimian sorcerer whose hodge-podge of various militias pointed in the right direction echoes his own ability to add the souls of foes to his own body. What really pushes them over the edge is a student of the generals' own superior (a wise but ruthless Chosen of Serenity who views an orderly and fair society as the greatest joy), and their capacity to serve as a medium for the emperor's law-spells, which by all rights should have killed them the first time they issued them; crushing organized resistance was easy with their help, and now the only real delay is the two generals' dislike for each other stopping them from crushing what remains of the resistance. And so the student comes bearing another spell-law, with a cold and crafty Day and an iron-plated Dusk at their side...but will the student become the master? After all, they seem to have realized that even mystical legalities have loopholes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:22:13-08:00","id":1038912,"title":"","content":"She <i>was</i> gentle, once. She was young and beautiful, the best friend of her town's most glamorous socialite- and if her own family was a mere step above poverty, no-one cared. No-one important, anyway.<br /> But that was before the murder.<br /> It was in the depths of her sorrow that she accepted it- wielded the pain like a tool, and allowed it to forge her into something <i>more</i>.<br /> Now, the Changing Moon stalks through dilapidated streets. For a price, she'll hunt down almost anything- cheaters, blackmail, deadbeat parents- but her true prey is no secret. Someone in this town murdered her best friend.<br /> She'll find them if it kills her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 01-27-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:17:46-08:00","id":1039073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=1038912#post1038912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She <i>was</i> gentle, once. She was young and beautiful, the best friend of her town's most glamorous socialite- and if her own family was a mere step above poverty, no-one cared. No-one important, anyway.<br /> But that was before the murder.<br /> It was in the depths of her sorrow that she accepted it- wielded the pain like a tool, and allowed it to forge her into something <i>more</i>.<br /> Now, the Changing Moon stalks through dilapidated streets. For a price, she'll hunt down almost anything- cheaters, blackmail, deadbeat parents- but her true prey is no secret. Someone in this town murdered her best friend.<br /> She'll find them if it kills her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this Veronica Mars? I never watched it, but it sounds like what I understand of it quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:00:08-08:00","id":1039221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=1039073#post1039073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this Veronica Mars? I never watched it, but it sounds like what I understand of it quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. (I've been reading the novel adaptation recently, it's excellent.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:34:24-08:00","id":1039671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=807127#post807127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got another one:<br /> <br /> Near a small city in the East, two children get lost in a Bordermarch on the eve of Calibration. Determined to find their way home again, the two brothers explore the forest with the help of a talking songbird who claims to be a woman cursed by a powerful Fair Folk. Along the way, the brothers find many a strange encounter in their journey, including a Shadowland village (secretly) ruled by a Lunar, a Dynast scholar trying to educate a tribe of beastmen and a half-mad Guild merchant wandering the labyrinthine corridors of his palace seeking a woman who may not exist. However, the greatest threat of this forest is constantly following them: A Deathlord who wishes to use their souls to fuel his own immortality and his Renegade Abyssal who is trying to sate his master while protect the children at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Over the Garden Wall! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T07:21:43-08:00","id":1039970,"title":"","content":"This is a pretty obscure story, but:<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> An Island to the West of Thorns is fighting a desperate war against the invading armies of the Mask of Winters, and has unofficially allied with nearby Scavenger Land states to do so. On this island, a young Dawn, Eclipse, Night and Zenith who along with a Twilight formed a Circle in the First Age, and have all recently exalted.<br /> <br /> The Dawn Caste knows he could be useful on the front lines, but his patrician family has other expectations and he feels obliged to go do as they expect. His tutor, an especially zealous Gold Faction Sidereal, considers it inappropriate for a mere Sidereal to question a Solar's judgement on such matters and so is training him in the ways of bureaucracy and in the Immaculate philosophy. He does, however, introduce the Dawn Caste to some of his friends, including a scholar slowly dying of malaria and a spymaster. These two both quickly realize the Dawn Caste is hiding something extraordinary. The scholar initially attempts to discover what exactly the Dawn Caste is hiding, but finds it is more interesting to simply discuss natural history- a passion of both, and something the scholar knows a lot about through extensive study and the Dawn Caste knows a lot about through extensive memories of talking with Lunars and nature spirits about it. The spymaster's investigations eventually lead him to meet the rest of the circle and become a disciple of the Zenith Caste and a valuable ally to the Eclipse Caste and the Night Caste, 'though he struggles to reconcile this service with his oaths to the Empress. The scholar also attempts and eventually succeeds in persuading the Dawn Caste to defy his family's expectations and go to war.<br /> <br /> The teenaged Eclipse Caste, meanwhile, has managed to get permission to travel to Nexus with her parents (a spy and a diplomat), and there has used a false identity (secret even from the other spies) to join a top secret team dedicated to persuading powerful Nexans to lend support to the alliance against the Mask. She performs various acts of espionage for this team- planting documents, gathering information and spreading rumors. But perhaps her main role is to serve as the handler of a soldier who, on their commander's orders, is having sex with several influential businesswomen in return for political favors- a state of affairs neither the soldier nor his handler is happy about, but which both consider necessary. Meanwhile, the Eclipse Caste is also writing a series of whimsical stories Letter-Within-a-Letter Technique. To most, they simply seem to be whimsical fantasy set in an anachronistic long-ago time. But Solars of the Eclipse's circle will recognize obvious allusions to their own lives in the First Age, which further create other obvious allusions back to the present- and from this perspective the stories are a detailed report of what the Eclipse Caste is doing and learning in Nexus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:57:30-08:00","id":1040124,"title":"","content":"South of Nexus lies a valley connected to the city by the Grey River. As the river flows to the southeast, it carries with it the refuse of the city. Over time, this refuse has accumulated in the valley and defiled it, causing it to become a place of decay and corruption, where the forgotten desperately swarmed in hope of a place to live.<br /> <br /> Recently, a pair of the Anathema have arrived in the Valley in the hope of bringing some solace to the valley\u2019s inhabitants with their powers, irredeemable though they be. One is a former Immaculate priestess whose desire to aid others corrupted her with false golden light, which she uses to protect and offer some aid to her followers. The other is her loyal guardian, a hulking brute clad entirely in silver armor who fights with the ferocity of beasts. While both are completely benevolent, they are still demons in the eyes of the Immaculate Order and the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> Now a lone Outcaste, seeking to rise in power, desires to eliminate the two Anathema to acquire glory for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12200-blitzmentalist","name":"BlitzMentalist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:19:16-08:00","id":1042928,"title":"","content":"The exorcists of this world must be tireless, for they are its only line of defense against Malfeas. Every day, more demons tear through the fabric of heaven, seeking human souls to devour. Good men and women breathe their last in a dead realm of rot and fire. And the grand Houses, the ideal of every 'lesser' exorcist? They are corrupted by vanity and petty squabbles.<br /> Yet they have hope- from their children, from their bonds, and from the prophecy.<br /> Fate has decreed that Thirteen Songs, founder of exorcism and strongest of all Zenith Castes, will be reborn. That he will purify Malfeas itself, leading the exorcists into a new and peaceful era.<br /> This is the story of that noble Exalt...'s parents. Betrothed in childhood by a well-meaning but ruthless Chosen of Serenity, the unhappy couple decide to resolve things by destroying Malfeas themselves.<br /> A mighty goal, to be certain, but the young prodigies soon learn that the Sidereal was right about one thing: when they work together, <i>nothing</i> is beyond them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T23:31:07-08:00","id":1045635,"title":"","content":"Some more stories, of varying obscurity:<br /> <br /> While pursuing an agent of a Deathlord, the warrior-savant Beauty became trapped in an underground manse, the doors of which were designed only to open for the Exalted. As she attempted to escape the manse, a blood ape approached her and offered a way out. Not understanding the direness of its terms and desperate to return to her fight against the forces of Oblivion, she accepted, and became a Defiler.<br /> <br /> The Yozis' orders did not allow her to return to her people, however; she was sent to the opposite end of creation, 'though she quickly learned sorcery and proceeded to establish channels of communication with her former comrades, as well as with the rest of her first-age circle, who were still Solars and who she would proceed to trade gossip with. She also- enraged at what she was learning of the Yozis' plans- begun efforts to assassinate as many akuma as possible.<br /> <br /> She proceeded to:<br /> * Team up with a group of heroic mortals trying to assassinate an Akuma warlord, who proceeded to become her closest confidants.<br /> * Develop an ingenious combat strategy based on using massive numbers of demons as cannon fodder.<br /> * Gain an entirely undeserved reputation for bestiality through a series of misunderstandings<br /> * Piss off Malfeas by publicly killing one of his most important Akuma. The other Yozis accepted that she was just trying to steal his manses and Solar Circle grimour, and were OK with that.<br /> * Finally reluctantly accept that, so long as she continued to be assigned horifically evil tasks by the Yozis, her home country was probably better off without her.<br /> * Receive an offer from the Incarnae to lock her in a prison where she wouldn't be able to do any harm, and refuse because out of the conviction that there had to be a way to escape the Yozis' influence.<br /> * Win a duel against a blood-ape through clever tricks while unable to use sorcery.<br /> * Get an Abyssal to swear fealty to her after she accidentally saved his life.<br /> * Begin recreating various wonderous first-age technologies from her own memories and from ancient books uncovered by her old Eclipse circlemate, including an army of automata to send in when demons weren't good enough.<br /> * Kill an entire abyssal circle through clever tricks.<br /> * Defeat a Dawn Caste solar by using lost first-age technology and taking advantage of his unwillingness to kill her mortal allies.<br /> * Get appointed Governor of Denandsor.<br /> * Finally establish contact with her mother via her old Solar Circle.<br /> * Accepting her mother's suggestion that using sending huge numbers of demons to their deaths was wrong and she ought to stop, reluctantly develop new battle strategies which were still ingenious but sacrificed effectiveness for the safety of her troops.<br /> * Rescue a large number of people from being used by the Dowager in a ritual to destroy the world.<br /> * After learning the rescued people's home country refused to take them back for fear that they the Dowager had infected them with some horrific disease, make parts of Denandsor habitable and grant them to the people she'd rescued.<br /> * Make discoveries which would revolutionize the study of essence necrosis, if she didn't refuse to share them with anyone.<br /> * Piss off a group of Third Circle Demon sorcerers by refusing to share what she'd learned about essence necrosis.<br /> * Get banned from Hell by an alliance of Malfeas, angry Third Circles and the Ebon Dragon, who had made a deal with angry Neverborn.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> On the Eastern edge of Creation was a kingdom of sedentary (in the economic/sociological sense, not the biological one) beastfolk ruled by an elder Zenith, who during the Usurpation had slain her Eclipse circlemate in self-defense and fled into the Wyld. A scholar in that kingdom learned from a Siderial that that dead solar would soon be reborn and return for revenge, but her attempts to prepare for this- by retrieving some artifacts from a manse in the Wyld with which the queen might defeat her nemesis- were derailed by her being unexpectedly being personally ordered to organize a festival by the queen.<br /> <br /> When the Eclipse- now a Moonshadow- arrived seeking revenge, the scholar, accompanied by some people she had met in her festival organization, headed into the Wyld to retrieve the artifacts. On the way, all six exalted as Solars- two Twilights, an Eclipse, a Dawn and two Zeniths. By the time they arrived, the Moonshadow had the artifacts- but six Solars were able to capture her and pursuade her to abandon her vengeance and seek redemption.<br /> <br /> This circle of Solars then returned to the village to continue the festival.<br /> <br /> Over the following year the Solars generally got up to a variety of stuff heroic and mundane:<br /> * The new Solars slowly learned to respect and trust each other despite their differences<br /> * A Zenith worked to repair her family's farm, a Twilight became increasingly successful as a fashion designer and strove to perfect her craft<br /> * And intimidated a monster into leaving the kingdom alone<br /> * And dealt with various Fair Folk invasions, including a powerful Raksha who briefly turned the kingdom to Deep Wyld and another who imprisoned and impersonated one of its princesses<br /> * One of the Twilights adjusted to living in a farming village rather than the capital, so as to stay with her Circle<br /> * And attempted unsuccessfully to study thaumaturgy<br /> * Some of the new solars took part in (and, being Solars, won) various sporting competitions<br /> * The Eclipse rescued some children who got lost in the Wyld<br /> * The new Solars together resolved a territorial dispute with a neighboring beastfolk nation<br /> * And annoyed the kingdom's nobility by behaving like uncultured peasants while being national heroes and possibly rightful Princes of the Earth in training<br /> * And got into a 1vs5 contest over who could save the most people<br /> * The Eclipse got a job as a babysitter<br /> * One of the Zeniths got into a dispute with a traveling Twilight inventer who almost put her family out of business<br /> * Save Autochthonia from being invaded by a deathlord<br /> * The Eclipse accidentally created a bunch of imperfect copies of herself using a demesne<br /> * On orders from the queen, one of the Zeniths pursuaded a Raksha they had already driven from the kingdom to abandon the Church of Balor for good and become a friend to the people of Creation<br /> * One of the Twilights ascended to Essence 3 and was officially recognized by the queen as a fellow Prince of the Earth.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> I've also had an idea in my head of a Steven Universe/Exalted fusion where the gems are second and third circle devas and demons, but 1) Steven Universe has already been done, 2) that's probably far from the most straightforward way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T07:57:43-08:00","id":1047211,"title":"","content":"<i>MLP: FIM</i>...and the first one sounds like <i>Dungeon Keeper Ami</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T20:08:39-08:00","id":1047510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=1047211#post1047211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>MLP: FIM</i>...and the first one sounds like <i>Dungeon Keeper Ami</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and yes! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T05:12:53-08:00","id":1054720,"title":"","content":"Another obscure one:<br /> <br /> Thousands of years ago, there lived in Malfeas a Solar who preached a doctrine based on vague inherited memories of Creation, scraps of misunderstood knowledge picked up from the demons among whom he lived, and wishful thinking. He taught that, before the imprisonment of the Yozis corrupted them, greater demons had not ruled cruelly tyranically over lesser ones, but rather all had lived as equals with mutual kindness and respect, and demons must strive to reagain that state of peace even in their imprisonment. His visionary and inspiring doctrines won to his cause numerous first circle demons and fellow human slaves, and also a few rebellious, disillusioned or kind demons of the second circle. But in time, the Solar and all but a few his followers were discovered and slain by Lucien, and the machinations of an Endings Caste spy ensured the Solar's exaltation could be imprisoned along with those killed at the Calibration banquet.<br /> <br /> One demon, however, was spared from death- thought not from punishment- by order of Cecelyne; a second circle demon of extraordinary power, compassion, conviction, courage and self-control was to be forged into a hellstrider fit for the fetich soul of that endless desert, using the Abscisic Template of the Slave.<br /> <br /> What Cecelyne and her souls did not count on, however, was that the demon so transformed was also a master sorcerer of the Sapphire Circle, and had for centuries been carrying out careful study of the limits of sorcerous binding, the ways in which all manner of magical workings could be corrupted from within, and the working of sorcery in less-than-ideal circumstances. Even bound, each fragment of his mind which he recovered sought out and took advantage of the flaws in his binding. Having corrupted his own binding, he set about working sorcery with which to spread this corruption to other hellstriders. Having compromised the bindings of other hellstriders, worked sorcery to enable those hellstriders to communicate in manners undetectable to their wearers. And having set up such channels of communication, he preached the doctrines of the martyred Solar and told of how he would surely someday return.<br /> <br /> When the Jade Prison was broken, that martyr's exaltation, perhaps feeling it had unfinished business, indeed returned to Malfeas, empowering a revolutionary against the law of Cecelyne. He remembered only a little of his past lives, and correctly recognized much of what &quot;knowledge&quot; he did gain from them as delusions. But after his exaltation, he lead armies Lucien could not defeat and recruited allies even among the Third Circle. Before any such triumphs, however, one of his closest friends, a Heranhal, was selected for use in a hellstrider. He was soon contacted by the renegade hellstriders, and told them of his friend, who the Second Circle hellstrider recognized and the reincarnation of the martyr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T04:07:42-07:00","id":1061503,"title":"","content":"(Forgive me if I've already posted this.)<br /> -<br /> Their war was legendary. The Dawn paladin, determined and fearless. The Midnight conqueror, sly and charismatic. Armed with sword and sorcery, these nemesis fought for dominance over their world. They warred for years.<br /> Then...<i>something</i>...went wrong, and they woke up in another age. An age of science and skyscrapers, where Essence is thin.<br /> The young Midnight has only one path left to ULTIMATE GREATNESS: working at MgRonalds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 03-12-2017, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T08:11:41-07:00","id":1061544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=1061503#post1061503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Forgive me if I've already posted this.)<br /> -<br /> Their war was legendary. The Dawn paladin, determined and fearless. The Midnight conqueror, sly and charismatic. Armed with sword and sorcery, these nemesis fought for dominance over their world. They warred for years.<br /> Then...<i>something</i>...went wrong, and they woke up in another age. An age of science and skyscrapers, where Essence is thin.<br /> The young Midnight has only one path left to ULTIMATE GREATNESS: working at <b>MgRonalds</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a very difficult thing to deduce...<br /> <br /> (The Devil Is A Part-timer/Hataraku Maou-sama!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:05:47-07:00","id":1066016,"title":"","content":"I may have done this one on the old site, but here goes anyway.<br /> <br /> The Realm Civil War has ended, and the forces of Malfeas have begun making their first insidious moves towards the Reclamation. Slowly but surely, demons have begun tempting all the denizens of the Blessed Isle, creating Akuma among the Dragon-Blooded nobility of the Realm and Yozi worshiping cults among the commoners. The Wyld Hunt now tracks the Realm's own people, seeking out heretics wherever they might stand, inadvertently sowing chaos throughout the Blessed Isle. In this dark time, a Dusk Caste wanders the Blessed Isle alone, mercilessly slaying any demons or Akuma that cross his path. The Dusk Caste, a former mercenary of the Realm Civil War, seeks the ones spearheading the Reclamation: a Circle of Green Sun Princes whom the Malfeans see as gods. While those who fight alongside him have their own goals in the fight against the Reclamation, the Abyssal only seeks one thing: to slay his former commander and the newest member of the Infernal Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:54:34-07:00","id":1066041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=1066016#post1066016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have done this one on the old site, but here goes anyway.<br /> <br /> The Realm Civil War has ended, and the forces of Malfeas have begun making their first insidious moves towards the Reclamation. Slowly but surely, demons have begun tempting all the denizens of the Blessed Isle, creating Akuma among the Dragon-Blooded nobility of the Realm and Yozi worshiping cults among the commoners. The Wyld Hunt now tracks the Realm's own people, seeking out heretics wherever they might stand, inadvertently sowing chaos throughout the Blessed Isle. In this dark time, a Dusk Caste wanders the Blessed Isle alone, mercilessly slaying any demons or Akuma that cross his path. The Dusk Caste, a former mercenary of the Realm Civil War, seeks the ones spearheading the Reclamation: a Circle of Green Sun Princes whom the Malfeans see as gods. While those who fight alongside him have their own goals in the fight against the Reclamation, the Abyssal only seeks one thing: to slay his former commander and the newest member of the Infernal Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this world, is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law? Is it like the hand of God hovering above? At least it is true that man has no control; even over his own will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T17:07:44-07:00","id":1066050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=1066041#post1066041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this world, is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law? Is it like the hand of God hovering above? At least it is true that man has no control; even over his own will.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/JTqSsh75Yr4?t=213\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;But... this is my will...&quot;</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T19:25:48-07:00","id":1066095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here?p=1066016#post1066016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have done this one on the old site, but here goes anyway.<br /> <br /> The Realm Civil War has ended, and the forces of Malfeas have begun making their first insidious moves towards the Reclamation. Slowly but surely, demons have begun tempting all the denizens of the Blessed Isle, creating Akuma among the Dragon-Blooded nobility of the Realm and Yozi worshiping cults among the commoners. The Wyld Hunt now tracks the Realm's own people, seeking out heretics wherever they might stand, inadvertently sowing chaos throughout the Blessed Isle. In this dark time, a Dusk Caste wanders the Blessed Isle alone, mercilessly slaying any demons or Akuma that cross his path. The Dusk Caste, a former mercenary of the Realm Civil War, seeks the ones spearheading the Reclamation: a Circle of Green Sun Princes whom the Malfeans see as gods. While those who fight alongside him have their own goals in the fight against the Reclamation, the Abyssal only seeks one thing: to slay his former commander and the newest member of the Infernal Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never even seen Berserk, but it's still the first thing I thought of from what I know of it =/<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T04:22:15-07:00","id":1066772,"title":"","content":"So, still no guesses what that one was?<br /> <br /> Anyway, another obscure one:<br /> <br /> In the wake of a terrible catastrophe, twelve teenaged Exalted have fled the devastated Blessed Isle to the far West, Exalted, and proceeded to become involved in various quests. Among these young Exalted is our hero, a shy writer of romance fiction and erotica now unexpectedly Chosen of Serenity but unfamiliar with her role. It comes to pass that this Sidereal confronts a Third Circle Demon who has been terrorizing a section of the Bordermarches, and this is where our story begins.<br /> <br /> The demon tells our hero that the catastrophe goes far beyond what she knows; Fate and its Loom have failed catastrophically, and only the power of the demon tenuously holds back the utter dissolution of Creation. She says (and this demon cannot lie) that she can get the Loom working again- for a price:<br /> <br /> 1) The Sidereal must play matchmaker, getting all her friends into relationships with each other.<br /> 2) The Sidereal must leave herself 'til last- although she loves the Zenith-Caste Solar who has become the leader of their band of adventurers, she must not pursue him until each of their other companions is in a relationship.<br /> 3) The Sidereal must do this without reshaping the destinies of those she is matchmaking.<br /> 4) The Sidereal must tell no-one of this deal until it is fulfilled.<br /> <br /> And so she goes about trying to matchmake her friends. Their leader (her crush) notices and officially puts her in charge of relationship stuff, saying he was sick of people wasting his time with it. A Water-Aspect Dragon-Blooded declares that, before our hero has gotten everyone a lover, he will have gotten everyone a rival. The other Sidereal in the group, an Endings caste, complains about people wasting time with relationships when the fate of creation is at stake; for she has discovered that the Loom of Fate is malfunctioning and that reality is on the brink of dissolution, and though she is searching in the Saigoth gate and in the dreams of Sacheverel she can find no solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T01:02:54-07:00","id":1134392,"title":"","content":"The fanfic <i>Herding Cats</i>, I think. (Hello, fellow troper!)<br /> <br /> -<br /> He failed. The plan was so <i>simple</i>- raze his casino to the ground, collect the insurance money, and retire with his beloved wife. One last brilliant gamble, to cap off a lifetime of them.<br /> He never meant for his friends to be caught in the fire. He never wanted them to die.<br /> But amid the smoking ruins of his home...<i>someone</i>...appears, and offers the man a second chance. Exaltation- immortality- <i>time</i>. Time enough that he could meet his victims' next incarnations, and tell them how very sorry he is.<br /> It's not free, of course. The burning shard demands Essence in exchange for life. Over and over, the man re-enacts bloody rituals, torments the innocent, lures in prey to feed the hellfire of his soul.<br /> He does so gladly. Even pain is a form of remembrance, after all. No one will ever forget his crimes- not even him. Though ages may flow by, his heart remains unchanged- just as hurt and ashamed and foolish as it was on that fatal day.<br /> He <i>will</i> see his friends again. No matter the cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:51:51-07:00","id":1208465,"title":"","content":"Far away, in the Threshold, there is a city. A city, built on a most inhospitable land, abandoned as the last age turned, as no one knew the magic which made it work.<br /> <br /> Until now. Some years ago, The Master of the House, a man of unknown origin (some claim he is the returned builder of the city, others, that he is a god, a demon, a powerful Exalt, or something even weirder. Some, that he is in fact just a clever mortal, using the rumours and tales to make him look more powerful and unassailable), has fixed the unknowable sorcerous machines, and turned the blasted ruins onto a paradise, in the middle of a veritable hellscape. He offered residence in his wonderful city to everybody, and fastly, the city has become a haven for lesser tribes, kept under control due to the living iron statues which enforce The Master\u00b4s will. The city has become known for its liberal policies, and any kind of vice, entertainment, service or pleasure can be found on it.<br /> <br /> But not everything is going well for the New Paradise. The riches of the city, and the promise of so much power, has made the suppossedly loyal liutenants of The Master greedy, and some of them carry considerable forces, as leaders of vassal tribes, or owners of profitable bussinesses. Maybe, there is something still unactive under the city, something that may still stir and awaken, as the agents of The Master dig ever deeper, in search of greater technologies and riches...<br /> <br /> But probably the most immediate danger comes from outside. The prosperity of the city has called the attention of The Killer of Burning Men, a barbarian warlord, unifier of an infinity of tribes, which looks forward to making the city the capital of his new empire. And, to make things more complicated, another polity is interested in the fate of this little valley: the Federation of the Shady Cities, an alliance of oligarchical cities, interested in adding a new piece to their collection, and a place where getting the technology and power they need to stablish their hegemony.<br /> <br /> You are a courier, hired by the Nexus Express to deliver a package to the New Paradise valley. <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">What seemed like a simple delivery job has taken a turn...for the worst.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13031,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","user":"Clophiroth","date":". 04-18-2018, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}